dBatch`, `defineBody`, `getBody`, `compileBody`, `recolor`, `createPuppet`, `createPuppetBatches`, `createBlobShadows`, `blobScale`; types `InstancedBatch`, `InstancedBatchOptions`, `InstancedBatchStats`, `InstanceColor`, `Body`, `BodySpec`, `BodyPart`, `BodyPoint`, `BodyLength`, `PartOptions`, `CompiledBody`, `BodyPiece`, `PieceShape`, `Puppet`, `PuppetMaterials`, `PuppetBatches`, `BlobShadows`.\n\n**The HTML/CSS overlay (WP 6.5)**: world-anchored labels and damage numbers placed from projected coordinates each frame (three.js's CSS2DRenderer pattern), HUD lines and a crosshair over the canvas; ui.state() for tests.\n`createOverlay`, `DAMAGE_NUMBERS`, `uiState`; types `Overlay`, `OverlayOptions`, `HudOptions`, `HudPlace`, `Label`, `LabelOptions`, `DamageOptions`, `WorldPoint`, `Anchor`, `OverlayCamera`, `UiState`, `UiElementState`.\n\n**The widgets (WP 10.6)**: bars, hearts and boxes, the dialog box and the menu as HTML/CSS over the overlay, reading the page's input (its system layer) and asking the page for sound cues; a gamepad's cursor over any panel. A menu sends the picks that change play as input (`send`), so replays hold them.\n`createBar`, `createHearts`, `createBox`, `createPadCursor`, `createDialog`, `createMenu`.\n\n**The store (WP 10.9)**: what a game keeps across sessions (high scores, progress, its settings) in the page's localStorage under the game's prefix, versioned and checked on load; memory in Node and in the isolated modes.\n`createStore`, `memoryBackend`.\n\n**Lights, shadows, atmosphere and sky (WP 7.1)**: light kinds for a level's light spots, a fixed pool of point lights near the focus with a shadow budget by quality tier, and sky presets (background, dome, backdrop, sun, ambient light, fog) that a sky puts on a scene.\n`defineLight`, `defineSky`, `createSky`; types `LightEntry`, `LightSource`, `SkyEntry`, `SkySpec`, `Sky`.\n\n**Materials v2 (WP 7.2)**: the same material data drawn in four styles (lambert, toon, flat, pbr), switched at run time with every style warmed; the toon look (bands and rim) as uniforms; outline shells for meshes and instanced batches.\n`createStyleSet`, `MATERIAL_STYLES`, `TOON_LOOK`, `createOutline`, `OUTLINE_MODES`; types `MaterialStyle`, `StyleSet`, `StyleSetOptions`, `ToonLook`, `ToonUniforms`, `Outline`, `OutlineMode`, `OutlineOptions`, `OutlineShells`.\n\n**Post-processing (WP 7.4, 13.32)**: one chain every frame draws through, every filter a uniform with an amount, scoped by part; looks as data (a material style, a filter chain, the sky, WP 7.8) that combine looks; objects tagged by part.\n`createPost`, `POST_SETTINGS`, `definePostSettings`, `setPart`, `PARTS`, `defineLook`, `FILTER_FIELDS`, `FILTER_NAMES`, `SCOPES`, `PALETTES`, `STYLIZE_KINDS`; types `Post`, `PostOptions`, `Part`, `PostTag`, `LookEntry`, `LookSpec`, `FilterName`, `Scope`, `FilterChain`, `FilterSpec`, `CombineLayer`, `PostShow`.\n\n**Props drawn (WP 4.5)**: every prop part a batch of the instancing service, posed by its body, the flames dancing on the visual streams, the light spots flickering, for the light pool; a part's geometry and where it stands (its matrix in the prop's frame), for a prop's tests.\n`createPropMeshes`, `FLICKER`, `buildPropPart`, `partMatrix`; types `PropMeshes`, `PropMeshesOptions`, `PropMeshPose`, `PropLight`.\n\n**Crowd rendering and pose LOD (WP 5.4)**: thousands of humanoids, blobs and floaters in a few dozen draw calls over the instancing service, each body seen through bands of detail by its distance (the animator's pose level, capes), culled by the view; the blob and floater bodies as data.\n`createCrowd`, `createCrowdLod`, `CROWD_LOD`, `BLOB_BODY`, `blobBody`, `FLOATER_BODY`, `QUADRUPED_BODY`; types `Crowd`, `CrowdDraw`, `CrowdRigDraw`, `CrowdStats`, `RigBody`, `RigPart`, `RigJoints`, `RigShape`, `CrowdLod`, `CrowdLodOptions`, `CrowdLodCounts`, `CrowdBand`, `CrowdBandSpec`, `BlobFeatures`.\n\n**Performance counters (WP 5.5)**: what `__engine.stats()` returns, means in ms and the renderer's counts, never fps.\ntypes `EngineStats`.\n\n**The texture library (v2, WP 7.3)**: a level's whole floor as a texture generator (define it under a game's id), with moss at the walls' feet, a rune circle on each dais and contact shadows along every block's foot.\n`levelFloorTexture`; types `LevelFloorOptions`, `ContactShadowOptions`, `FloorMossOptions`, `FloorRuneOptions`.\n\n**Clips in pages (WP 8.4)**: three.js's AnimationClip and AnimationMixer, for presentation only (a page plays a baked clip on a puppet with clipJSON and AnimationClip.parse); the sim samples the same tracks through the clip layer. The mannequin: the Quaternius figure the library was measured on, as a body and a build.\n`AnimationClip`, `AnimationMixer`, `defineMannequin`, `mannequinBody`, `MANNEQUIN_SLOTS`; types `MannequinData`.\n\n**Effects (WP 6.4)**: particles as data (emitters: shardfall's presets, the 2D engine's kinds, event effects), drawn with telegraphs on the floor, socket trails, bolts and camera shake by a view's effects; never part of the hash.\n`createEffects`, `FX_BUDGET`, `BOLT`, `defineEmitter`, `getEmitter`, `TRAIL_TINTS`, `ScreenShake`, `SHAKE`; types `Effects`, `EffectsOptions`, `FxEventPayload`, `FxStats`, `Emitter`, `EmitterSpec`, `EmitterLayer`, `ParticleFields`, `FxLight`, `BurstOptions`, `ParticleStats`, `TrailSampleLike`.\n\n**The feel kit (WP 13.4)**: courses, scripted runs of a scene and the numbers measured on them (`node x feel`); the runner and its verdicts; the owner's feel panel and copy as profile.\n`defineCourse`, `getCourse`, `listCourses`, `METRICS`, `runCourse`, `createFeelPanel`, `tunedSpec`, `profileText`; types `Course`, `Measure`, `Metric`, `CourseResult`, `CourseSample`, `MeasureResult`, `FeelPanel`, `FeelRow`, `FeelInspector`.\n\n**Camera modes (WP 2.5, WP 3.9, WP 13.8)**: a code to a camera, each mode's factory, and a game's own.\n`readCameraCode`, `createCamera`, `createShoulderCamera`, `SHOULDER`, `createFollowCamera`, `FOLLOW_RIG`, `createFirstCamera`, `createChaseCamera`, `createViewCamera`, `followCamera`, `defineCamera`, `makePose`, `poseForward`, `poseRight`, `poseUp`, `poseTarget`; types `AnyCamera`, `AnyCameraSpec`, `ShoulderInput`, `ShoulderSpec`, `FollowInput`, `FollowSpec`, `FollowCamera`, `FollowSteps`, `CameraKindSpec`, `Camera`, `CameraInput`.\n\n**The rig a view steps (WP 13.8)**: blends on live switches, the view effects, the view settings cam.*.\n`createCameraRig`, `rigOptions`, `CAMERA_SETTINGS`, `blendCameras`, `BLEND_TIME`, `createCameraEffects`, `applyEffects`, `cameraPlayer`, `apexFov`, `EFFECTS`; types `CameraRig`, `RigOptions`, `RigInput`, `CameraPlayer`, `EffectWeights`, `EffectsFrame`.\n<!-- api-map:end -->\n","numLines":94,"startLine":386,"totalLines":479}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VQ3x5YaQe515Q9cinvZ8ZN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9JcNuRB85c8TyLUW4K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SUV4Mjkx6to19CuaLpcwrf","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work/.research/my-3dge/lean/README.md","offset":517,"limit":340},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41986,"cache_read_input_tokens":55766,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41986},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"b0a58a46-84e9-44b7-8f51-d30b6fddb1af","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:47.231Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9Jc91g8Cm2Gm2yBZBk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SUV4Mjkx6to19CuaLpcwrf":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work/.research/my-3dge/lean/README.md","offset":517,"limit":340}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SUV4Mjkx6to19CuaLpcwrf","type":"tool_result","content":"517\t- `crt` (the whole picture): A CRT's glass: phosphor glow, an aperture grille and a flicker (curvature: screen; lines: scanlines). `mask` 0.25 (0–1), `glow` 0.25 (0–1), `flicker` 0.1 (0–1).\n518\t- `vhs` (the whole picture): VHS tape: rows slipping sideways, colour bleeding to the right, snow in a rolling band. `jitter` 0.5 (0–1), `bleed` 0.5 (0–1), `noise` 0.3 (0–1).\n519\t- `speedlines` (the whole picture): Speed lines: comic-book streaks round a clear centre, redrawn 12 times a second. `density` 0.6 (0–1), `clear` 0.35 (0–0.9), `x` 0.5 (0–1), `y` 0.5 (0–1), `color` '#ffffff'.\n520\t- `vignette` (the whole picture): A vignette: the corners toward a colour, round or following the screen, soft or hard. `strength` 0.45 (0–1), `softness` 0.5 (0.05–1), `roundness` 1 (0–1), `color` '#000000'.\n521\t- `grain`: Film grain that changes every frame. `amount` 0.35 (0–1).\n522\t- `chroma`: Colour fringes: red and blue pulled apart toward the screen edges. `amount` 0.5 (0–1).\n523\t- `letterbox` (the whole picture): Letterbox bars that crop the picture to a film aspect ratio. `aspect` 2.39 (1.2–2.8), `color` '#000000'.\n524\t- `screen` (the whole picture): The screen itself: CRT curvature, a vignette, low resolution. `curvature` 0 (0–0.5), `vignette` 0 (0–1), `pixelate` 1 (1–16 px).\n525\t\n526\t**A look's other fields** (`defineLook(id, { description, filters, combine, … })`):\n527\t\n528\t- `style`: The material style everything is drawn in (lambert, toon, flat, pbr); '' keeps the scene's own.\n529\t- `sky`: The sky preset that lights the scene (a 'sky' id: sky:hall, the torch-lit hall); '' keeps the scene's own lights.\n530\t- `skyGradient`: How much of the sky's dome is a clean gradient, horizon haze to zenith, instead of daylight's model.\n531\t- `toon`: The toon style's bands, rim, shade and dither, used when the style is 'toon'.\n532\t- `shells`: Outline shells round the props and bodies (engine/gfx/stageShells.ts), drawn in front of the sky.\n533\t- `resolution`: The resolution mode it is drawn at while gfx.resolution is 'auto' (pixels, balanced or full); '' keeps the engine's pixels.\n534\t- `textures`: How every material's textures are filtered: 'smooth' blends their texels, 'pixel' keeps them crisp; '' keeps each texture's own.\n535\t- `perspective`: The look drawn instead while the camera is a perspective one (its variant: same style, sky, resolution and textures); '' keeps this.\n536\t- `strength`: How much of the whole look shows, 0 to 1: every filter's amount is scaled by it, so 0 draws the scene clean.\n537\t<!-- lean:looks:end -->\n538\t\n539\t## Built-in ids and the level legend\n540\t\n541\t<!-- lean:ids:start -->\n542\t**Built-in ids**, by kind, as a scene names them (`material: 'material:glow'`, `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench',\n543\tat: [x, 0, z], yaw: 0 })`); `__engine.describe('<kind>')` in a running page lists a kind's fields, and\n544\t`define<Kind>` adds your own.\n545\t\n546\t- `sky:` dawn, daylight, dusk, hall, night, noon. Sky presets.\n547\t- `material:` asphalt, barrel, barrelLid, barrelStaves, blobShadow, brick, carpet, checker, cloth, concrete, crate, default, flagstone, flame, glass, glow, iron, paint, planks, puppet, puppetGlow, puppetHalo, shingles, siding, stone, tiles, wallpaper, wood. Materials as data with three.js's classic parameters.\n548\t- `texture:` asphalt, brick, carpet, checker, concrete, crate, dirt, flagstone, glass, grass, metal, moss, planks, plaster, runes, shingles, siding, staves, stone, tiles, wallpaper, water, wood. Seeded, periodic texture generators.\n549\t- `geometry:` box, frustum, limb, pillar, ramp, ring, roundedBox. Shapes props, levels and bodies name by id.\n550\t- `prop:` banner, barrel, bench, brazier, chair, chest, crate, door, garageDoor, lamp, lantern, pane, pillar, sconce, statue, switch, table. Props: things that stand in a level, as data: meshes (geometry and material by id), a body, an optional light spot, where a level places them, and interaction hooks.\n551\t- `light:` torch. What a level's light spot shines with.\n552\t- `emitter:` bits, block, bubbles, confetti, destroyed, dust, embers, explosion, fire, fireflies, fountain, glass, glints, hit, impact, land, magic, rain, shatter, shot, slain, slam, smoke, snow, sparks, splinters, steam. Emitters. Burst by a sim event of the type: block, destroyed, explosion, glass, hit, land, shatter, shot, slain, slam, splinters. Running at a rate (lay them into your own): bubbles, confetti, dust, embers, fire, fireflies, fountain, magic, rain, smoke, snow, sparks, steam.\n553\t- `telegraph:` arc, cone, line, ring. Telegraphs.\n554\t- `sfx:` blip, bodyFall, boom, bump, cancel, charge, climbGrip, coin, confirm, crouchCloth, die, door, doorBreak, doorClose, doorLocked, doorOpen, drawGun, drumCrash, drumHat, drumKick, drumOpenHat, drumSnare, drumTom, dryFire, explode, glassBreak, grab, heal, hit, holsterGun, hurt, impactBody, impactConcrete, impactDirt, impactGlass, impactMetal, impactWood, jump, jump2, key, kick, kickHit, ladderRung, land, landBody, laser, launch, mantle, oneup, pause, pickup, pistolShot, powerup, punch, punchHit, reload, rifleShot, secret, select, shoot, slide, step, stepCarpet, stepConcrete, stepGrass, stepGravel, stepMetal, stepTile, stepWood, stomp, swing, swish, switchClick, text, warp, whoosh, wind, windowSlide, zipAttach, zipRun. A sound effect.\n555\t- `song:` adventure, boss, dungeon, title, victory. A looping tune in tracker notation.\n556\t- `body:` humanoid. Puppet bodies.\n557\t- `build:` adult, bulky, chibi, heroic, skeleton. Body proportions for the humanoid skeleton, in metres before size.\n558\t- `movement:` apex, platformer. How a character moves.\n559\t- `move:` axekick, backslash, bash, breach, cast, claw, cross, elbow, flyingkick, haymaker, hook, jab, kick, knee, overhead, plunge, rising, roundhouse, slash, spin, sweep, throw, thrust, twohand, uppercut. A named strike.\n560\t- `weapon:` gun. Firearms.\n561\t- `thing:` target. Things that can be hit.\n562\t- `actionMap:` firstPerson, platformer, shmup, thirdPerson. Named actions and the physical codes bound to each.\n563\t\n564\t**The level legend**, a character a tile (`compileLevel`; `defineGlyph` adds one):\n565\t\n566\t- `t`: A brazier: an iron bowl on a stone foot, 0.75 m high (a cylinder collider, 0.3125 m in radius), with a torch spot 1 m up.\n567\t- `o`: The dais: an octagonal platform 0.5 m up (a hull frustum), its edge a 1.5 m slope all round.\n568\t- `+`: A doorway in a wall, 2.1 m high: walk through; the wall stands over its head.\n569\t- `<`: A flight of stairs up to the storey above: a ramp (a hull wedge) from this floor to that one, rising toward the one side that floor meets.\n570\t- `.`: Open floor at ground level: walkable.\n571\t- `=`: A gallery: a walkway 1 m up, a block from the ground (a box collider).\n572\t- `@`: Floor with the hero's spawn point (spawn:hero).\n573\t- `|`: A ladder: open floor with a ladder against the neighbouring tile that stands highest (a wall, a tower), up to its top.\n574\t- `_`: Floor under a low ceiling 1.4 m up (a crawlspace): crouch or slide under it.\n575\t- `w`: A low wall (0.75 m): solid at ground level, but a body may jump onto it and stand on its top.\n576\t- `P`: A pillar (3.5 m), 2 × 2 tiles: write it PP over PP.\n577\t- `!`: A railing 1 m high round a landing, a deck or a stairwell: solid at ground level, a box collider.\n578\t- `^`: Stairs: a ramp from the ground up to 1 m (a hull wedge), rising toward the one side that meets a gallery.\n579\t- `~`: Void: no floor on this storey (a stairwell, a double height, the air beside a building).\n580\t- `#`: A full-height wall (3 m): solid, a box collider, nobody walks or stands on it.\n581\t- `:`: A window in a wall: solid to its sill 0.9 m up, open to its head 2.1 m up, the wall over it.\n582\t- `1` to `9`: Floor with the spawn marker n (spawn:n): where a scene places what it numbers n, such as a mover's start.\n583\t<!-- lean:ids:end -->\n584\t\n585\t## The API by area\n586\t\n587\t<!-- lean:api:start -->\n588\tEvery name below is an export of `my3dge` (`import { createEngine, defineScene } from 'my3dge'`). Each has the\n589\tfirst sentence of its doc comment in docs/API.md, and its whole manual where engine/ declares it.\n590\t\n591\t**Scenes**: defined as data with a setup and a step, run by x sim, x replay and createHeadless.\n592\t`defineScene`, `defineDevAction`; types `Scene`, `SceneSpec`, `SceneAction`, `SceneSound`, `DevActionSpec`.\n593\t\n594\t**The world**: entities, components, systems, timers, events.\n595\t`defineComponent`, `PHASES`; types `World`, `SimRng`, `WorldTimers`, `WorldEvents`, `Entity`, `With`, `SpawnSpec`, `ComponentOf`, `Phase`, `SystemFn`.\n596\t\n597\t**Registries and settings**: content as data, one schema for every setting.\n598\t`defineKind`, `def`, `defineSettings`; types `Entry`, `Kind`, `KindSpec`, `Field`, `Schema`, `SimSettings`, `SettingValue`.\n599\t\n600\t**Intents**: what the sim reads from outside each step.\n601\t`held`, `pressed`, `fromCamera`, `INTENT_KEYS`, `createInputBuffer`, `updateInputBuffer`, `released`, `buffered`, `consume`, `consumeAll`, `repeated`, `BUFFER_STEPS`, `REPEAT_DELAY`, `REPEAT_RATE`; types `Intents`, `IntentValue`, `CustomIntentKey`, `InputBuffer`.\n602\t\n603\t**Math**: three.js's math classes and the engine's helpers (MathUtils covers clamp, lerp, damp, smoothstep).\n604\t`Vector3`, `Quaternion`, `Matrix4`, `Euler`, `Box3`, `Sphere`, `Ray`, `Plane`, `Color`, `MathUtils`, `approach`, `angDiff`, `lerpAng`, `approachAng`, `smoothDamp`, `ease`, `swingTwist`.\n605\t\n606\t**Randomness**: seeded streams (the world's are w.rng('<stream>')).\n607\t`Rng`.\n608\t\n609\t**Events**: emitted with w.emit, heard with w.events.on.\n610\ttypes `EventMap`, `Listener`, `TraceRecord`.\n611\t\n612\t**Levels**: a legend of glyphs, level text compiled to plain data (heights, solid grid, colliders, meshes, spawns).\n613\t`compileLevel`, `validateLevel`, `defineGlyph`, `defineLevel`, `getLevel`, `floorHeight`, `topHeight`, `solidAt`, `tileAt`, `LEVEL_FORMAT`; types `CompileOptions`, `LevelSource`, `LevelProblem`, `Glyph`, `GlyphSpec`, `LevelEntry`, `CompiledLevel`, `LevelGlyph`, `BoxCollider`, `ColliderDescriptor`, `GroundDescriptor`, `MeshDescriptor`, `SpawnPoint`, `LightSpot`, `TileRect`, `Point3`.\n614\t\n615\t**Animation (WP 3.4)**: the humanoid skeleton (a root plus 23 joints) and its builds, poses with three.js quaternions, blending under bone masks, additive layers, forward kinematics, SVG contact sheets and the pose checks.\n616\t`JOINTS`, `SOCKETS`, `MASKS`, `createSkeleton`, `boneMask`, `defineBuild`, `getBuild`, `Pose`, `blendPoses`, `makeAdditive`, `addPose`, `hashPose`, `forwardKinematics`, `createWorldPose`, `jointPosition`, `jointRotation`, `jointMatrix`, `jointToWorld`, `socketPosition`, `tipPosition`, `animSheet`, `animCheck`, `twoBone`, `twoBoneRot`, `LIMBS`, `aim`, `AIM_CHAIN`, `footPlant`, `createFootPlantState`, `FOOT_LOCK`, `FOOT_PLANT`, `FootPlant`, `queryGround`, `handTo`; types `JointName`, `SocketName`, `MaskName`, `Skeleton`, `BoneMask`, `Build`, `BuildSpec`, `JointRef`, `BlendOptions`, `WorldPose`, `Sheet`, `SheetFrame`, `SheetOptions`, `SheetView`, `AnimCheckSpec`, `AnimCheckReport`, `AnimProblem`, `RigidPair`, `PointName`, `TwoBoneOptions`, `LimbEnd`, `Limb`, `AimOptions`, `AimLink`, `FootPlantOptions`, `FootPlantState`, `FootLock`, `FootPlantLayerOptions`, `GroundQueries`, `GroundProbe`, `GroundHit`.\n617\t\n618\t**The procedural humanoid (WP 3.6)**: my-3d2dge's gait, idle, lean, arm swing, held poses and stances as effector targets written with B(forward, right, up), solved onto the skeleton; a fixed step and a seeded stream.\n619\t`Humanoid`, `POSES`, `STANCES`, `WEAPONS`, `B`, `turnRight`; types `HumanoidOptions`, `HumanoidInput`, `HumanoidState`, `HumanoidWeights`, `BodyMotion`, `PoseName`, `StanceName`, `Weapon`, `Effectors`, `FRU`, `LimbSide`, `Sided`.\n620\t\n621\t**The character animator (WP 3.7)**: a body driven through an explicit layer stack (weights, base, override, solve, then layers in clips, additive, post, physics and secondary), told its body states each step (unknown words warn with the closest), with footsteps, sockets, a trail and detail levels; step runs in the sim, pose in the view.\n622\t`Animator`, `BODY_STATES`, `checkBodyStates`, `TRAILS`, `SAMPLE_STATES`, `SLOTS`, `LAYER_SLOTS`, `LOD`, `easeWeight`, `HUMANOID_WEIGHTS`; types `AnimatorOptions`, `PoseOptions`, `AnimatorReport`, `AnimEvent`, `TrailSample`, `BodyStateName`, `AnimatorInput`, `TrailName`, `SampleState`, `SlotName`, `LayerSlot`, `AnimLayer`, `WeightRates`, `WeightInfo`.\n623\t\n624\t**Blob and floater rigs (WP 5.3)**: my-3d2dge's squash-and-stretch blob on a minimal skeleton (a volume-preserving squash spring, a smoothed look, wings, its moves as data: bite, leap, pounce, spit) and a floater that hovers over the floor, banks into turns and carries orbiting motes; step runs in the sim, pose in the view.\n625\t`Blob`, `BLOB`, `BLOB_JOINTS`, `BLOB_LEAP`, `BLOB_MOVES`, `blobMove`, `blobMoveTimes`, `Floater`, `FLOATER`; types `BlobOptions`, `BlobInput`, `BlobState`, `BlobJoint`, `BlobPose`, `BlobLeap`, `BlobMove`, `BlobMoveName`, `BlobMoveFrame`, `FloaterOptions`, `FloaterInput`, `FloaterState`, `FloaterPose`.\n626\t\n627\t**The animation library (WP 8.4)**: readable key-pose clips (format 1 and 2: parse, print, check, the normalized lens, mirroring, the decode to 36 body points), loaded per set; baked to 30 fps rotation tracks on the skeleton, retargeted onto any build (rotation copy aligned at rest, the hip-height ratio, contact IK) or given to three.js as AnimationClip JSON; played by the clip layer in the animator's clip slot, loops at the ground speed, with shardfall's walk-run switch and strike time.\n628\t`parseClip`, `parseClipSet`, `validateClip`, `poseError`, `poseMeanError`, `clipText`, `normalizedLens`, `mirrorClip`, `decodePose`, `samplePose`, `POSE_POINTS`, `POINT_INDEX`, `bakeClip`, `sampleBaked`, `travelAt`, `BAKE_FPS`, `retargetPose`, `clipJSON`, `hipRatio`, `standingHipHeight`, `restSkeleton`, `restPoints`, `restBuild`, `RETARGET`, `loadClipLibrary`, `clipPace`, `walkRate`, `runOverWalk`, `strikeTime`, `GROUND_SPEED`, `STRIKE`, `ClipLayer`, `CLIP_LAYER`; types `ClipSet`, `ClipSource`, `RestBody`, `ClipWarning`, `Clip`, `ClipKey`, `KeyPose`, `LimbPose`, `ClipEvent`, `ClipContact`, `BakedClip`, `RetargetOptions`, `AnimationClipJSON`, `ClipLibrary`, `ClipOrigin`, `ClipLayerOptions`, `ClipPlay`, `ClipSlot`, `ClipLayerState`, `ClipLayerEvent`, `ClipStepInput`.\n629\t\n630\t**Moves (WP 6.1)**: moves as data in metres (the kind move: my-3d2dge's 24, converted by Appendix C's table), timelines whose events carry leftover time, attacks and combos with hit windows, sweeps and root motion, moves played on a humanoid through its body state (the arm path), moves at a moment for previews, measured hit shapes, the cone helpers and a hit's knockback velocity.\n631\t`defineMove`, `getMove`, `resolveMove`, `MOVE_PHASES`, `LEGACY_FIELDS`, `fromLegacy`, `Timeline`, `Attack`, `Combo`, `moveAt`, `measureMove`, `strikePart`, `strikeSegment`, `inArc`, `inHitShape`, `knockbackVelocity`; types `Move`, `MoveSpec`, `MoveInput`, `MovePhase`, `LegacyMove`, `TimelinePhase`, `TimelineMark`, `TimelineEvent`, `TimelineState`, `AttackState`, `ComboState`, `Sweep`, `HitShape`, `StrikeBody`, `StrikeAnimator`, `ArmState`.\n632\t\n633\t**Reactions and secondary motion (WP 6.2)**: a directional flinch, knockdown, death and the get-up chosen by how the body lies (face up or face down), stepped in the sim; verlet chains (hair, tails) with bone-capsule colliders, a floor probe and a rest shape, a cape of two chains, and the squash spring as a volume-preserving root scale, drawn by an animator layer in the view.\n634\t`Reactions`, `RE