version\"' tools/deps.json | head -5; echo \"--- x help\"; sed -n 1,20p x.js; echo '---- engine dirs'; ls engine engine/*|head -100","description":"Search the engine API for vehicles and fire, and list the tool commands"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01J3vF9upcbuRzwA8UYsYpoe":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work/.research/my-3dge"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J3vF9upcbuRzwA8UYsYpoe","type":"tool_result","content":"--- vehicle/car/drive mentions in engine public docs\n200:- `CameraInputSample` (interface from [`engine/input/input.ts`](../engine/input/input.ts)): What the camera takes each frame: mouse look `[right, up]` rad, the right stick `[right, up]`, wheel notches.\n5493:- `postHue` (const): `c`'s hue on the colour wheel, in degrees: 0 red, 60 yellow, 120 green, 180 cyan, 240 blue, 300 magenta.\n5494:- `postSelective` (const): `c` with every hue but `hue` (degrees on the colour wheel, ± `range`) turned grey, and every near-grey.\n6192:- `CameraInputSample` (interface from [`engine/input/input.ts`](../engine/input/input.ts)): What the camera takes each frame: mouse look `[right, up]` rad, the right stick `[right, up]`, wheel notches.\n6263:- `WHEEL_CODES` (const): The wheel's codes: a notch is a tap, never held.\n6329:- `CameraInputSample` (interface): What the camera takes each frame: mouse look `[right, up]` rad, the right stick `[right, up]`, wheel notches.\n8763:- `BARE` (const): What a bare room's contents soak up (a share of its floor's area): a basement's boxes, a garage's car.\n--- fire\n467:- `FLICKER` (const from [`engine/gfx/props.ts`](../engine/gfx/props.ts)): A flame's flicker at time `t` (s): about 0.77 to 1.03, the 2D hall's (my-3d2dge's `FLICKER`).\n868:- `PropDefinition` (type from [`engine/world/props/prop.ts`](../engine/world/props/prop.ts)): What `defineProp` takes: any field, and of its objects (body, light, place, each part and its flame) any key.\n1853:- `PropDefinition` (type from [`engine/world/props/prop.ts`](../engine/world/props/prop.ts)): What `defineProp` takes: any field, and of its objects (body, light, place, each part and its flame) any key.\n5514:- `PROP_MATERIALS` (const): The props' materials, by id: `material:crate` (texture:crate, my-3d2dge's `crateTex`, a 0.75 m face per tile), `material:barrelStaves` (texture:staves wrapped exactly once round the twelve-sided barrel, a stave per side), `material:barrelLid`, `material:flame` (unlit white, so tints show), the library's (WP 10.3) `material:iron` and `material:cloth`, and the fittings' (WP 13.16) `material:paint`; their pane is the built-in `material:glass`.\n5521:- `FLICKER` (const): A flame's flicker at time `t` (s): about 0.77 to 1.03, the 2D hall's (my-3d2dge's `FLICKER`).\n5528:- `tongueMatrices` (function): Tongue `k`'s outer flame and core in its part's frame at `t` (s): the 2D hall's dance, in metres.\n7847:- `PropDefinition` (type): What `defineProp` takes: any field, and of its objects (body, light, place, each part and its flame) any key.\n8249:- `default` (default): The hall with its props, Box 3 (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 4.6): the hall with a hero (labs/box/scenes/hall.ts) and its props, standing in the scene through `spawnProp` (their bodies in the physics world, the page drawing them through the instanced prop meshes): the level's own, a brazier's fire on each of its 30 stands (`levelProps`), and `box.hallProps.count` crates and barrels, 10 to 300, on the first of `HALL_SPOTS`.\n--- html bundler\nanim.test.ts\nanim.ts\naudio.test.ts\naudio.ts\ncheck.test.ts\ncheck.ts\nci-workflow.test.ts\nci.test.ts\nci.ts\ndeps.test.ts\ndeps.ts\ndescribe.test.ts\ndescribe.ts\ndocs.test.ts\ndocs.ts\ndump.ts\nengine.test.ts\nengine.ts\nesc.test.ts\nesc.ts\neval.ts\nevals.test.ts\nevals.ts\neye.test.ts\neye.ts\nfeel.test.ts\nfeel.ts\nfilm.test.ts\nfilm.ts\ngallery.test.ts\ngallery.ts\nhelp.ts\nhtml.test.ts\nhtml.ts\ninspect.test.ts\ninspect.ts\nlab.test.ts\nlab.ts\nmcp.test.ts\nmcp.ts\nnew.test.ts\nnew.ts\nperf.test.ts\nperf.ts\nport.test.ts\nport.ts\nqa.test.ts\nqa.ts\nreplay.test.ts\nreplay.ts\nset.test.ts\nset.ts\nsheet.test.ts\nsheet.ts\nshot.test.ts\nshot.ts\nsim.test.ts\nsim.ts\nsrc.ts\n\n2: * @file Writes and checks the one-file playground, `playground.html` (tools/lib/oneFile.ts; ADR-0023 amendment 5): the\n3: * playground as one self-contained HTML page, the file the engine is distributed and tested as.\n6: * - `--check` (the default) builds it and fails while the committed file differs (`HTML_STALE`, fixed by `--write`) or\n7: *   loads anything from outside itself (`HTML_EXTERNAL`). The quick gate runs it (tools/cmd/ci.ts).\n11: * Usage: node x html [--check | --write]. Exit 0 when the file is current (or was written), 1 otherwise, 2 on a\n15: * // node x html --write   → x html: ok: wrote playground.html (6,912,709 bytes)\n16: * // node x html --check   → x html: ok: playground.html current (6,912,709 bytes)\n17: * @see tools/cmd/html.test.ts\n26:export function createHtmlCommand(build: (root: string) => Promise<string> = buildOneFile): Command {\n28:    usage: 'html [--check | --write]',\n33:      const html = await build(root);\n35:      const current = existsSync(path) && readFileSync(path, 'utf8') === html;\n36:      const failures: Finding[] = externalRefs(html).map((ref) => ({\n37:        id: 'HTML_EXTERNAL',\n41:      const bytes = Buffer.byteLength(html);\n44:        if (!current) writeFileSync(path, html);\n54:          id: 'HTML_STALE',\n55:          message: `${ONE_FILE} ${existsSync(path) ? 'differs from a build of its sources' : 'is missing'}: run node x html --write and commit it`, // prettier-ignore\n69:export default createHtmlCommand();\n--- deps\n7:        \"version\": \"0.180.0\",\n11:        \"version\": \"0.182.0\",\n15:        \"version\": \"0.182.0\",\n21:        \"version\": \"0.183.0\",\n29:        \"version\": \"0.19.2\",\n--- x help\n// x.js: `node x <cmd>` (PLAN.md §8.1). Registers tsx so Node runs the TypeScript tools, then hands over to the\n// dispatcher in tools/x.ts, whose file comment documents the commands, the output contract and the exit codes.\nimport { register } from 'tsx/esm/api';\n\nregister();\nconst { dispatch } = await import('./tools/x.ts');\nprocess.exitCode = await dispatch(process.argv.slice(2));\n---- engine dirs\nengine/index.ts\