{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016f7V5qdMPjZehDvwWdNbch","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The intents vocabulary (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.5 item 3, §8.4, WP 1.5; doctrine: Reproducible): everything the sim\n * reads from outside arrives once per step as plain data, recorded by replays. `move` is a world-space direction\n * `[x, z]` (`fromCamera` turns a stick or keys into one, so W walks away from the camera), `cam` the camera heading,\n * `aim` a world-space aim point, `look` a view direction, `b` the buttons held and `p` the buttons pressed this step,\n * and game code adds its own keys, namespaced (`'game:charge'`). Devices (WP 3.3) make intents; the sim only reads them.\n *\n * Invariants: `normalizeIntents` checks every key and value (an unknown key names the closest; numbers are finite;\n * custom values are plain data) and returns a frozen object with keys in a fixed order, buttons sorted and unique, and\n * absent or empty entries left out. `p` is the union of the presses given and the edges of `b` (held now, not held the\n * step before), so a press is never lost and a hold presses once; when one frame runs several steps, the frame loop\n * passes its taps to the first step only (§6.4). `diffIntents` and `applyIntents` are the replay encoding (§8.4): held\n * state repeats until a change-point changes it (`null` clears a key), `p` belongs to its step and is written only for\n * presses the edges of `b` do not explain, so `applyIntents(prev, diffIntents(prev, next))` is `next` again. `-0` is\n * kept (`Object.is`), since replays must give the sim the very bits live play gave it.\n *\n * `cam` is the yaw of the camera's horizontal view direction, forward(ψ) = (sin ψ, 0, cos ψ) (§6.3), not three.js's\n * `camera.rotation.y`, which is ψ − π since a camera looks down its −Z.\n *\n * Edges, buffering and `consume` in sim time (WP 3.3): an `InputBuffer` is what a body remembers of its buttons across\n * steps, plain data in a component field, so the world hashes, captures and restores it. `updateInputBuffer(buffer,\n * intents, w.tick)` runs once per step (a system in the phase `intents`); then `released` says a button went up this\n * step (a tap shorter than a step is pressed and released on the same one), `buffered` that it was pressed within the\n * last `BUFFER_STEPS` steps and not yet used up by `consume` (a jump pressed just before landing still jumps), and\n * `repeated` that a held button repeats, as a menu cursor does. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:564-583`\n * (`released`, `repeat`, `buffered`, `consume`, `consumeAll`), counted in steps instead of seconds.\n *\n * @example\n * const step1 = normalizeIntents({ move: fromCamera(Math.PI / 2, [0, 1]), b: ['jump'] }); // move ≈ [1, 0]: +X\n * pressed(step1, 'jump'); // true: an edge of b\n * const step2 = normalizeIntents({ move: step1.move, b: ['jump'] }, step1);\n * [held(step2, 'jump'), pressed(step2, 'jump')]; // [true, false]\n * diffIntents(step1, normalizeIntents({}, step1)); // { b: null, move: null }\n * const buffer = updateInputBuffer(createInputBuffer(), step1, 1);\n * buffered(buffer, 'jump'); // true for 9 steps, or until consume(buffer, 'jump')\n * @see engine/input/intents.test.ts\n * @see engine/input/buffer.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../core/log';\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const INTENT_CODES = defineCodes('input', {\n  INPUT_BAD_INTENTS: {\n    template: '{where}: {problems}',\n    fix: 'give intents as { move: [x, z], cam, aim: [x, y, z], look: [yaw, pitch], b: [held buttons], p: [pressed buttons] } with finite numbers, plus custom keys namespaced \"game:key\" holding plain data (engine/input/intents.ts); null or a missing key means not given',\n    doc: 'Raised by `normalizeIntents`, `applyIntents` and the replay checks (engine/input/intents.ts, engine/sim/replay.ts) for an unknown key (named with the closest), a non-finite or misshapen number, a button that is not a non-empty string, or a custom value that is not plain data. Every problem is listed at once.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** A custom intent's value: plain data, as a replay file holds it. */\nexport type IntentValue = number | string | boolean | readonly IntentValue[] | { readonly [key: string]: IntentValue };\n\n/** A namespaced key for game code's own intents: `'game:charge'`. */\nexport type CustomIntentKey = `${string}:${string}`;\n\n/** One step's intents, as the sim reads them (systems get them as their second argument). */\nexport type Intents = {\n  /** The direction to move in, world space `[x, z]`, length 1 at most from `fromCamera`. */\n  readonly move?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The camera heading: the yaw of its horizontal view direction, rad (see the file comment). */\n  readonly cam?: number;\n  /** The point aimed at, world space `[x, y, z]`, m. */\n  readonly aim?: readonly [number, number, number];\n  /** The view direction `[yaw, pitch]`, rad (first-person look). */\n  readonly look?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The buttons held this step, sorted. */\n  readonly b?: readonly string[];\n  /** The buttons pressed this step (edges of `b` plus taps released within the step), sorted. */\n  readonly p?: readonly string[];\n} & { readonly [key: CustomIntentKey]: IntentValue | undefined };\n\n/** A replay change-point's intent part: the keys that changed, `null` for a key cleared, `p` for unexplained presses. */\nexport type IntentChanges = { -readonly [K in keyof Intents]?: Intents[K] | null };\n\n/** The built-in keys, in the order a normalized object holds them, each with what it means. */\nexport const INTENT_KEYS = {\n  move: 'the direction to move in, world space [x, z]',\n  cam: 'the camera heading (yaw of its view direction), rad',\n  aim: 'the point aimed at, world space [x, y, z], m',\n  look: 'the view direction [yaw, pitch], rad',\n  b: 'the buttons held, sorted',\n  p: 'the buttons pressed this step, sorted',\n} as const;\n\n/** A built-in key. */\nexport type IntentKey = keyof typeof INTENT_KEYS;\n\n/** No intents: what a step gets when nothing is given. */\nexport const NO_INTENTS: Intents = Object.freeze({});\n\n/** A namespaced key: a lower-case word, a colon, a name. */\nconst CUSTOM = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\n\n/** The namespaced key a bad one most likely means: `'Game:x'` → `'game:x'`, `'charge'` → `'game:charge'`. */\nfunction customKey(key: string): string {\n  const at = key.indexOf(':');\n  const space = (at < 0 ? '' : key.slice(0, at)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9]/g, '').replace(/^[^A-Za-z]+/, '');\n  const name = (at < 0 ? key : key.slice(at + 1)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]/g, '');\n  return `${space ? space[0].toLowerCase() + space.slice(1) : 'game'}:${name || 'key'}`;\n}\n\n/** How many numbers each vector key holds. */\nconst VECTORS: Partial<Record<IntentKey, number>> = { move: 2, aim: 3, look: 2 };\n/** Code-unit order, so sorting never depends on the locale. */\nconst byText = (a: string, b: string) => (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0);\n/** Deepest nesting a custom value may have. */\nconst MAX_DEPTH = 32;\n\n/** A frozen copy of plain data, or a problem pushed for the first value that is not. */\nfunction plainData(value: unknown, path: string, problems: string[], depth = 0): IntentValue | undefined {\n  if (typeof value === 'number') {\n    if (Number.isFinite(value)) return value;\n    problems.push(`${path} is ${show(value)}; numbers must be finite`);\n  } else if (typeof value === 'string' || typeof value === 'boolean') {\n    return value;\n  } else if (depth >= MAX_DEPTH) {\n    problems.push(`${path} nests deeper than ${MAX_DEPTH} levels`);\n  } else if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    const out = value.map((item, i) => plainData(item, `${path}[${i}]`, problems, depth + 1));\n...\n64:export interface InputOptions {\n65-  /** The action map's id (`actionMap:thirdPerson`) or ready bindings. */\n66-  map?: string | Bindings;\n67-  /** Where bindings made from an id are saved (the page's `localStorage`). */\n68-  storage?: BindingsStorage;\n69-  /** Where keys, releases, blur and gamepad events arrive (`window`). */\n70-  window?: EventTarget;\n71-  /** The document: visibility and pointer lock (`document`). */\n72-  document?: MouseTargets['document'] & { visibilityState?: string };\n73-  /** The game's element, the canvas: mouse presses, wheel and pointer lock (`document.body`). */\n74-  element?: MouseTargets['element'];\n75-  /** Where pads come from (`navigator.getGamepads`). */\n76-  gamepads?: GamepadSource;\n77-  /** The stick deadzone (0.18), clamped to [0.05, 0.5]. */\n78-  deadzone?: number;\n79-  /** A view action pressed (the map's `view`: a camera switch, a view's turn), as it happens (see the file comment). */\n80-  onView?: (action: string) => void;\n81-  /** The look settings now (`lookOptions` over the view settings `input.*`), read every frame; defaults when absent. */\n82-  look?: () => LookOptions;\n83-  /** The keyboard layout for prompts (`readKeyboardLayout()`). */\n84-  layout?: ReadonlyMap<string, string>;\n85-  /** The `touch` setting now (`auto`, `on`, `off`): touch mode follows the screen unless forced. */\n86-  touchMode?: () => TouchSetting;\n87-  /** A tap on a touch tap control (`data-tap`: `menu`) or on the open game (`game`), as it happens. */\n88-  onTap?: (name: string) => void;\n89-  /** Where the map is registered (the shared registry). */\n90-  registry?: Registry;\n91-  /** Where advice goes (the shared log). */\n92-  log?: Log;\n93-}\n94-\n95-/** What the camera takes each frame: mouse look `[right, up]` rad, the right stick `[right, up]`, wheel notches. */\n96-export interface CameraInputSample {\n97-  look: [number, number];\n98-  turn: [number, number];\n99-  zoom: number;\n100-}\n101-\n102-/** A page's input. */\n103:export interface Input {\n104-  /** The bindings of the map in use: rebind, reset, labels. */\n105-  readonly bindings: Bindings;\n106-  /** Switches to the action map `map` (an id, its bindings made and saved as the first's, or bindings); returns them. */\n107-  use(map: string | Bindings): Bindings;\n108-  /** The bindings of the action map `map` (an id), made and saved as the first's, without switching to them. */\n109-  bindingsFor(map: string): Bindings;\n110-  /** The virtual device, merged into every sample (`__engine.input` drives it). */\n111-  readonly virtual: VirtualDevice;\n112-  /** The mouse (pointer lock, pointer), when there is a page. */\n113-  readonly mouse: MouseDevice | undefined;\n114-  /** Fingers (touch mode, the stick, the buttons under them), when there is a page. */\n115-  readonly touch: TouchDevice | undefined;\n116-  /** The device used last: prompts follow it. */\n117-  readonly lastDevice: DeviceKind;\n118-  /**\n119-   * One frame's intents (unnormalized) at the frame's timestamp `now` (ms): see the file comment. Every action also\n120-   * binds `touch:<action>` (WP 3.12), and the touch stick adds to the move axes before `fromCamera` clamps them to\n121-   * length 1. A code a held binding waits on (engine/input/codes.ts `Hold:<code>`, WP 13.20) is held back as it goes\n122-   * down: let go before `HOLD_TIME`, it taps (its plain actions pressed at the next sample, never held); kept down, its\n123-   * held binding's actions press and hold until it goes up, and its plain ones never see it. The time is `now`, or a\n124-   * 60 Hz frame a sample without one; such a code is digital, its analog strength unread.\n125-   */\n126-  sample(camera?: CameraLike, now?: number): Record<string, unknown>;\n127-  /** Whether `action` (either layer) was held at the last sample. */\n128-  held(action: string): boolean;\n129-  /** Whether `action` (either layer) was pressed at the last sample. */\n130-  pressed(action: string): boolean;\n131-  /** How far `action` was pushed at the last sample, 0 to 1. */\n132-  strength(action: string): number;\n133-  /** What the camera takes since the last call (mouse look, right stick, wheel); then zero. */\n134-  camera(): CameraInputSample;\n135-  /** The label of `action`'s binding on the device used last: `Space`, `A`, `LMB`. */\n136-  prompt(action: string): string;\n137-  /** The next code pressed on `device`'s family, swallowed; null when Escape cancels or another listen starts. */\n138-  listen(device: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'): Promise<string | null>;\n139-  /** Lets go of everything held and drops pending presses. */\n140-  clear(): void;\n141-  /** Removes every listener. */\n142-  dispose(): void;\n143-}\n144-\n145-/** The look settings' defaults: what `camera()` scales by without `options.look`. */\n146-const DEFAULT_LOOK = lookOptions(() => undefined);\n147-\n148-/** Makes the page's input. */\n149-export function createInput(options: InputOptions = {}): Input {\n150-  const made = (map: string | Bindings) => (typeof map === 'object' ? map : createBindings(map, options));\n151-  let bindings = made(options.map ?? 'actionMap:thirdPerson');\n152-  const known = new Map<string, Bindings>([[bindings.map.id, bindings]]);\n153-  const scope = globalThis as { window?: EventTarget; document?: InputOptions['document'] & { body?: EventTarget } };\n154-  const win = options.window ?? scope.window;\n155-  const doc = options.document ?? scope.document;\n156-  const element = options.element ?? scope.document?.body;\n157-  const nav = (globalThis as { navigator?: { getGamepads?(): readonly unknown[] } }).navigator;\n158-  const source = options.gamepads ?? (() => (nav?.getGamepads?.() ?? []) as ReturnType<GamepadSource>);\n159-  const down = new Set<string>();\n160-  const taps = new Set<string>();\n161-  const values = new Map<string, number>();\n162-  let last: DeviceKind = 'keyboard';\n163-  let heldNow = new Set<string>();\n164-  let pressedNow = new Set<string>();\n165-  let strengths = new Map<string, number>();\n166-  let listening: { family: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'; resolve: (code: string | null) => void } | null = null;\n167-  let table = { of: bindings, version: -1, codes: new Map<string, readonly string[]>(), bound: new Set<string>(), holds: new Set<string>() }; // prettier-ignore\n168-\n169-  const codesOf = (action: string): readonly string[] => {\n170-    if (table.of !== bindings || table.version !== bindings.version) {\n171-      const codes = new Map<string, readonly string[]>();\n172-      for (const [name, own] of Object.entries(SYSTEM_ACTIONS)) codes.set(name, [...own, touchCode(name)]);\n173-      for (const name of bindings.actions()) codes.set(name, [...bindings.codes(name), touchCode(name)]);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"1b2f0ef8-df07-4d50-a14c-50fab72dddda","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:26:48.551Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The intents vocabulary (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.5 item 3, §8.4, WP 1.5; doctrine: Reproducible): everything the sim\n * reads from outside arrives once per step as plain data, recorded by replays. `move` is a world-space direction\n * `[x, z]` (`fromCamera` turns a stick or keys into one, so W walks away from the camera), `cam` the camera heading,\n * `aim` a world-space aim point, `look` a view direction, `b` the buttons held and `p` the buttons pressed this step,\n * and game code adds its own keys, namespaced (`'game:charge'`). Devices (WP 3.3) make intents; the sim only reads them.\n *\n * Invariants: `normalizeIntents` checks every key and value (an unknown key names the closest; numbers are finite;\n * custom values are plain data) and returns a frozen object with keys in a fixed order, buttons sorted and unique, and\n * absent or empty entries left out. `p` is the union of the presses given and the edges of `b` (held now, not held the\n * step before), so a press is never lost and a hold presses once; when one frame runs several steps, the frame loop\n * passes its taps to the first step only (§6.4). `diffIntents` and `applyIntents` are the replay encoding (§8.4): held\n * state repeats until a change-point changes it (`null` clears a key), `p` belongs to its step and is written only for\n * presses the edges of `b` do not explain, so `applyIntents(prev, diffIntents(prev, next))` is `next` again. `-0` is\n * kept (`Object.is`), since replays must give the sim the very bits live play gave it.\n *\n * `cam` is the yaw of the camera's horizontal view direction, forward(ψ) = (sin ψ, 0, cos ψ) (§6.3), not three.js's\n * `camera.rotation.y`, which is ψ − π since a camera looks down its −Z.\n *\n * Edges, buffering and `consume` in sim time (WP 3.3): an `InputBuffer` is what a body remembers of its buttons across\n * steps, plain data in a component field, so the world hashes, captures and restores it. `updateInputBuffer(buffer,\n * intents, w.tick)` runs once per step (a system in the phase `intents`); then `released` says a button went up this\n * step (a tap shorter than a step is pressed and released on the same one), `buffered` that it was pressed within the\n * last `BUFFER_STEPS` steps and not yet used up by `consume` (a jump pressed just before landing still jumps), and\n * `repeated` that a held button repeats, as a menu cursor does. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:564-583`\n * (`released`, `repeat`, `buffered`, `consume`, `consumeAll`), counted in steps instead of seconds.\n *\n * @example\n * const step1 = normalizeIntents({ move: fromCamera(Math.PI / 2, [0, 1]), b: ['jump'] }); // move ≈ [1, 0]: +X\n * pressed(step1, 'jump'); // true: an edge of b\n * const step2 = normalizeIntents({ move: step1.move, b: ['jump'] }, step1);\n * [held(step2, 'jump'), pressed(step2, 'jump')]; // [true, false]\n * diffIntents(step1, normalizeIntents({}, step1)); // { b: null, move: null }\n * const buffer = updateInputBuffer(createInputBuffer(), step1, 1);\n * buffered(buffer, 'jump'); // true for 9 steps, or until consume(buffer,