a command's file comment: its one-line description in `x help`. */\n185:/** Names the usage problem in a `parseArgs` error, with the closest valid flag when one is close. */\n203:/** Where an unexpected error was thrown, as a file and line relative to this repository, when the stack names one. */\n240:    // The whole output beside the report when it is cut; none left from an earlier run when it is not.\n12: * repository (its plan, records, CI, the one-file playground, test suites, fixtures, the playground, labs/playground/, whose\n78:/** The engine's own: plan, records, CI, the one-file playground, suites, fixtures, evals and mutation runs, playground and lean. */\n80:  /^(PLAN\\.md|AGENTS\\.md|CLAUDE\\.md|GEMINI\\.md|README\\.md|index\\.html|package(-lock)?\\.json|playwright\\.config\\.ts|stryker\\.config\\.json|playground\\.html|\\.gitignore|\\.gitattributes|\\.github\\/|\\.claude\\/|fixtures\\/|tests\\/|docs\\/|scripts\\/|evals\\/|labs\\/hello\\/|labs\\/playground\\/|labs\\/labs\\.json|labs\\/(anim|cameras|fx|index|library|materials|physics|props)\\/|lean\\/)/;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015iU4hJ5ufTDx5RQG5cC6pH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
