{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWcZCC7REfkPiCqU6k1AG2","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The viewmodel's arms rig (PLAN.md WP 13.12, docs/PLAYGROUND.md §4): first person's arms posed against the\n * camera, as games pose a viewmodel. Its skeleton, the player's build, stands upright under the camera, its eyes at the\n * camera's eye and its heading the camera's, so its shoulders sit just under and behind the eye whatever the body does\n * (the body's own, which the camera's profile height leaves 0.1 to 1.4 m away in a slide, a mantle or a skydive, could\n * not reach the picture). Each hand's grip (`weaponL`, `weaponR`) goes to a place in the camera's frame (`ARMS`): fists\n * up at rest, pumping with the gait's phase in a sprint, out for balance in a slide, raised in the air; a little bob on\n * the view effects' weapon bob (engine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts), a breath, and a sway behind the look's turn. A hand the\n * body holds on a contact (a ledge in a mantle, the wall in a climb, a rung, the cable, the floor) goes where the body's\n * is, as far as it holds it, and a carried gun where the body holds it from its eyes (from its right eye as far as its\n * sights are up, so they line up on the picture's centre: the hold's `aimed`, WP 13.20); then every hand is kept on the\n * arms' frame (lens.ts `intoArmsFrame`) and drawn along its ray within the arm's reach (the arms are drawn at their own\n * depth anyway, so only the ray shows). A punch throws its fist where the body's goes from its eyes (WP 13.19), and a\n * kick shows its leg: the body's right leg as it kicks, under the rig's hips. `armsInputOf` reads what the rig needs\n * off the player's animator and its traversal plant.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: it reads the body and the camera and writes its own pose; pure but for its own state\n * (the eased shares, the sway, the last look); the shown parts (`shown`) are the arms (and the kicking leg) bar any\n * part nearer the eye than `VIEWMODEL.cull`.\n *\n * @example\n * import { makePose } from '../cameras/pose';\n * const rig = new ArmsRig('build:adult');\n * const camera = makePose({ position: [0, 1.52, 0], fov: 74, near: 0.05 }); // facing +Z\n * rig.update(camera, { player: null, effects: null, phase: 0, clock: 0, held: [null, null], kick: null, gun: null, aspect: 16 / 9 }, 1 / 60); // prettier-ignore\n * rig.hands[1].z > 0.3; // true: the right fist in front of the eye\n * rig.shown; // ['upperArmL', 'forearmL', 'handL', 'upperArmR', 'forearmR', 'handR']\n * @see engine/gfx/viewmodel/rig.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Animator } from '../../anim/character';\nimport {\n  createWorldPose,\n  forwardKinematics,\n  jointPosition,\n  jointRotation,\n  socketPosition,\n  tipPosition,\n} from '../../anim/fk';\nimport { handTo } from '../../anim/ik';\nimport { Pose } from '../../anim/pose';\nimport { createSkeleton, JOINTS, PARENTS, socketIndex, type JointName, type Skeleton } from '../../anim/skeleton';\nimport type { Build } from '../../anim/builds';\nimport type { HoldPlant } from '../../anim/traversal/hold';\nimport type { TraversalPlant } from '../../anim/traversal/plant';\nimport { angDiff, MathUtils, Quaternion, Vector3 } from '../../core/math';\nimport type { CameraPlayer, EffectsFrame } from '../cameras/effects';\nimport { eyePoint, FIRST_ARMS, FIRST_KICK, nearBodyCull } from '../cameras/first';\nimport { poseForward, poseRight, poseUp, type CameraPose, type Vec3 } from '../cameras/pose';\nimport { intoArmsFrame, VIEWMODEL } from './lens';\n\n/** Places in the camera's frame, `[right, up, forward]`, m for a build of size 1 (the right hand's; the left's mirrored). */ // prettier-ignore\ntype Place = readonly [number, number, number];\n\n/** The rig's numbers (see the file comment): places, metres, seconds. */\nexport const ARMS = Object.freeze({\n  ready: [0.13, -0.13, 0.4] as Place,\n  /** A sprint's fists, and their pump forward and up over the gait's phase. */\n  sprint: [0.17, -0.2, 0.34] as Place,\n  pump: [0.08, 0.08] as const,\n  /** A slide's hands: the right low and back, the left out ahead. */\n  slide: [0.22, -0.24, 0.32] as Place,\n  slideLeft: [-0.25, -0.17, 0.43] as Place,\n  air: [0.16, -0.08, 0.38] as Place,\n  /** The breath's rise (m) and rate (rad/s); the weapon bob's sway across and dip (m) at its full share. */\n  breath: [0.004, 1.6] as const,\n  bob: [0.008, 0.012] as const,\n  /** The sway: m per rad/s of the look's turn, the most, and its lag (s). */\n  sway: [0.012, 0.04, 0.08] as const,\n  /** S: the states ease in and out. */\n  ease: 0.1,\n....\n/**\n * @file ACTIONS (PLAN.md WP 8.7; I-11; docs/ANIMATION-RESEARCH.md §2, §6): multi-beat sequences played on a body,\n * between one move and a behaviour. `Actions` plays the registry kind `action` (actions-data.ts: the beats and their\n * fields, `defineAction`, `loadActions`) one at a time. A beat `until: 'next'` holds its contact frame (a charge, a\n * hang, a fall) until the game calls `next()` or `go(beat)`; `then` loops; `finish()` goes to the `exit` beat; a\n * `pair` plays on a partner in lockstep (`play(id, partner)`). actions-check.ts plays one for the `anim` QA.\n *\n * The two update paths (§6.4), as reactions': `step()` is the sim's tick (beats, clip calls, events) and `body` what\n * the beat tells the humanoid, to lay over the animator's input; plain data (`save`, `load`). The view: `apply` (slot\n * `post`) solves the effectors; `flipLayer` (slot `physics`, every detail level) turns and squashes the body.\n *\n * Invariants:\n * - Exact in ticks, as timeline.ts: time left when a beat ends carries into the next; events fire in order.\n * - Nothing pops: as a beat begins, its channels (`CHANNELS`: motion, effectors, flip, scale) are taken from where\n *   they are and ease (smoothstep) to the beat's over its `seconds`; after an action they ease to rest over\n *   `ACTION.out`. They come from data, never from a pose, so posing never changes the hash.\n * - Effector targets are `[forward, right, up]` metres times the build's size (actions-data.ts says from where).\n * - A flip turns the body `turns` times about a pivot `ACTION.pivot` hip heights up (a `ground` one, a roll, keeps its\n *   lowest point on its ground point; in the air the arc is the game's); a scale keeps the lowest point where it was.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/emberdeep/96-hero-clips.js:31-49` (`HCL_MOVES`, as input: a moment's clip and its\n * speed, fades, mask, walk, hold, landed and next, as a beat's `clip` and the beats after it) and\n * `src/emberdeep/20-hero.js:193-196` (`heroRoll`: the pivot at 0.55 of the hip height, the eased whole turn).\n *\n * @example\n * import { defineAction } from './actions-data';\n * import { Animator } from './character';\n * const bend = { name: 'bend', seconds: 0.4, motion: { lean: 0.6 }, events: [{ type: 'lowest', at: 1 }] };\n * defineAction('action:bow', { desc: 'A bow.', beats: [bend, { name: 'rise', seconds: 0.3, cancel: { by: ['walk'] } }] });\n * const hero = new Animator({ build: 'build:heroic' });\n * const acts = new Actions().attach(hero).play('bow'); // acts.beat: 'bend'\n * for (let i = 0; i < 25; i++) hero.update({ ...acts.step() && acts.body });\n * acts.beat; // 'rise': 0.4 s in, after 'lowest'\n * acts.cancel('walk'); // true: walking may cut the rise\n * @see engine/anim/actions.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../core/log';\nimport { MathUtils, Quaternion, Vector3 } from '../core/math';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { SIM_DT } from '../core/time';\nimport { ACTION, EFFECTORS, FLIP_AXES, getAction, type Action, type Beat } from './actions-data';\nimport { B } from './authoring';\nimport type { Animator } from './character';\nimport { ClipLayer, type ClipPlay } from './clip/layer';\nimport { forwardKinematics, socketPosition, tipPosition, type WorldPose } from './fk';\nimport { aim, handTo, twoBoneRot } from './ik';\nimport { blendPoses, Pose } from './pose';\nimport { boneMask, JOINT_COUNT, SOCKETS, socketIndex, type Skeleton } from './skeleton';\nimport type { AnimatorInput } from './states';\nimport { TICK_EPSILON, type TimelineEvent } from './timeline';\nimport type { AnimLayer } from './weights';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const ACTION_CODES = defineCodes('anim', {\n  ANIM_UNKNOWN_BEAT: {\n    template: 'action {action} has no beat {name}{suggestion}',\n    fix: 'go to one of its beats: {names}',\n    doc: 'Thrown by `Actions.go` (engine/anim/actions.ts) for a beat name the playing action lacks, or when nothing plays. The message names the closest beats.',\n  },\n  ANIM_ACTION_NO_CLIPS: {\n....\ndata/anim:\nLICENSES\nSOURCES.md\nactions\ncatalogs\ncmu\nsets\nupgrade.json\n\ndata/anim/actions:\nbackflip.json\nbored.json\ncharge.json\ndeathBlown.json\ndeathCrush.json\ndeathPop.json\ndeathShock.json\ndeathShrink.json\ndeathSink.json\ndeathSpin.json\ndeathTopple.json\ndizzy.json\ngetUp.json\ngrab.json\ngrabbed.json\ngroundPound.json\nhurt.json\nitemGet.json\njump.json\nlandHeavy.json\nledgeHang.json\npant.json\nrise.json\nroll.json\nshiver.json\nspinJump.json\ntechRoll.json\nwallSlide.json\n/**\n * @file The first-person camera (PLAN.md WP 3.9; doctrine: Common ground): the hero's eyes, turned by the devices,\n * and the near-body culling that hides his own body from them. `stepFirst` and `firstPose` are the pure steps;\n * `createFirstCamera` wraps them in a camera.\n *\n * It sits at the eye: `input.eye`, the midpoint of the rig's eye sockets (`eyePoint(skeleton, world)` on the animated\n * pose's FK, engine/anim/fk.ts) or the shooter model's eye height (engine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts), or\n * `FIRST_EYE_HEIGHT` above `input.follow` without either. It follows the eye across at once, and up and down with a\n * time constant of `FIRST_BOB_LAG` real seconds, which softens the head's bob, never more than `FIRST_TRAIL` behind.\n * `input.look` and `input.turn` turn it right and up (its yaw is the hero's aim), or `input.view` sets the view (the\n * sim's look, when no device turns the camera); `input.zoom` narrows the lens 5° a step within `FLY_FOV_RANGE`, from\n * `input.lens` when given (the player's field of view, engine/gfx/cameras/rig.ts).\n *\n * Near-body culling (`nearBodyCull`): the joints whose parts a renderer hides from this camera: all but those in `show`\n * (the hands, `FIRST_SHOWN`) and any shown part within `FIRST_NEAR_BODY` of the eye, a part running from its joint to\n * its children or its tip. The view draws first person's arms apart (`FIRST_ARMS`, a kick's leg `FIRST_KICK`: WP 13.12),\n * so the body hides every part (`firstBodyCull`), or with the full body on, its head, its arms and what is near the eye.\n *\n * Invariants: the pitch stays within ±`FLY_MAX_PITCH`; the head is always culled (the eyes are on it); pure.\n *\n * Codes: `cam3=first[,<yaw>,<pitch>[,<fov>]]` (degrees); a bare one looks where the camera before it looked. The\n * reader and the camera wrapper are engine/gfx/cameras/chase.ts's, shared by WP 3.9's cameras.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/40-cameras.js:95-101` (`firstPose`: the head point and its lag) and `:37`\n * (its pitch and lens; the hero was not drawn), at the eye sockets of the skeleton (engine/anim/skeleton.ts).\n *\n * @example\n * import { forwardKinematics } from '../../anim/fk';\n * import { Pose } from '../../anim/pose';\n * import { createSkeleton } from '../../anim/skeleton';\n * const skeleton = createSkeleton('build:heroic');\n * const world = forwardKinematics(skeleton, new Pose()); // standing at the origin, facing +Z\n * const first = createFirstCamera();\n * first.update({ eye: eyePoint(skeleton, world) }).position; // [0, 1.83…, 0.18…]: at his eyes (the first eye snaps)\n * nearBodyCull(skeleton, world, first.pose().position); // ['pelvis', 'spine0', …, 'toeR']: all but the hands\n * firstBodyCull(skeleton, world, first.pose().position, true).includes('thighL'); // false: the full body's legs show\n * first.code(); // 'cam3=first,0,-4.58,75'\n * createFirstCamera().update({ follow: [2, 0, 3] }).position; // [2, 1.5, 3]: eye height, without a rig\n * @see engine/gfx/cameras/first.test.ts\n */\nimport { socketPosition, tipPosition, type WorldPose } from '../../anim/fk';\nimport { JOINTS, PARENTS, type JointName, type Skeleton } from '../../anim/skeleton';\nimport { MathUtils, Vector3 } from '../../core/math';\nimport { codeDegrees, codeNumber, followCamera, readCode, type CodePart, type FollowCamera } from './chase';\nimport { FIRST_EFFECTS } from './effects';\nimport { FLY_FOV_RANGE, FLY_MAX_PITCH } from './fly';\nimport { makePose, rangeProblems, refuse, wrapAngle, type CameraInput, type CameraPose, type Vec3 } from './pose';\n\nconst DEG = MathUtils.DEG2RAD;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"b9b7e362-a997-4e21-8c7d-0e083ba36c3a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:28:38.416Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The viewmodel's arms rig (PLAN.md WP 13.12, docs/PLAYGROUND.md §4): first person's arms posed against the\n * camera, as games pose a viewmodel. Its skeleton, the player's build, stands upright under the camera, its eyes at the\n * camera's eye and its heading the camera's, so its shoulders sit just under and behind the eye whatever the body does\n * (the body's own, which the camera's profile height leaves 0.1 to 1.4 m away in a slide, a mantle or a skydive, could\n * not reach the picture). Each hand's grip (`weaponL`, `weaponR`) goes to a place in the camera's frame (`ARMS`): fists\n * up at rest, pumping with the gait's phase in a sprint, out for balance in a slide, raised in the air; a little bob on\n * the view effects' weapon bob (engine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts), a breath, and a sway behind the look's turn. A hand the\n * body holds on a contact (a ledge in a mantle, the wall in a climb, a rung, the cable, the floor) goes where the body's\n * is, as far as it holds it, and a carried gun where the body holds it from its eyes (from its right eye as far as its\n * sights are up, so they line up on the picture's centre: the hold's `aimed`, WP 13.20); then every hand is kept on the\n * arms' frame (lens.ts `intoArmsFrame`) and drawn along its ray within the arm's reach (the arms are drawn at their own\n * depth anyway, so only the ray shows). A punch throws its fist where the body's goes from its eyes (WP 13.19), and a\n * kick shows its leg: the body's right leg as it kicks, under the rig's hips. `armsInputOf` reads what the rig needs\n * off the player's animator and its traversal plant.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: it reads the body and the camera and writes its own pose; pure but for its own state\n * (the eased shares, the sway, the last look); the shown parts (`shown`) are the arms (and the kicking leg) bar any\n * part nearer the eye than `VIEWMODEL.cull`.\n *\n * @example\n * import { makePose } from '../cameras/pose';\n * const rig = new ArmsRig('build:adult');\n * const camera = makePose({ position: [0, 1.52, 0], fov: 74, near: 0.05 }); // facing +Z\n * rig.update(camera, { player: null, effects: null, phase: 0, clock: 0, held: [null, null], kick: null, gun: null, aspect: 16 / 9 }, 1 / 60); // prettier-ignore\n * rig.hands[1].z > 0.3; // true: the right fist in front of the eye\n * rig.shown; // ['upperArmL', 'forearmL', 'handL', 'upperArmR', 'forearmR', 'handR']\n * @see engine/gfx/viewmodel/rig.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Animator } from '../../anim/character';\nimport {\n  createWorldPose,\n  forwardKinematics,\n  jointPosition,\n  jointRotation,\n  socketPosition,\n  tipPosition,\n} from '../../anim/fk';\nimport { handTo } from '../../anim/ik';\nimport { Pose } from '../../anim/pose';\nimport { createSkeleton, JOINTS, PARENTS, socketIndex, type JointName, type Skeleton } from '../../anim/skeleton';\n