{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0118QiAQzLewg178JA3r6Ja4","type":"tool_result","content":"# Prettier checks code, data and the generated docs (ADR-0014, amendment 2). Hand-written prose stays as its author\n# wrote it: Prettier would re-pad its tables and rewrite its emphasis and lists, and DOCTRINE.md and docs/research/\n# are frozen. .gitignore's paths (out/, node_modules/, .cache/…) are skipped too.\n*.md\n!docs/INDEX.md\n!docs/API.md\n!docs/ERRORS.md\n!docs/escalations/README.md\ntests/baselines/port/\n# The clip sets: machine-written by tools/anim/repack.ts, each clip its codec text() (three lines a key), pinned\n# byte for byte by tests/unit/data/anim/sets/; Prettier would spread each key over 13 lines (ADR-0010 amendment 2).\ndata/anim/sets/\n# Written by npm.\npackage-lock.json\n# The lean package: the engine built as one module, and its page and README, hand-written but for the blocks\n# tools/lib/lean.ts writes (ADR-0024 amendment 1).\nlean/\n# The one-file playground: a build, written by node x html --write (tools/lib/oneFile.ts, ADR-0023 amendment 5).\nplayground.html\nout/\ndist/\n.cache/\nnode_modules/\ntest-results/\n.env*\n.claude/settings.local.json\n\n# TypeScript build info (tsc -b writes it)\n*.tsbuildinfo\n16: * owner asked of a self-contained file (ADR-0023 amendment 5). A file deleted between the listing and its read is skipped (`scanAssets`): at gate G6's\n120:  if (!game) return { approvals: [{ file: APPROVALS, keys: APPROVAL_KEYS, record: true }], fonts: ['data/fonts/'], newFonts: 'data/fonts/', ask: ASK }; // prettier-ignore\n138:/** The files git tracks or would track under `root`: tracked plus untracked, ignored ones left out. */\n189:      return fail(`${at} needs ${needsRecord ? 'a path, an escalation (\"ESC-NNNN\") and a reason' : 'a path and a reason (the owner\\'s answer)'}`); // prettier-ignore\n197:      warnings.push({ id: 'ASSET_STALE', message: `${at} approves ${path}, which no longer exists: remove the entry`, file }); // prettier-ignore\n231: * skipped, never counted: it is no asset, and reading it would crash the scan (see the file comment).\n294:      stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'ignore'],\ntools/checkAll.ts\ndepsCheck.ts\n/**\n * @file `npm run check` (T0, PLAN.md §8.1–§8.2): runs `tsc`, ESLint, Prettier and `node x check` at the same time and\n * fails if any fails. Run one after another they took about 9 s of T0's 10 s budget at G0, `tsc` alone about 4 s; in\n * parallel T0 takes as long as the slowest. Node runs this file directly (type stripping, as the hooks do; ADR-0014\n * amendment 4), so it needs nothing installed beyond the tools it starts.\n *\n * `tsc` is `npm run typecheck`'s command: `tsc -b` over the projects of tsconfig.check.json, which together hold\n * tsconfig.json's files. It reuses what the last run checked (node_modules/.cache/tsc/), so it costs what a change\n * reaches: measured 0.2 s unchanged, 1.5–3 s after a typical edit, about 6 s when an export of a module every file\n * reaches changes, against 6 s every time for `tsc --noEmit` (ADR-0014 amendment 7).\n *\n * Invariants: every tool runs to the end, so one run names every failure; each tool's output is printed whole, in\n * the fixed order below, after all have finished (never interleaved); the exit code is 0 only when all four pass,\n * else 1. Caches live under node_modules/.cache/, which `x ci --local` keeps across `npm ci`; a new checkout or\n * worktree has none, so its first run fills them (measured after G5: 13.9 s cold, Prettier 13.7 s of it; 5.8 s warm).\n *\n * Usage: `npm run check` (package.json: `\"check\": \"node tools/checkAll.ts\"`). Importing the module runs nothing.\n *\n * @see package.json, docs/TESTING.md\n */\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\n\n/** One T0 tool: its name and its command line, run from the repository root. */\nexport interface CheckTool {\n  name: string;\n  command: string;\n}\n\n/** The T0 tools, in the order their output is printed; `tsc` runs package.json's `typecheck` command. */\nexport const CHECK_TOOLS: CheckTool[] = [\n  { name: 'tsc', command: 'npx tsc -b tsconfig.check.json' },\n  { name: 'eslint', command: 'npx eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .' },\n  { name: 'prettier', command: 'npx prettier --check --cache .' },\n  { name: 'x check', command: 'node x check' },\n];\n\n/** The outcome of one tool: its exit code, combined output and time taken. */\ninterface ToolResult {\n  tool: CheckTool;\n/**\n * @file Vite's settings (the dev server and the build) and Vitest's (T1), in one file as Vitest expects (PLAN.md\n * §6.10, WPs 0.2 and 0.12).\n *\n * Invariants: every lab page (`labs/<name>/index.html`) and test page (`tests/pages/<name>.html`) is served as its\n * own page, and a missing page is a 404 (`appType: 'mpa'`). A bare `three` resolves to `three/webgpu`, as three.js's\n * WebGPU examples map it. The runtime dependencies are pre-bundled at startup, so a first page load never\n * re-optimizes and reloads (§4.7). The server listens on 127.0.0.1 and `$PORT` (default 5173). Every test file runs\n * the advice trap first (tests/setup/adviceTrap.ts), and `vitest --changed` reruns everything on the files that\n * tools/lib/tiers.ts's `T1_FULL` names.\n *\n * The build (`npm run build`) writes dist/ from the landing page (the root's\n * `index.html`) and every `labs/<name>/index.html`; test pages never ship (`harness.html` throws on purpose). In a game\n * made from the engine (engine-lock.json at its root, ADR-0024) the box is the worked example: served, never built. A page\n * ships only what it imports, never a `fetch()` of a repository path (§6.3). Nothing here needs the network, a\n * browser, the source checkouts or an `x` command: the build and Vitest both read this file. The one-file\n * playground (playground.html, tools/lib/oneFile.ts) is built apart, with this file's alias. The reference to\n * `vitest/config`, which adds `test` to Vite's config type, is kept in the declaration tsc -b emits (`preserve`), so\n * the tests' project, which sees this file through it, knows `config.test` (Vitest 4's main types no longer add it).\n *\n * @see tools/lib/vite.test.ts\n */\n/// <reference types=\"vitest/config\" preserve=\"true\" />\nimport { existsSync, globSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { availableParallelism } from 'node:os';\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\nimport { vitestRerunTriggers } from './tools/lib/tiers';\n\n/** The dev server's port: `$PORT` (each ultracode lane sets its own), else 5173. */\nconst PORT = Number(process.env.PORT) || 5173;\n\n/** The repository root: this file's directory. */\nconst ROOT = import.meta.dirname;\n\n/** Whether this is a game made from the engine (tools/game/new-game.mjs), not the engine's own repository. */\nconst GAME = existsSync(join(ROOT, 'engine-lock.json'));\n\n/** The pages a build ships, as absolute paths by entry name: `index` (the landing page), then `labs/<name>`. */\nconst PAGES = Object.fromEntries(\n  ['index.html', ...globSync('labs/*/index.html', { cwd: ROOT }).sort()]\n    .filter((page) => !(GAME && page.startsWith('labs/box/')))\n    .map((page) => [dirname(page) === '.' ? 'index' : dirname(page), join(ROOT, page)]),\n);\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  appType: 'mpa',\n  resolve: {\n    alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }],\n  },","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"252087d8-1cb0-41a7-a96e-6817c38f82d3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:36:04.576Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Prettier checks code, data and the generated docs (ADR-0014, amendment 2). Hand-written prose stays as its author\n# wrote it: Prettier would re-pad its tables and rewrite its emphasis and lists, and DOCTRINE.md and docs/research/\n# are frozen. .gitignore's paths (out/, node_modules/, .cache/…) are skipped too.\n*.md\n!docs/INDEX.md\n!docs/API.md\n!docs/ERRORS.md\n!docs/escalations/README.md\ntests/baselines/port/\n# The clip sets: machine-written by tools/anim/repack.ts, each clip its codec text() (three lines a key), pinned\n# byte for byte by tests/unit/data/anim/sets/; Prettier would spread each key over 13 lines (ADR-0010 amendment 2).\ndata/anim/sets/\n# Written by npm.\npackage-lock.json\n# The lean package: the engine built as one module, and its page and README, hand-written but for the blocks\n# tools/lib/lean.ts writes (ADR-0024 amendment 1).\nlean/\n# The one-file playground: a build, written by node x html --write (tools/lib/oneFile.ts, ADR-0023 amendment 5).\nplayground.html\nout/\ndist/\n.cache/\nnode_modules/\ntest-results/\n.env*\n.claude/settings.local.json\n\n# TypeScript build info (tsc -b writes it)\n*.tsbuildinfo\n16: * owner asked of a self-contained file (ADR-0023 amendment 5). A file deleted between the listing and its read is skipped (`scanAssets`): at gate G6's\n120:  if (!game) return { approvals: [{ file: APPROVALS, keys: APPROVAL_KEYS, record: true }], fonts: ['data/fonts/'], newFonts: 'data/fonts/', ask: ASK }; // prettier-ignore\n138:/** The files git tracks or would track under `root`: tracked plus untracked, ignored ones left out. */\n189:      return fail(`${at} needs ${needsRecord ? 'a path, an escalation (\"ESC-NNNN\") and a reason' : 'a path and a reason (the owner\\'s answer)'}`); // prettier-ignore\n197:      warnings.push({ id: 'ASSET_STALE', message: `${at} approves ${path}, which no longer exists: remove the entry`, file }); // prettier-ignore\n231: * skipped, never counted: it is no asset, and reading it would crash the scan (see the file comment).\n294:      stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'ignore'],\ntools/checkAll.ts\ndepsCheck.ts\n/**\n * @file `npm run check` (T0, PLAN.md §8.1–§8.2): runs `tsc`, ESLint, Prettier and `node x check` at the same time and\n * fails if any fails. Run one after another they took about 9 s of T0's 10 s budget at G0, `tsc` alone about 4 s; in\n * parallel T0 takes as long as the slowest. Node runs this file directly (type stripping, as the hooks do; ADR-0014\n * amendment 4), so it needs nothing installed beyond the tools it starts.\n *\n * `tsc` is `npm run typecheck`'s command: `tsc -b` over the projects of tsconfig.check.json, which together hold\n * tsconfig.json's files. It reuses what the last run checked (node_modules/.cache/tsc/), so it costs what a change\n * reaches: measured 0.2 s unchanged, 1.5–3 s after a typical edit, about 6 s when an export of a module every file\n * reaches changes, against 6 s every time for `tsc --noEmit` (ADR-0014 amendment 7).\n *\n * Invariants: every tool runs to the end, so one run names every failure; each tool's output is printed whole, in\n * the fixed order below, after all have finished (never interleaved); the exit code is 0 only when all four pass,\n * else 1. Caches live under node_modules/.cache/, which `x ci --local` keeps across `npm ci`; a new checkout or\n * worktree has none, so its first run fills them (measured after G5: 13.9 s cold, Prettier 13.7 s of it; 5.8 s warm).\n *\n * Usage: `npm run check` (package.json: `\"check\": \"node tools/checkAll.ts\"`). Importing the module runs nothing.\n *\n * @see package.json, docs/TESTING.md\n */\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\n\n/** One T0 tool: its name and its command line, run from the repository root. */\nexport interface CheckTool {\n  name: string;\n  command: string;\n}\n\n/** The T0 tools, in the order their output is printed; `tsc` runs package.json's `typecheck` command. */\nexport const CHECK_TOOLS: CheckTool[] = [\n  { name: 'tsc', command: 'npx tsc -b tsconfig.check.json' },\n  { name: 'eslint', command: 'npx eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .' },\n  { name: 'prettier', command: 'npx prettier --check --cache .' },\n  { name: 'x check', command: 'node x check' },\n];\n\n/** The outcome of one tool: its exit code, combined output and time taken. */\ninterface ToolResult {\n  tool: CheckTool;\n/**\n * @file Vite's settings (the dev server and the build) and Vitest's (T1), in one file as Vitest expects (PLAN.md\n * §6.10, WPs 0.2 and 0.12).\n *\n * Invariants: every lab page (`labs/<name>/index.html`) and test page (`tests/pages/<name>.html`) is served as its\n * own page, and a missing page is a 404 (`appType: 'mpa'`). A bare `three` resolves to `three/webgpu`, as three.js's\n * WebGPU examples map it. The runtime dependencies are pre-bundled at startup, so a first page load never\n * re-optimizes and reloads (§4.7). The server listens on 127.0.0.1 and `$PORT` (default 5173). Every test file runs\n * the advice trap first (tests/setup/adviceTrap.ts), and `vitest --changed` reruns everything on the files that\n * tools/lib/tiers.ts's `T1_FULL` names.\n *\n * The build (`npm run build`) writes dist/ from the landing page (the root's\n * `index.html`) and every `labs/<name>/index.html`; test pages never ship (`harness.html` throws on purpose). In a game\n * made from the engine (engine-lock.json at its root, ADR-0024) the box is the worked example: served, never built. A page\n * ships only what it imports, never a `fetch()` of a repository path (§6.3). Nothing here needs the network, a\n * browser, the source checkouts or an `x` command: the build and Vitest both read this file. The one-file\n * playground (playground.html, tools/lib/oneFile.ts) is built apart, with this file's alias. The reference to\n * `vitest/config`, which adds `test` to Vite's config type, is kept in the declaration tsc -b emits (`preserve`), so\n * the tests' project, which sees this file through it, knows `config.test` (Vitest 4's main types no longer add it).\n *\n * @see tools/lib/vite.test.ts\n */\n/// <reference types=\"vitest/config\" preserve=\"true\" />\nimport { existsSync, globSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { availableParallelism } from 'node:os';\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\nimport { vitestRerunTriggers } from './tools/lib/tiers';\n\n/** The dev server's port: `$PORT` (each ultracode lane sets its own), else 5173. */\nconst PORT = Number(process.env.PORT) || 5173;\n\n/** The repository root: this file's directory. */\nconst ROOT = import.meta.dirname;\n\n/** Whether this is a game made from the engine (tools/game/new-game.mjs), not the engine's own repository. */\nconst GAME = existsSync(join(ROOT, 'engine-lock.json'));\n\n/** The pages a build ships, as absolute paths by entry name: `index` (the landing page), then `labs/<name>`. */\nconst PAGES = Object.fromEntries(\n  ['index.html', ...globSync('labs/*/index.html', { cwd: ROOT }).sort()]\n    .filter((page) => !(GAME && page.startsWith('labs/box/')))\n    .map((page) => [dirname(page) === '.' ? 'index' : dirname(page), join(ROOT, page)]),\n);\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  appType: 'mpa',\n  resolve: {\n    alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }],\n  },","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0118QiAQzLewg178JA3r6Ja4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
