{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P1Su2XXrtY4CQMRGEp7ETu","type":"tool_result","content":"labs/playground/looks/clean.ts:4: * lit style (`style` left `''`), lit by the hour's sky (`sky:daylight`, engine/gfx/daylight.ts: the sun, the moon,\nlabs/playground/looks/clean.ts:16: * Invariants: data only, the kind's fields (`node x describe look`); the sky `sky:daylight`; the scene's own style;\nlabs/playground/looks/clean.ts:29:/** The look `look:playground-clean`: the scene's own lit materials under the hour's sky at full resolution, smoothed. */\nlabs/playground/looks/clean.ts:32:    \"The playground clean, its default: the scene's own lit materials under the hour's sky at full resolution, textures and edges smoothed; no bands, ink, outlines or pixels.\",\nlabs/playground/looks/clean.ts:33:  sky: 'sky:daylight',\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:2: * @file The kind `sky` (PLAN.md WP 7.1, §6.6): its fields (`SKY_FIELDS`: the background colour, the dome, the sun, the\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:4: * a preset, and the built-in presets, declared on the shared registry when this module loads: `sky:hall`, the\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:5: * torch-lit hall (dark, torches, fog past the focus), and `sky:daylight`, a plain day for fixtures. Others arrive\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:6: * when a scene needs one. engine/gfx/sky.ts's `createSky` puts a preset on a scene. Split from sky.ts at its line cap.\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:14: * defineSkies(reg); // the kind and its presets, sky:hall and sky:daylight\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:15: * defineSky('sky:dusk', { background: '#402030', sun: { intensity: 1, elevation: 0.1 } }, reg).sun.azimuth; // 0: as the field's default\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:16: * @see engine/gfx/sky.test.ts\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:32:/** The fields of a `sky` entry; see the file comment. Angles in radians, lengths in metres. */\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:37:  dome: group(\"The sky dome: three.js's SkyMesh (the Preetham daylight model), lit by the sun's direction.\", {\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:80:/** A `sky` entry. */\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:90:/** A backdrop as a `sky` entry gives it. */\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:93:/** Declares the kind `sky` and the built-in presets on `registry`, unless it has them. */\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:95:  if (!registry.kinds().includes('sky')) {\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:96:    registry.defineKind('sky', {\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:100:      fallback: 'sky:daylight',\n/**\n * @file The kind `sky` (PLAN.md WP 7.1, §6.6): its fields (`SKY_FIELDS`: the background colour, the dome, the sun, the\n * ambient light, the fog, the backdrop's layers and how bright the light pool's point lights shine), `defineSky` for\n * a preset, and the built-in presets, declared on the shared registry when this module loads: `sky:hall`, the\n * torch-lit hall (dark, torches, fog past the focus), and `sky:daylight`, a plain day for fixtures. Others arrive\n * when a scene needs one. engine/gfx/sky.ts's `createSky` puts a preset on a scene. Split from sky.ts at its line cap.\n *\n * Invariants: data only, nothing drawn; every object field's default holds its properties' defaults, so a preset may\n * leave a whole object out. Angles in radians, lengths in metres.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n * const reg = createRegistry();\n * defineSkies(reg); // the kind and its presets, sky:hall and sky:daylight\n * defineSky('sky:dusk', { background: '#402030', sun: { intensity: 1, elevation: 0.1 } }, reg).sun.azimuth; // 0: as the field's default\n * @see engine/gfx/sky.test.ts\n */\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport type { Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { AMBIENT_FIELDS, FOG_FIELDS } from './atmosphere';\nimport { BACKDROP_KINDS } from './backdrop';\n\nconst text = (description: string, value: string) => ({ type: 'string', default: value, description }) as const;\nconst num = (description: string, value: number, minimum = 0, maximum?: number, unit?: string) =>\n  ({ type: 'number', default: value, minimum, ...(maximum === undefined ? {} : { maximum }), ...(unit ? { unit } : {}), description }) as const; // prettier-ignore\n/** An object field whose default holds every property's default, so a preset may leave the whole object out. */\nconst group = <const P extends Schema>(description: string, properties: P) => {\n  const defaults = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(properties).map(([key, field]) => [key, field.default]));\n  return { type: 'object', default: defaults, description, properties } as const;\n};\n\n/** The fields of a `sky` entry; see the file comment. Angles in radians, lengths in metres. */\nexport const SKY_FIELDS = {\n  description: text('What it looks like, in plain sentences.', ''),\n  background: text('The colour behind everything, hex, where neither dome nor backdrop is drawn.', '#06050b'),\n  pointLights: num(\"A multiplier on the light pool's intensities: 1 as the light kinds say, 0 puts them out.\", 1),\n  dome: group(\"The sky dome: three.js's SkyMesh (the Preetham daylight model), lit by the sun's direction.\", {\n    show: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Whether the dome is drawn.' },\n    turbidity: num('Haze in the air (SkyMesh turbidity): 2 is clear, 10 is hazy.', 2),\n    rayleigh: num('Rayleigh scattering (SkyMesh rayleigh): more is bluer, then redder.', 1),\n...\nengine/sim/lights.ts:3: * and runs. `setDaytime(w, { hour, rate })` sets the world's clock, the component `daytime` on an entity of its own,\nengine/sim/lights.ts:20: * // setDaytime(w, { hour: 17, rate: 24 / (20 * 60) });\nengine/sim/lights.ts:121:export function setDaytime<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(\nengine/sim/lights.ts:127:  if (!(hour >= 0 && hour < 24)) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where: 'setDaytime(w, { hour })', value: String(hour), expected: 'an hour from 0 up to 24: 12 is noon, 18.5 half past six in the evening' }); // prettier-ignore\nengine/sim/lights.ts:128:  if (!(rate >= 0 && Number.isFinite(rate))) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where: 'setDaytime(w, { rate })', value: String(rate), expected: 'hours a sim second, 0 or more: 24 / 1200 passes a day in 20 minutes' }); // prettier-ignore\n16: * Budgets (`FX_BUDGET`): every pool is made at its full size before the warm-up and never grows: 4,096 particles and\n17- * 1,024 glows (sprites, in pages of 1,024), 1,024 decals, 32 ribbons, so a frame costs at most 7 draw calls and builds\n18- * no pipeline. Past a budget, particles are not born and shapes are left out; `stats()` counts them. An emitter whose\n19- * entry says `gpu` bursts into the GPU's ring instead while the effects have one (`useGpuParticles`, WP 11.3), which the\n20- * chain draws (engine/gfx/enhanced/particles.ts); the floor rings are engine/gfx/fx/rings.ts's.\n21- * `register(warmup)` registers every pool. With `enabled` false it draws nothing, draws no random number and plays\n22- * no event (the trace is still read, so turning it on again plays only what comes next).\n23- *\n24- * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/35-effects.js:81-131` (`drawEffects`: telegraphs, trails, bolts with the\n25- * first four lit, particles) and `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:1569-1580` (`hitFx`), with shardfall's event bursts\n26- * and object lights (`shardfall:crates/pav_view/src/fx.rs:264-276, 290-480`).\n27- *\n28- * Invariants: presentation only: it reads what it is given and writes only its own objects; equal calls, streams and\n--\n70:export const FX_BUDGET = { particles: 4096, glows: 1024, decals: 1024, ribbons: 32, boltLights: 4 } as const;\n71-\n72-/** How a bolt looks: the Stress test's hero bolt by default. */\n73-export const BOLT = { color: '#ffb347', core: '#fff3c4', halo: 0.3125, radius: 0.125, light: 10, reach: 2.5 } as const;\n74-\n75-/** What `createEffects` takes. */\n76-export interface EffectsOptions {\n77-  /** The visual streams: the sim world's (`(...keys) => w.fxRng(...keys)`); seed 1's by default. */\n78-  fxRng?: (...keys: readonly (string | number)[]) => Rng;\n79-  /** The registry of the emitters and telegraphs; the shared one by default. */\n80-  registry?: Registry;\n81-}\n82-\n--\n136:  /** This frame's lights: running emitters' (flickering, pulsing) and the first `FX_BUDGET.boltLights` bolts'. */\n137-  lights(): FxLight[];\nengine/gfx/enhanced:\naa.test.ts\naa.ts\nair.test.ts\nair.ts\nao.test.ts\nao.ts\ncrowdNodes.ts\ncrowdRegions.ts\ncrowds.test.ts\ncrowds.ts\ncsm.test.ts\ncsm.ts\ngi.test.ts\ngi.ts\nlighting.test.ts\nlighting.ts\nparticles.test.ts\nparticles.ts\nssr.test.ts\nssr.ts\ntiming.test.ts\ntiming.ts\n\nengine/gfx/fx:\ndecals.test.ts\ndecals.ts\neffects.test.ts\neffects.ts\nemitters.test.ts\nemitters.ts\nparticles.test.ts\nparticles.ts\npayload.ts\npresets.ts\nribbons.test.ts\nribbons.ts\nrings.ts\nshake.test.ts\nshake.ts\nsprites.test.ts\nsprites.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"58a99d14-e5fa-40e9-83f2-f42d73e5023f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:43:16.871Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"labs/playground/looks/clean.ts:4: * lit style (`style` left `''`), lit by the hour's sky (`sky:daylight`, engine/gfx/daylight.ts: the sun, the moon,\nlabs/playground/looks/clean.ts:16: * Invariants: data only, the kind's fields (`node x describe look`); the sky `sky:daylight`; the scene's own style;\nlabs/playground/looks/clean.ts:29:/** The look `look:playground-clean`: the scene's own lit materials under the hour's sky at full resolution, smoothed. */\nlabs/playground/looks/clean.ts:32:    \"The playground clean, its default: the scene's own lit materials under the hour's sky at full resolution, textures and edges smoothed; no bands, ink, outlines or pixels.\",\nlabs/playground/looks/clean.ts:33:  sky: 'sky:daylight',\nengine/gfx/skyKind.ts:2: * @file The kind `sky` (PLAN.md WP 7.1, §6.6): its fields (`SKY_FIELDS`: the background colour, the dome, the sun, th