{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gc3ZWxH64vEa2gdLFpebuB","type":"tool_result","content":"audio.test.ts\naudio.ts\nbuffers.test.ts\nbuffers.ts\ngesture.test.ts\ngesture.ts\nmixer.ts\nmusic.ts\nreverb.test.ts\nreverb.ts\nsound.ts\nspatial.test.ts\nspatial.ts\nvoices.test.ts\nvoices.ts\n12- * a pause menu), `duck(seconds)` holds for that long (an effect played with `duck`), and timed ducks overlap.\n13- *\n14: * Invariants: volumes are clamped to [0, 1]; `BUS_VOLUMES` are the starting levels (the source's: master 0.7, music\n15- * 0.5, the rest 1). A room change fades the old reverb out and the new one in over `ROOM_FADE` seconds; asking for\n16- * the room already in place changes nothing, so a game may name its room every frame. Nothing here reads a clock but\n17- * the context's own `currentTime`.\n18- *\n19- * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3714-3735` (`_init`, `_levels`, `setVolume`, `mute`, `_duck`): the\n20- * master, sfx and music buses and their levels, the 0.35 duck; `ui`, `ambience`, timed ducks and the reverb added.\n21- *\n22- * @example\n23- * // browser: Web Audio's nodes exist only in a page (tests/e2e/examples.spec.ts; tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts mixes)\n24- * const mixer = createMixer(new OfflineAudioContext(2, 44100, 44100));\n--\n37-\n38-/** The starting volumes, the master's included. */\n39:export const BUS_VOLUMES: Readonly<Record<AudioBus | 'master', number>> = Object.freeze({\n40-  master: 0.7,\n41-  effects: 1,\n42-  music: 0.5,\n43-  ui: 1,\n44-  ambience: 1,\n45-});\n46-\n47-/** How ducking sounds: the level the ducked buses fall to, and how fast, s. */\n48-export const DUCK = Object.freeze({\n49-  level: 0.35,\n--\n91-    return node;\n92-  };\n99:export interface Audio {\n100-  readonly state: AudioState;\n101-  /** The context, once there is one. */\n102-  readonly context: BaseAudioContext | null;\n103-  play(id: string, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\n104-  footstep(surface: stri