{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G5aXombYuVQJx4mTXEQspz","type":"tool_result","content":"7: * `engine/dev/bot.ts` and the gallery's scene (`engine/dev/galleryScene.ts`), every lab's scenes and cast (the box's,\n8: * the starter game's, a game's own), the box's and the playground's sound events (labs/box/sounds/events.ts,\n9: * labs/playground/sounds/{events,ground}.ts: the scenes' `sounds`), and the fixture scenes; `*.test.ts` files are\n8: * the starter game's, a game's own), the box's and the playground's sound events (labs/box/sounds/events.ts,\n9: * labs/playground/sounds/{events,ground}.ts: the scenes' `sounds`), and the fixture scenes; `*.test.ts` files are\n43:export const SIM_SIDE = [\n54:  'labs/*/scenes/**',\n55:  'labs/*/cast/**',\n56:  'labs/box/sounds/events.ts',\n57:  'labs/playground/sounds/events.ts',\n58:  'labs/playground/sounds/ground.ts',\n111:function imports(name: string, files: string[], patterns: object[]): Linter.Config {\n143:      files: SIM_SIDE,\n169:    imports('sim: three.js and Node built-ins', SIM_SIDE, [THREE_ENTRY, NODE_PREFIX]),\n20: * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\n21- * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\n22- *\n23- * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\n24- * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\n25- * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\n26- * shared registry when this module loads.\n27- *\n28- * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\n29- * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\n30- *\n--\n56:export const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\n57-  'Escape',\n58-  'PadStart',\n59-  'PadHome',\n18: * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\n19- * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\n20- * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\n21- * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\n22- *\n23- * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\n24- * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\n25- * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\n26- * shared registry when this module loads.\n27- *\n28- * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\n29- * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\n30- *\n--\n35: * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\n36- * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\n37- * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\n38- */\n39-import { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\n40-import { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\n71:export const PARTICLE_FIELDS = {\n129:export const EMITTER_FIELDS = {\n131:  ...PARTICLE_FIELDS,\n170:export type ParticleFields = Omit<Entry<typeof PARTICLE_FIELDS>, 'id' | 'kind'>;\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'number', minimum },\n    default: value,\n    type: 'number',\n    default: value,\n    minimum: 0,\n  area: vec3('Half extents of the box particles start in, around where it bursts.', 'm'),\n  velocity: vec3(\"Every particle's starting velocity.\", 'm/s'),\n  spread: amount(1, 'm/s', 'Random extra speed in any direction, up to this.'),\n  gravity: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm/s²', description: 'Pulls particles down; below 0 they rise.' },\n  drag: amount(0, '1/s', 'Slows them: the share of their speed lost per second.'),\n  turbulence: amount(0, 'm/s²', 'Swirls them (smoke, fireflies).'),\n  life: pair([1, 1.5], 'The shortest and longest a particle lives.', 's'),\n  size: pair([0.1, 0], 'Its radius at birth and at death.', 'm'),\n  color: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: ['#ffffff', '#ffffff'],\n    description: 'Its colour at birth and at death, hex.',\n  brightness: pair([1, 1], 'What each colour is multiplied by, linear: above 1 it glows (with bloom, WP 7.4).'),\n  alpha: pair([1, 0], 'Its opacity at birth and at death, 0 to 1.'),\n  additive: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: 'Adds light (fire, sparks, magic) instead of covering.' },\n  stretch: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Streaks along its velocity (sparks, rain).' },\n  lands: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Lands on the floor and bounces: see floor.' },\n  floor: {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 0,\n    unit: 'm',\n    description: \"The floor's height above the ground the burst names (else where it bursts), when it lands.\",\n  bounce: amount(0.3, '', 'How much of its fall speed a landing keeps, 0 to 1.', 1),\n  prewarm: amount(0, 's', 'Born as if emitted over the last this many seconds, so a new emitter starts in full swing.'),\n  emitter: { type: 'string', default: 'emitter:sparks', description: \"The other emitter's id.\" },\n  count: { type: 'integer', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'Its particles per burst.' },\n  offset: vec3('Where it bursts, from where this one does.', 'm'),