{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GCXtkieb3zpMJ3FNcJZDcC","type":"tool_result","content":"level.test.ts.tmpl\nlevel.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n/**\n * @file The level `level:{{name}}`: what it is (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX). It\n * starts as a cabin of two storeys on 0.5 m tiles, 8 × 6 m: the ground floor, the hall (2.7 m clear), with a door\n * in its south wall, a window in its east wall and a flight of stairs along its west wall, rising north to the loft\n * (3 m up, 2.4 m clear), whose stairwell is railed on its east and south sides, a window in its east gable end and a\n * gable roof over it (30°, the ridge east to west, 0.3 m of eaves). The player starts in the hall.\n *\n * The text is level format 2 (engine/world/level/parse.ts): front matter, then a block (`storey`, `base`, `height`\n * and the top storey's roof) and a map per storey, bottom first, every map the same size; row 1 is the north edge,\n * column 1 the west. The engine's glyphs: `#` wall, `.` floor, `@` the player's spawn, `+` door (1 m: two tiles), `:`\n * window, `<` the flight (the loft's floor meets the void `~` over it on one side only: it rises toward that side),\n * `!` railing. Its room markers are its own glyphs (`{{NAME}}_ROOMS`): a character writes one glyph in a legend, so a level\n * made from this template gives its markers characters no other glyph has (`defineGlyph` names a clash).\n *\n * Invariants: the text compiles when it is defined (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` names each structural problem at its line and\n * column); its `rooms` (each room's floor) and `recipes` (the roof's look) are presentation only, never the sim's or\n * the hash's. Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * import { getLevel } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n * getLevel('level:{{name}}').storeys?.map((s) => s.name); // ['ground', 'loft']\n * @see {{id}}.test.ts\n */\nimport { defineGlyph, defineLevel } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n\n/** Its room markers: each one's character and the room it names. */\nexport const {{NAME}}_ROOMS = { g: 'hall', u: 'loft' } as const;\n\nfor (const [char, room] of Object.entries({{NAME}}_ROOMS)) {\n  defineGlyph(`glyph:{{name}}-${room}`, { char, description: `Floor marking the ${room}.`, mesh: 'floor', room });\n}\n\n/** Its text: two storeys, bottom first (see the file comment). */\nconst TEXT = `---\ndescription: A cabin on 0.5 m tiles, 8 × 6 m, the hall and the loft above it under a gable roof (replace).\ntile: 0.5\n---\n---\nstorey: ground\nbase: 0\nheight: 2.7\n---\n################\n#..............#\n#<<...........g#\n#<<............#\n#<<............:\n#<<............:\n#<<............#\n#<<.....@......#\n FAIL  labs/game/probe/site.test.ts [ labs/game/probe/site.test.ts ]\nEngineError: [CORE_BAD_SPEC] level \"level:hut\": [LEVEL_BAD_STOREY] hut:1:1: it has no base: give its floor's height (base: 0): write each storey as a block between two lines holding only --- before its map, bottom storey first: storey (a name), base (its floor, m) and height (its clear height, m), e\n ❯ codeError engine/core/log.ts:138:10\n    136| /** An `EngineError` for `code`, to throw: `throw codeError('CORE_NO_E…\n    137| export function codeError(code: string, values: CodeValues = {}, cause…\n    138|   return new EngineError(code, values, cause === undefined ? undefined…","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"631e1ae3-9818-4c5a-aca9-a31fd7c30775","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:27.992Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"level.test.ts.tmpl\nlevel.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n/**\n * @file The level `level:{{name}}`: what it is (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX). It\n * starts as a cabin of two storeys on 0.5 m tiles, 8 × 6 m: the ground floor, the hall (2.7 m clear), with a door\n * in its south wall, a window in its east wall and a flight of stairs along its west 