{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEFbstaBcD3ZhtLBU53","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All the checks passed and setup no longer needs a temp folder. I'm now applying the corrections: the missing use-system spec, a bad cross-reference, the look filter scopes, the ropeway behaviour, and replacing the literal exit-interview file name with STAGE.md.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8798,"cache_read_input_tokens":562969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8798},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"b0007b7c-d9bb-4cc2-8e15-2ba70bd1bcb0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:29:01.490Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEFbbmT7CPq5XJ55oth","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEFbstaBcD3ZhtLBU53","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JGRi1ak5BcwsXJXaBJW48R","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b) if count==0 else s.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# Header and exit-interview naming: each builder's TASK.md names its own files.\nrep('''without the plan's author. Paths are relative to your dev folder. \"The deliverable\" means the `.html` your TASK.md\nnames, in the folder above the dev folder; `exit-interview.json` goes beside it.''',\n'''without the plan's author. Paths are relative to your dev folder. \"The deliverable\" means the `.html` your TASK.md\nnames, in the folder above the dev folder (`..`); \"the exit-interview file\" is the JSON file your TASK.md names, beside it.''')\nrep('''**`scripts/bundle.mjs` reads `../exit-interview.json` and injects it as data''' if False else '''`scripts/bundle.mjs` reads `../exit-interview.json` and injects it as data''','''`scripts/bundle.mjs` reads the exit-interview file and injects it as data''')\nrep('''About matches `exit-interview.json`.''','''About matches the exit-interview file.''')\nrep('''inject exit-interview.json as data too''','''inject the exit-interview file as data too''')\nrep('''Write `../exit-interview.json` in exactly the shape your TASK.md gives''','''Write the exit-interview file in exactly the shape your TASK.md gives''')\nrep('''Source Information, feedback in chat and About; exit-interview.json''','''Source Information, feedback in chat and About; the exit-interview file''')\n\n# Original-work wording.\nrep('''taxi or hotel opening, no philosophy quotes on tapes in its style lifted from it, no music, logos or screens that copy it.''',\n'''taxi or hotel opening, no tapes of a villain quoting philosophers, no music, logos or screens that copy it.''')\n\n# Setup without a temp folder (verified).\nrep('''src=$(mktemp -d) && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge \"$src\" && node \"$src/tools/game/new-game.mjs\" . --name <slug>\nnpm ci --no-audit --no-fund                     # 6 s. Do NOT run scripts/setup.sh: it downloads Node and Chrome outside your folder\nmkdir -p .cache && mv \"$src\" .cache/engine-src && rm -rf .cache/engine-src/.git   # the engine's examples, to read\n''','''mkdir -p .cache && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge .cache/engine-src   # stays: the engine's examples, to read\nnode .cache/engine-src/tools/game/new-game.mjs . --name <slug> && rm -rf .cache/engine-src/.git\nnpm ci --no-audit --no-fund                     # 6 s. Do NOT run scripts/setup.sh: it downloads Node and Chrome outside your folder\n''')\n\n# Cross-reference.\nrep(\"`defineMovement('movement:merc', …)` from apex (§7.1)\",\"`defineMovement('movement:merc', …)` from apex (§6.1)\")\nrep('''intents. They can't drive NPCs or other seats, and calling them breaks lockstep. **Don't call them.** Write `arms` and\n   `use` systems (§6.2) that keep writing''','''intents. They can't drive NPCs or other seats, and calling them breaks lockstep. **Don't call them.** Write `arms` (§6.2)\n   and `use` (§6.12) systems that keep writing''')\n\n# Eye heights for arms.\nrep('''A system for every actor with `weapons`: draw, sights, fire, reload, recoil, per `engine/sim/weapons.ts`, driven by\n`seat.wants` for players and AI wants for NPCs.''','''A system for every actor with `weapons`: draw, sights, fire, reload, recoil, per `engine/sim/weapons.ts`, driven by\n`seat.wants` for players and AI wants for NPCs. Shots leave the eye (1.52 m standing, 0.81 m crouched).''')\n\n# Vehicles: seating and blocker, honest about what was verified.\nrep('''- **Seating:** in phase `rules` each step, `placeActor(w, driver, seatPoint)` (verified with the driver following the\n  car). While occupied, an empty seat's blocker is gone: a **blocker** is a kinematic body in group `crowd` that follows an\n  unoccupied car, so people on foot can't walk through it; remove it while anyone is seated. Hit people by `overlap` ahead of the\n  bumper: damage by speed, then `handOff` to ragdoll.\n- **Drawing:** chassis prop with `body:'none'`, writing its `sceneProp` `x, y, z, q` each step from the body (the view\n  interpolates). Four wheel props and a steering-wheel prop are written the same way (spin, steer, suspension).''',\n'''- **Seating:** in phase `rules` each step, `placeActor(w, driver, seatPoint)` with the seat's feet about 0.3 m below the\n  chassis centre (verified: the driver follows the car over 40 s). It throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` under a low level roof: catch\n  it and eject the driver.\n- **People on foot vs cars** (not verified; test it): a `flyer` chassis doesn't block actors, so an unoccupied car also holds a\n  **blocker**, a kinematic body in group `crowd` moved to the chassis each step. Remove it while anyone is seated. Map shots\n  on it to the vehicle. Hit people by `overlap` ahead of the bumper: damage by speed, then `handOff` to ragdoll.\n- **Drawing:** chassis prop with `body:'none'`, writing its `sceneProp` `x, y, z, q` each step from the body. The view reads those\n  fields and interpolates them, body or no body. Four wheel props and a steering-wheel prop are written the same way (spin,\n  steer, suspension).''')\nrep('''- **Other rides:** Mine ropeway with `addZipline` works only for `actor.player`; in co-op seats use your own simple ride, or leave the\n  ropeway out of the contract arena.''','''- **Other rides:** Mine ropeway with `addZipline`. Rides live in the movement model, so they work for any seat whose wants hold\n  `interact`; keep usables away from cable ends so one press means one thing. Ladders likewise.''')\n\n# Empty heading out; use system in.\nrep('''### 6.10 Map in hand and HUD (page, §10)\n\n### 6.11 Story engine (`contracts/`)''','''### 6.10 Story engine (`contracts/`)''')\nrep('''choices return through a custom intent (`'game:pick'`), so replays and co-op hold them.\n''','''choices return through a custom intent (`'game:pick'`), so replays and co-op hold them.\n\n### 6.11 Other world rules\n\nCeasefire: inside Sainte-Aurore's radius guns are forced holstered and nobody shoots first. Falling back from the map edge: §5.\nSave points: sleeping, and each contract step. Water: §5.\n\n### 6.12 Use (`use.ts`)\n\nOne system for every seat, replacing `addInteraction`. Each step (rate-limited per seat) find the nearest usable: a table of entries\n(door, usable prop, dropped gun, vehicle seat, bed, crate, person, tape, tin box, phone) within 2 m of the eye and within 60° of the look,\npreferring what the eye ray hits. Write it to `seat.target` with a prompt verb, which the page shows only for its own seat. A press acts through\nthe entry's data: doors with `useDoor`, a seat by entering the vehicle, a person by starting dialogue. **Carrying** (Contract 2's crates, charges): lift holsters your\ngun and caps speed at walk; use again drops it; it can ride in a pickup's bed. **Picking up a gun** swaps it with the slot's, condition and all.\n''')\nrep('''| Infrastructure for later content with normal tools | §4, §6.11 |''','''| Infrastructure for later content with normal tools | §4, §6.10 |''')\n\n# Look filters need scopes.\nrep('''- **`look:dry-season`:** `sky:'sky:daylight'`, `grade` (temperature +0.18, saturation 0.9, contrast 1.08), `split` warm/teal, `vignette` 0.25,\n  `air` (haze 0.35, height 8, shafts 0.6), light `grain`. Verified base: this reads as hot savanna already.''',\n'''- **`look:dry-season`:** `sky:'sky:daylight'`, `grade` (temperature +0.18, saturation 0.9, contrast 1.08), `split` warm/teal, `vignette` 0.25,\n  `air` (haze 0.35, height 8, shafts 0.6), light `grain`. A filter stays off until it has a `scope`, so give each `scope:'all'`. Verified:\n  `sky:daylight` + `grade` over the savanna texture and thorn trees already reads as hot savanna.''')\n\n# Same screens on every device; no-WebGPU message.\nrep('''Own action maps (`defineActionMap`, `look:true, aimWith:'centre', lock:true` for first person; a second for vehicles). Bindings rebindable with `input.listen`.\n''','''Every device gets the same game on the same screens; no desktop layout. Own action maps (`defineActionMap`, `look:true, aimWith:'centre', lock:true` for first person; a second for vehicles). Bindings rebindable with `input.listen`.\n''')\nrep('''A pad press or key press dismisses it for good. Test with Playwright's phone profile.\n''','''A pad press or key press dismisses it for good. Test with Playwright's phone profile.\n\nIf WebGPU is missing on any device, show a plain message naming a browser that has it; the engine has no WebGL fallback, and the sim still runs.\n''')\n\n# Title camera focus.\nrep('''No player needed for the camera; keep the player actor parked off-screen. Starting play''','''The view lights and shadows round the player actor, so park it near the camera's target, out of frame. Starting play''')\n\n# Slider reset wording.\nrep('''Settings use `when:'now'` and systems read them each use. `__engine.set` applies; `session.settings` reset restores.''','''Settings use `when:'now'` and systems read them at each use. `__engine.set` applies a value; reset writes each default from the table back the same way.''')\n\n# Pump wording, honest about what was run.\nrep('''5. **The pump:** `setInterval(pump, 16)` until the first `onFrame`, then from `onFrame`. All copies run on the paused clock through `inspector.step`.''',\n'''5. **The pump:** a 16 ms `setInterval` alone passes the harness (verified); once frames flow, step from `onFrame` for smooth motion, and keep the timer for when frames stop. All copies run on the paused clock through `inspector.step`.''')\n\n# Raw URLs.\nrep('''const session = readFileSync('.cache/hub/session.js', 'utf8'); // the unmodified client, from the raw URL in the hub README''','''const session = readFileSync('.cache/hub/session.js', 'utf8'); // the unmodified client: scripts/fetch-hub.mjs downloads it''')\nrep('''Everything is inline, so nothing depends on a CDN. Keep `.cache/hub/session.js` out of lint by living in `.cache/`. The client must stay byte-identical.''',\n'''`fetch-hub.mjs` downloads `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `.cache/hub/`, where lint and format can't touch them: the client must stay byte-identical. The protocol's full text is `README.md` at the same address; read it once. Everything in the deliverable is inline, so nothing depends on a CDN.''')\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf8').write(s)\nprint(len(s.split()), 'words', s.count('\\n'), 'lines')\nEOF\ngrep -n \"exit-interview\\|GameTitle\\|claude-opus\\|mktemp\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-140","description":"Apply the verified corrections to the plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8798,"cache_read_input_tokens":562969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8798},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"d4fadfbc-cda1-4ccf-bd47-df69d00fd2c9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:29:34.351Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEFbbmT7CPq5XJ55oth","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JGRi1ak5BcwsXJXaBJW48R":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b) if count==0 else s.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# Header and exit-interview naming: each builder's TASK.md names its own files.\nrep('''without the plan's author. Paths are relative to your dev folder. \"The deliverable\" means the `.html` your TASK.md\nnames, in the folder above the dev folder; `exit-interview.json` goes beside it.''',\n'''without the plan's author. Paths are relative to your dev folder. \"The deliverable\" means the `.html` your TASK.md\nnames, in the folder above the dev folder (`..`); \"the exit-interview file\" is the JSON file your TASK.md names, beside it.''')\nrep('''**`scripts/bundle.mjs` reads `../exit-interview.json` and injects it as data''' if False else '''`scripts/bundle.mjs` reads `../exit-interview.json` and injects it as data''','''`scripts/bundle.mjs` reads the exit-interview file and injects it as data''')\nrep('''About matches `exit-interview.json`.''','''About matches the exit-interview file.''')\nrep('''inject exit-interview.json as data too''','''inject the exit-interview file as data too''')\nrep('''Write `../exit-interview.json` in exactly the shape your TASK.md gives''','''Write the exit-interview file in exactly the shape your TASK.md gives''')\nrep('''Source Information, feedback in chat and About; exit-interview.json''','''Source Information, feedback in chat and About; the exit-interview file''')\n\n# Original-work wording.\nrep('''taxi or hotel opening, no philosophy quotes on tapes in its style lifted from it, no music, logos or screens that copy it.''',\n'''taxi or hotel opening, no tapes of a villain quoting philosophers, no music, logos or screens that copy it.''')\n\n# Setup without a temp folder (verified).\nrep('''src=$(mktemp -d) && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge \"$src\" && node \"$src/tools/game/new-game.mjs\" . --name <slug>\nnpm ci --no-audit --no-fund                     # 6 s. Do NOT run scripts/setup.sh: it downloads Node and C