{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xn8RxdHK72xUgX33mu9RJe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN: an open-world first-person mercenary game in a burning country\n2\t\n3\tInspired by Far Cry 2. Original world, cast, story, art and music. You build it from this plan and your TASK.md,\n4\twithout the plan's author. Paths are relative to your dev folder. \"The deliverable\" means the `.html` your TASK.md\n5\tnames, in the folder above the dev folder (`..`); \"the exit-interview file\" is the JSON file your TASK.md names, beside it.\n6\t\n7\t## 0. How to use this plan\n8\t\n9\t- **The design is decided.** Build it; don't reopen it. Every number is a starting value and most are dev sliders:\n10\t  tune by playtest scripts. Where you must deviate, do the simplest thing that keeps the feature, and write the call in\n11\t  `labs/game/README.md`.\n12\t- **\"Verified\"** means the plan's author ran it on this machine on 2026-11-04, on engine commit `e7a1243` and hub client\n13\t  1.4.0, with throwaway probes. If a verified recipe fails for you, look for what changed; don't redesign around it.\n14\t- **Your TASK.md wins** over this plan on anything it states. §15 maps each TASK.md requirement to the section here.\n15\t- **Features beat content.** No feature on the never-cut list may be stubbed. If you run short, shrink content, never\n16\t  below the floors:\n17\t\n18\t| Never cut | May shrink, never below |\n19\t|---|---|\n20\t| Gun wear, jams and clearing; wounds, syrettes and field surgery; fire with wind; fever and pills; buddies with rescue, debt and mercy; drivable vehicles with repair; map in hand; two factions' contracts and an ending; stones, locator and dealer; safehouses and saves; stealth in grass; day and night; dev mode with sliders; attract mode; hub session passing the harness; co-op on its own; touch notice; About/Credits; code-only audio with gibberish voices | Places: 7 (town + 6). Contracts: prologue + 5. Weapons: 8. Tapes: 4. Stone caches: 5. Buddies: 3. Enemy types: 4. Vehicles: pickup + boat. Songs: 3 |\n21\t\n22\t## 1. The game\n23\t\n24\t**Pitch.** You come up the river at the end of the dry season to serve a warrant on the Auctioneer, the arms dealer who\n25\tkeeps a civil war solvent by selling to both sides. You have a fever, a rusting rifle, debts to people who may or may not\n26\tdrag you out of the next fire, and a wind that is the only honest thing in the country.\n27\t\n28\t**Genre:** open-world first-person shooter with systemic fire and survival pressure. **Perspective:** first person, with\n29\tan over-the-shoulder option in Settings, a chase option while driving, and short eye-level \"body camera\" moments (§10.2).\n30\t\n31\t**Pillars**\n32\t\n33\t1. **Everything wears out.** Guns, vehicles, your body, your friends. Reliability is the real economy.\n34\t2. **Fire is your best weapon and you don't control it.** Wind decides. Burn scars stay and change the map.\n35\t3. **No clean hands.** Two factions, no good side, debts kept in a ledger. The writing never winks.\n36\t4. **The body is the interface.** Map in the hands, pills from the bottle, a bullet dug out of the arm, a wrench on the\n37\t   engine, all in real time. Only the pause menu stops the world.\n38\t5. **The land is the antagonist.** Long sightlines, chest-high grass, checkpoints on every road, heat haze.\n39\t\n40\t**What we take from the source, and what we make of it.** Mechanics are fair game; names, characters, places, story\n41\tbeats, art and music are not.\n42\t\n43\t| Source's idea | This game's version |\n44\t|---|---|\n45\t| Fire spreads with the wind | Same verb, deeper: a forecastable wind, ember spotting, fuel types, firebreaks, smoke that blinds AI, scars that strip stealth cover and regrow |\n46\t| Guns degrade and jam | Same, and condition shows on the gun in three rust tiers; enemy guns are junk; reliability upgrades at the dealer |\n47\t| Malaria and pills | Blackwater fever and quinine; attacks can show harmless mirages of people you failed |\n48\t| Buddies rescue you | A **ledger of debts**: each rescue is owed, and overdrawn buddies stop coming; mercy or a syrette when they fall |\n49\t| Map held in the hands | Paper map and tick-box locator on a diegetic CSS layer; you can walk or drive with it up |\n50\t| Diamonds | Rough stones in dead prospectors' tin boxes, found by a Geiger-style tick-box |\n51\t| Arms dealer villain with tapes | The **Auctioneer**: cassette \"lots\" in the patter of a sale. Every contract you do adds to his catalogue |\n52\t| Two rotten factions, ceasefire town | The Provisional Authority and the Basin Front; ceasefire in Sainte-Aurore |\n53\t\n54\t**Original-work rules.** Use nothing named or written in the source: no character, faction, place or mission names, no\n55\ttaxi or hotel opening, no tapes of a villain quoting philosophers, no music, logos or screens that copy it.\n56\tThe title is the one riff on the source's name, as TASK.md asks; everything else stands alone. Don't call the game a\n57\tsequel. Portray the invented country's people as people: named characters on every side, with no real nation, ethnic\n58\tgroup or leader named or caricatured.\n59\t\n60\t## 2. Setup and verified ground truth\n61\t\n62\tRun from the empty dev folder:\n63\t\n64\t```sh\n65\tmkdir -p .cache && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge .cache/engine-src   # stays: the engine's examples, to read\n66\tnode .cache/engine-src/tools/game/new-game.mjs . --name <slug> && rm -rf .cache/engine-src/.git\n67\tnpm ci --no-audit --no-fund                     # 6 s. Do NOT run scripts/setup.sh: it downloads Node and Chrome outside your folder\n68\texport CHROMIUM_PATH=$(ls ~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-*/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell | head -1)\n69\tnpm test && npm run check && node x shot labs/game   # all green on the starter (verified)\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\tRead `AGENTS.md` and `docs/GAME-GUIDE.md` once. **`labs/playground/` is not in a game's workspace**, but it is the best\n73\tworked example of nearly everything here (first person, guns, bodies, doors, sites, neighbours, looks, front end, attract\n74\tmode, sound): read it at `.cache/engine-src/labs/playground/` as needed. Grep `docs/API.md`; don't read it whole.\n75\t\n76\tVerified facts that will save you hours:\n77\t\n78\t- **Browser flags.** TASK.md's listed flags (`--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan\n79\t  --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`) alone **fail with this engine** (\"Instance dropped in popErrorScope\", never ready).\n80\t  Use `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. Adding\n81\t  `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader` is harmless. With these the starter is `ready` in 3.6 s from `file://`.\n82\t- **Headless shell only.** Playwright's default headless works. Full Chromium dies here with \"Socket path too long\"\n83\t  because run paths are long, so skip headed mode and xvfb.\n84\t- **`CHROMIUM_PATH`** (above) makes `node x shot`, `x film`, `x inspect` and `x replay --browser` work. Node 24.22.1 is\n85\t  fine. In Node drivers: `chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, args })` from `@playwright/test`.\n86\t- **Ports.** `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` piped to a script never prints its port (buffered): use\n87\t  `python3 -u`, or Node's `http` on port 0. Confirm the page's marker before trusting a result. Stop only your own PID.\n88\t- **What the checks scan.** `npm run check` fails on any PNG or base64 blob under the dev folder, except in git-ignored\n89\t  places: `out/` and `.cache/` are skipped by ESLint, Prettier, the asset scan and Vitest. Screenshots and temp bundles go\n90\t  in `out/`, hub files in `.cache/hub/`, the deliverable outside the dev folder.\n91\t- **Git.** The dev folder sits inside a larger repository that isn't yours. Make no commits there; `git init` inside the\n92\t  dev folder if you want history.\n93\t- **Sim costs on this machine.** A 1536 m terrain at 4 m cells adds 0.35 ms a step. An actor costs about 0.15 ms. A prop\n94\t  with **no** body costs about nothing a step. A prop with **its own body** costs about 1.2 µs a step (3,000 trees 3.9 ms),\n95\t  so trees are `body:'none'` props plus **one** fixed body holding all their colliders (verified). A site of 40 buildings\n96\t  on that terrain starts in 1.1 s and steps 24 actors in 1.8 ms.\n97\t- **`capture()` is 35–80 MB of JSON** at this scale. Never use it for saves or network resync.\n98\t\n99\t## 3. The engine: what to use and the walls\n100\t\n101\t| Need | Use | Note |\n102\t|---|---|---|\n103\t| World | `defineTerrain`, `defineLevel` (format 2 storeys), `defineSite`, scene `site:`, `addSiteBodies`, `createSiteNav` | The scene must name `site:` or `terrain:`, or the ground isn't drawn |\n104\t| Player feel | `defineMovement('movement:merc', …)` from apex (§6.1), `createCharacter`, `spawnActor`, settings `movement.*` | |\n105\t| Drawing things | `defineProp` + `spawnProp`, `defineMaterial`, `defineTexture`, `defineGeometry`, `defineBody` | Props are instanced and interpolated |\n106\t| Effects | `defineEmitter`, `frame.emit(id, at, key, scale)` in `onFrame`, sim events that burst emitters, `gpu: true` emitters, flame tongues on prop parts | Budget 4,096 CPU particles; use GPU emitters for smoke and fire |\n107\t| Look | `defineLook` (`sky:'sky:daylight'`, filters), `setDaytime`, `post.combine` set live | Numbers and amounts change without a shader build |\n108\t| Guns | `defineWeapon`, the `weapons` component (`weaponsFor`), `recoilStep`, `spreadOf`, `gunshot` events | Engine draws gun, sights, kick, tracers, flashes, holes |\n109\t| People | `spawnActor({ player:false })` with `actor.intents`, `sense`/`canSee`, `takeToken`, `damage`, `reactTo`, `addRagdolls`/`handOff`, `followRoute`, `stepAside` | See `labs/playground/cast/neighbours.ts` |\n110\t| Animals, refugees | Crowd bodies (`addAgent`, `crowdBody`, rig `quadruped`) | |\n111\t| Body animation | `defineAction` + `actOn` (call it after step 1, not in `setup`: verified), library clips (`node x anim find crawl`) | Credit imported clips per `data/anim/SOURCES.md` |\n112\t| Sound | `defineSfx`, `defineSong`, `createAudio` (`volume`, `music`, `intensity`, `stinger`, `play({position, bus})`, `footstep`) | `audio.context` is exposed |\n113\t| UI | `engine.ui.root` + plain HTML/CSS, `createMenu`, `createDialog`, `createBar`, `createPadCursor`, `createStore`, `createEngine({ modal, store })` | `createMenu` already does pad, keys, hover-moves-focus, click |\n114\t| Data as a tool | `defineKind`/`def` for contracts, places, squads, dealer stock | `node x describe contract` then lists them for designers |\n115\t| New entries | `node x new <kind> labs/game/<dir>/<name>` | Writes module + test |\n116\t\n117\t**Five walls. Plan around them; don't fight them.**\n118\t\n119\t1. **No access to the three.js scene.** Game code may import only `engine/index.ts` and `engine/sim-api.ts` (lint). Everything\n120\t   in the world is a prop, terrain, site, body, emitter, sky or look; everything else is the HTML overlay. For arbitrary\n121\t   meshes (grass, road ribbons, canopies), `defineGeometry` can return raw buffers by borrowing classes off a kit shape\n122\t   (verified, with a 36-blade grass tuft):\n123\t\n124\t   ```ts\n125\t   const g = boxGeometry({ width: 1, height: 1, depth: 1 });\n126\t   const Attr = g.getAttribute('position').constructor as new (a: Float32Array, n: number) => never;\n127\t   g.setAttribute('position', new Attr(new Float32Array(pos), 3)); // also 'normal' and 'uv'\n128\t   g.setIndex(indices); g.clearGroups(); return g; // set `budget` to its vertex count\n129\t   ```\n130\t   Give blades real normals (up-ish, both faces lit) and `side:'double'` in the material, or half of them draw black.\n131\t2. **`addWeapons`, `addMelee` and `addInteraction` only serve `actor.player === true`**, reading the step's one set of\n132\t   intents. They can't drive NPCs or other seats, and calling them breaks lockstep. **Don't call them.** Write `arms` (§6.2)\n133\t   and `use` (§6.12) systems that keep writing the same `weapons` component and emit `gunshot` with the same payload\n134\t   (`{ id, weapon, from, to, normal, body, target, hit }`), and set `motion.holstered` and `animator.weapon` as\n135\t   `engine/sim/weapons.ts` does. Then the engine draws guns, sights and tracers for players and NPCs alike. Read that file\n136\t   and copy its timing logic. `useDoor`, `strikeDoor`, `damage`, `entityOfBody`, `strikeEntity` are callable directly.\n137\t3. **First-person arms are a closed rig.** Games can't pose them, and reloads aren't animated at all. Fakes: lower the gun\n138\t   for a reload by setting `weapons.slot = -1` for the middle of the reload with `motion.holstered` kept false (film it to\n139\t   check); kick by `shots`; big moments use the body camera (§10.2). Full-body actions always show in shoulder view and\n140\t   to other players.\n141\t4. **Terrain paint is slope and height only.** Roads are draped ribbon props. Burn scars are props. Biomes are scatter.\n142\t5. **A running page can't switch scenes.** One scene, `game:world`, with a setting `game.mode`\n143\t   (`title | story | attract | contract`); change it with `__engine.set`, then restart with `inspector.seed(n)`.\n144\t\n145\tTexture generators write `texel.color` in **sRGB bytes 0–255**, not 0–1 (verified; 0–1 draws black).\n146\t\n147\t## 4. Architecture\n148\t\n149\t```\n150\tlabs/game/\n151\t  index.html  main.ts          page entry: reads mode, starts engine, wires everything (keep small)\n152\t  title.ts                     the game's title, one constant\n153\t  scenes/                      SIM-SIDE: imports only engine/sim-api.ts (lint enforces scenes/** and cast/**)\n154\t    world.ts                   defineScene('game:world'), setup order, modes\n155\t    settings.ts                every tunable in one table: path, default, min, max, label, group\n156\t    map.ts roads.ts scatter.ts terrain + site + places, road polylines, deterministic scatter\n157\t    seats.ts arms.ts use.ts health.ts fever.ts fire.ts wind.ts vehicles.ts buddies.ts economy.ts story.ts save.ts digest.ts\n158\t    ai/ perception.ts squads.ts soldier.ts driver.ts wildlife.ts\n159\t    contracts/ *.ts            contracts as data; the engine that runs them\n160\t    text/ *.ts                 every line of dialogue, briefing and tape, as data\n161\t  cast/                        SIM-SIDE: spawn player, soldiers, buddies, civilians, animals; actions\n162\t  props/ weapons/              SIM-SIDE defineProp, defineWeapon (sim-api exports them)\n163\t  art/                         PAGE: textures, materials, geometry, bodies, emitters, looks, cameras\n164\t  sounds/                      PAGE: sfx, songs, voice synth, event-to-sound map\n165\t  ui/                          PAGE: hud, prompts, glyphs, title, pause, settings, map, ledger, dialogue, shop, dev, about, card, touch\n166\t  net/                         PAGE: net.ts (interface), hub.ts, tabs.ts, rtc.ts, lockstep.ts, wire.ts\n167\t  bot.ts attract.ts            bot intents shared by tests and attract mode\n168\t  replays/                     one short golden replay\n169\ttests/game/                    browser and harness drivers (.mjs), verify.mjs\n170\tscripts/                       bundle.mjs, fetch-hub.mjs\n171\t```\n172\t\n173\tRules from the engine that apply everywhere: sim code uses no clock, `Math.random`, DOM or storage; time in whole steps;\n174\trandomness from `w.rng('name')`; state in components; `Math.pow`, not `**`; every file opens with an `@file` comment, warns\n175\tpast 400 lines and fails past 600. Presentation reads the sim and never writes it.\n176\t\n177\t**Seats: one path for every player from day one.** Every human-controlled actor has a `seat` component. The first system\n178\tin phase `intents` (`game.seats`) builds `seat.wants = { move, look, aim, b, p }` for each seat: for the actor with\n179\t`actor.player === true` from the step's intents, for the others from the step's custom key `'game:seats'[n]`, which it\n180\talso copies to `actor.intents`. It computes `p` itself as the edges of `b` against last step, plus any `p` given. **All\n181\tgame systems read `seat.wants`, never the raw intents.** NPCs have no seat. In solo play there is one seat. Sim settings\n182\tthat fork behaviour by `actor.player` (`input.sprint`, `input.crouch`) stay at defaults in co-op.\n183\t\n184\t**Saves are game data, not captures.** `save.ts` writes plain JSON (seat position, inventory, condition, stones, flags,\n185\tbuddies, hour, wind, burn map as run-length text, cleared places) to `createStore` at sleep and at contract steps. Load\n186\trestarts the scene and applies it through the dev action `load`. A session gets the hub's empty storage and saves nothing.\n187\t\n188\t**Data-driven so designers can extend it:** places, squads, contracts, dealer stock and weapons are registry kinds or\n189\ttables with schemas. Adding a contract or a checkpoint takes no new code.\n190\t\n191\t## 5. The world\n192\t\n193\t**Map.** A 1536 × 1536 m site, 4 m cells (`size:[1536,1536], cell:4`; `size` is metres), x east, z south. A ring of hills\n194\t70–120 m high (`hills` round the edge, plus a sim rule that turns back anything past 1450 m from centre) keeps you in;\n195\tthe terrain ends at the edge, and a vehicle will fall off it (verified), so the rule must hold. Rolling ground: `height:14,\n196\tscale:180, octaves:5, ridges:0.3`. Materials: ground `material:savanna` (straw over red earth), steep `material:laterite`,\n197\thigh `material:ironstone` from 45 m up. Every place sits on `flats`.\n198\t\n199\t**The river** crosses west to east near z≈900 as a chain of negative `hills` (depth ≤ 1.2 m below `waterY`), drawn as one\n200\tflat water prop at `waterY` with `texture:water`. No swimming: you wade at half speed. Vehicles stall past 0.8 m, except\n201\tfords. North of it is dry savanna; south is greener riverine woodland that burns slower (fuel table, §6.5).\n202\t\n203\t**Places** (coordinates are the centre; adjust to fit the terrain, keep the relations):\n204\t\n205\t| Place | At (x, z) | What it's for |\n206\t|---|---|---|\n207\t| **Sainte-Aurore**, ceasefire town | 760, 790 | Weapons forced holstered. Hotel Splendide (bar, Yaw), Customs House (Authority), Cinema Rex (Front), jetty. 12 buildings, townsfolk on routes |\n208\t| **Km-40 checkpoint** | 620, 520 | First firefight. Boom gate, sandbags, watchtower, radio hut |\n209\t| **Bridge Post checkpoint** | 1010, 790 | East road; a technical parks here |\n210\t| **Ford Post checkpoint** | 560, 985 | South crossing |\n211\t| **Pump Station** | 1010, 360 | Pipeline, fuel tanks, explosive set piece; co-op's arena |\n212\t| **Salt Works** | 1240, 260 | White pans (no fuel: a natural firebreak), conveyors, wide-open fight; buddy rescue |\n213\t| **Mine No. 6** | 300, 300 | Red pit in iron hills, rail cars, aerial ropeway (`addZipline`); the finale |\n214\t| **Belvédère Estate** | 1130, 1180 | Tobacco barns, drying racks, the big burn |\n215\t| **Mission Sainte-Claire** | 330, 1120 | Clinic, refugees on routes, Sister Perpetua, pills |\n216\t| **Airstrip** | 1200, 620 | Ferreira's container (dealer), hangar safehouse, wrecked plane |\n217\t| **Broken rail bridge** | 880, 905 | Landmark and ambush spot |\n218\t| **Safehouses** | Water Tower 470, 650; Ferry Shed 640, 1040; Hangar 1240, 640 | Clear the guards to claim each |\n219\t| **Barge wreck** | 300, 900 | Prologue start |\n220\t\n221\t**Roads** are polylines in `roads.ts` joining all of the above (one main east–west road through town, north road to Km-40\n222\tthen Mine, east road to Bridge Post and Airstrip, south road over the ford to Mission and Estate). The same data draws the\n223\tdraped ribbon props, gives footstep surface and fire-free cells, and steers AI drivers. A pipeline and a power line on\n224\tpoles run across the savanna as long-distance landmarks.\n225\t\n226\t**Scatter** is deterministic (`scatterTerrain` with `salt`, or your own by road and place distance):\n227\t\n228\t- About 1,200 trees: 3 flat-topped thorn trees, a fat bottle tree, thorn bushes. `body:'none'` plus one fixed body of\n229\t  capsule colliders.\n230\t- Grass as **patches**: a prop per 16 m square of fuel, 200–400 raw-geometry blades, knee to chest high, about 6,000 patches.\n231\t  Removing one is how grass burns. A setting `game.detail` (0.1–1) thins scatter for tests and software adapters (read\n232\t  `__engine.info().adapter.fallback`); default 1. TASK.md puts FPS out of scope, so don't hold back on real GPUs.\n233\t- Rocks, termite mounds, wrecks, oil drums, burned-out cars, game trails.\n234\t\n235\t**Day and night.** `setDaytime(w, { hour, rate })` on `sky:daylight`: a day lasts `game.day.minutes` (24). Start at 17:00.\n236\tSleeping skips to dawn, noon or dusk. Lamps with `lightsAtDusk`. AI sight is ×0.6 at night. A rain front arrives about once a\n237\tday for 90 s (GPU rain emitter, wet fuel: no spread) and is forecast by thunder and darkening.\n238\t\n239\t## 6. Core systems (all sim-side unless noted)\n240\t\n241\t### 6.1 Player\n242\t\n243\t`movement:merc`: start from `movement:apex` (`node x describe movement`) and make it heavier: run 4.2, sprint 6.4,\n244\tcrouch 2.0, jump 1.0 m, mantle on, wall-climb and superglide off, shorter slide, `holstered` ×1.05. Fall damage from landing\n245\tspeed. In tall grass: −10% speed and a rustle sound.\n246\t\n247\t### 6.2 Guns (`arms.ts`)\n248\t\n249\tA system for every actor with `weapons`: draw, sights, fire, reload, recoil, per `engine/sim/weapons.ts`, driven by\n250\t`seat.wants` for players and AI wants for NPCs. Shots leave the eye (1.52 m standing, 0.81 m crouched). Extra state in a component `gunState`, per slot: `condition` 0–1, `jammed`.\n251\tThree `defineWeapon` ids per gun (`-new`, `-worn`, `-rusted`, same stats, different prop tint); swap the slot's id at\n252\tcondition 0.66 and 0.33, so the gun's look shows its state.\n253\t\n254\t- **Wear:** each shot `condition -= game.wear.perShot × weapon.wear`. Dust storms and fire ×2.\n255\t- **Jam:** per shot, `p = game.wear.jamK × max(0, 0.65 − condition)²  × weapon.jamRate`. Jam: dry click, gun won't fire,\n256\t  prompt shows. Clearing: **hold** reload 0.9 s (with a 1-in-3 chance of needing it twice); the gun dips and racks, with a `jam` sound.\n257\t- **Break:** below 0.08, each shot has a 2% chance the gun comes apart: it drops, you take 8 damage.\n258\t- **Sources:** dealer guns start at 1.0; enemy guns drop at 0.15–0.5; an armoury crate reissues an owned gun at 1.0.\n259\t- **Slots:** Sidearm, Primary, Special, plus machete (always), syrettes and throwables. Ammo per class, modest.\n260\t- **Melee:** machete drawn as a `weapon` with `prop`; a chop is a fan of rays (`fanHits`), one hit, big damage, kick plus a\n261\t  camera roll.\n262\t- **Hits:** raycast; head (hit y above eye level −0.1) ×2.5, limbs ×0.7. NPC guns use the same system with a wider cone\n263\t  (`game.ai.accuracy`).\n264\t- **Fire guns:** flare pistol (ballistic flare; ignites the cell it lands in), molotov (thrown arc, ignites a 3-cell blob),\n265\t  sprayer (crop-sprayer flamethrower: short cone, ignites along it, ammo is fuel). Rocket launcher and frag use\n266\t  projectiles with blast `overlap`, `knock`, falloff damage and ignition.\n267\t\n268\t### 6.3 Health (`health.ts`)\n269\t\n270\t100 HP in 5 segments. Regen 6 HP/s to the top of the current segment after 4 s out of damage. Syrette (L1 / H, 0.9 s, the\n271\t`action:syrette`): to full; carry 3, max 5 (upgrades 7). **Critical** at ≤ 20 HP: the syrette press becomes **field surgery**\n272\t(2.6 s, interruptible, heals to 60 HP, uses no syrette): one of three body-camera actions in random order: dig the bullet out of the\n273\tforearm, set a dislocated finger, cauterize with a lighter (§10.2). Screen edge pulses and heartbeat on critical. Damage\n274\tdirection arcs on the HUD.\n275\t\n276\t**Down at 0 HP.** Story: if a buddy can come (alive, debt < 3, not on a contract elsewhere) you go down (low camera, drained\n277\tcolour, your sidearm still fires, 25 s); the buddy runs in from cover 40 m off, fights, then `action:rescue` pair (drag and\n278\tsyrette). You wake at 40 HP, debt +1, and a line from the buddy (\"That is two you owe me. I write them down.\"). Otherwise\n279\tblack, a note (\"Reserve not met.\"), reload from last save. Co-op: teammates revive (hold use 3 s); bleed-out 40 s.\n280\t\n281\t### 6.4 Fever (`fever.ts`)\n282\t\n283\tScripted first attack in the prologue. Then every `game.fever.intervalMin` (11) ± 3 minutes. Warning, 20 s: heartbeat, slight\n284\tvignette. Attack: `look:fever` amount rises (colour bleed, lens wobble, chroma, darkened edges), aim sway grows, move speed\n285\t×0.7. Take a pill (D-pad left / P, 1.2 s) to end it. With no pill: at 60 s you collapse, as for Down. Strong attacks (past 30 s) spawn\n286\t1–3 **mirages**: silent grey figures of dead buddies or soldiers you killed, standing in the grass, flagged so AI ignores them,\n287\tgone when shot at or within 8 m. Pills start at 4, max 8, come only from the Mission's contracts and crates. A `Fever\n288\tintensity` accessibility setting scales the screen effects, not the rules.\n289\t\n290\t### 6.5 Fire and wind (`fire.ts`, `wind.ts`): the star\n291\t\n292\t**Grid.** 8 m cells, 192 × 192. Per cell: fuel type, state (0 none, 1 unburnt, 2 burning, 3 burnt), timer, and regrow timer.\n293\tFuel comes from scatter, places and roads at setup. Keep arrays in one component; iterate burning cells in index order; draw\n294\tonly from `w.rng('fire')`. Update every 15 steps (4 Hz).\n295\t\n296\t| Fuel | Spread chance per tick (base) | Burns (s) | Notes |\n297\t|---|---|---|---|\n298\t| Dry grass (north) | 0.10 | 8 | Removes grass patches, leaves scorch props |\n299\t| Green grass (south) | 0.04 | 8 | |\n300\t| Brush | 0.07 | 14 | |\n301\t| Tree | 0.03 | 40 | Becomes a charred tree prop. Throws embers |\n302\t| Building, barn, racks | 0.05 | 60 | Roof and walls swap to charred props |\n303\t| Road, salt, water, bare earth | 0 | – | Firebreak |\n304\t\n305\t**Spread.** For each of 8 neighbours with unburnt fuel: `p = base × game.fire.spread × (1 + game.fire.windBias × (wind/5) ×\n306\tcos(angle to wind))`, floored at `0.15 × base`, × 1.4 uphill, × 0 in rain. **Embers:** a burning tree in wind ≥ 8 m/s has a 1% per\n307\ttick chance to ignite a cell 2–5 cells downwind, which jumps roads. **Target (a test):** on dry grass with 5 m/s wind a fire front runs\n308\t≥ 60 m downwind in 30 s and ≤ 25 m upwind. Slower than a sprint, faster than a crouch.\n309\t\n310\t**Effects.** Actors within 4 m of a burning cell take `game.fire.damage` (14 HP/s) and may catch: burning NPCs panic, run,\n311\tand die (ragdoll with fire emitter); burning players have a fast drain until they leave fuel. Oil drums, tanks and ammo crates have heat:\n312\tdrums explode, crates cook off in random pops. Vehicles take damage, and a fuel tank explodes. Burning and fresh-burnt cells count as\n313\tsmoke: AI sight rays crossing 2 or more smoke cells fail. Animals flee downwind-perpendicular. Burnt grass offers no concealment. After\n314\t`game.fire.regrow` (18) game-minutes scars regrow as green stubble with half fuel.\n315\t\n316\t**Drawing (page).** A burning cell spawns `prop:flame-patch` (parts with `flame.tongues`, an orange light spot on a few) and\n317\tremoves it when done; the 32 nearest clusters run smoke and ember emitters with `frame.emit`, picking the variant for the\n318\twind's compass direction (emitter `velocity` is fixed data, so define 8 directions); ash falls near big fires. Scars are small dark\n319\t`prop:scorch` patches tilted to the terrain normal. Fire crackle is positional. Light spots follow the engine's fixed\n320\tlight pool.\n321\t\n322\t**Wind.** A `wind` component: direction, speed (base `game.wind.speed` 5 m/s, gusts ±2). Every `game.wind.shiftMinutes` (4)\n323\tit swings ±30–110° over 20 s, chosen in advance. **Forecast:** 30 s before a shift, a HUD ribbon flutters and dust devils appear\n324\ton the new heading; flags at places and dust always show the current wind. The ribbon is shown while a fire weapon is out\n325\tor while the map is up.\n326\t\n327\t### 6.6 Stealth and AI (`ai/`)\n328\t\n329\t- **Activation.** Squads within 350 m have actors; the rest are data. Cap about 60 live NPCs.\n330\t- **Perception.** `sense` per NPC every 6 steps, staggered by id. Sight `game.ai.sight` (70 m) in a 120° cone, ×0.35 when\n331\t  you're crouched in unburnt tall grass, ×0.8 standing in it, ×0.6 at night, then a `clearSight` ray and the smoke test. Noise radii: sprint 18,\n332\t  walk 8, crouch 3, gunshot 120, suppressed 25, vehicle 60, explosion 250. A detection meter (0–1) rises by proximity at\n333\t  `1/game.ai.reaction`; HUD shows a subtle arc toward a watcher only above 0.5.\n334\t- **States.** Patrol → Suspicious (walks to the noise, barks) → Combat → Search → back. Plus Panic (fire) and Wounded.\n335\t- **Combat.** Squad blackboard shares your last known position. `game.ai.attackers` tokens (4) cap shooters at once. Roles: Assault\n336\t  flanks through `approachRing` and `createSiteNav().direction`; Suppressor holds cover and fires bursts; Officer calls and\n337\t  tosses frags. Cover from a per-place list of points. They keep their guns' wear rules, and a jammed NPC swears and clears it (a real\n338\t  window for you).\n339\t- **Wounded.** Below 25% HP, 30% fall and crawl (library clip `mesh2motion/Crawl`) calling out; a squadmate may drag them\n340\t  (`action:drag` pair). Finish them or leave them; they bleed out.\n341\t- **Checkpoints.** Guards shoot on sight **unless** your gun is holstered and your standing with that faction ≥ +1: then they\n342\t  shout, you get 6 s to pass at walking speed, and drawing a gun breaks it. Cleared posts repopulate after\n343\t  `game.ai.respawnHours` (6) game hours when you're over 300 m away. Claimed safehouses don't.\n344\t- **Patrols.** Technicals drive roads; on alert they chase and their gunner fires; passengers dismount when stopped.\n345\t- **Types:** Rifleman, Officer, Sniper (towers), Gunner (technical), Rocketeer, Flamer (Front only). Outfits by faction.\n346\t- **Wildlife and people.** Herds of 8–12 gazelles (`quadruped` crowd rig, custom body) graze and bolt from shots and fire.\n347\t  Vultures circle old fights if you have time. Townsfolk and refugees on `followRoute`.\n348\t\n349\t### 6.7 Vehicles (`vehicles.ts`). Verified recipe\n350\t\n351\tA **dynamic body in group `flyer`** (`flyer` touches only world and other flyers, so seated capsules don't fight it, while shots\n352\tstill hit it): box 1.8 × 1.0 × 3.9 m, density 220 (mass ≈ 1,544 kg), `linearDamping:0.02, angularDamping:0.6, canSleep:false`. System in\n353\tphase `ai`. For each of 4 wheel points (±0.85, −0.2, ±1.35): cast a ray down the car's up axis, `maxDistance` 0.75, groups\n354\t`world, prop`, excluding itself. If hit, with compression `c = 1 − dist/0.75`:\n355\t\n356\t- suspension `F = max(0, 42000 × c × 0.75 − 5200 × (point velocity · up))`;\n357\t- lateral grip `−side × (1400/4) × 2.2 / 0.35`, drive `throttle × 7800 / 4`, both clamped to ±`F × 1.1`; front wheels turn by\n358\t  `steer × 0.5` rad;\n359\t- `physics.applyImpulse(body, (up×F + right×lat + fwd×drive) × dt, point)`.\n360\t\n361\tVerified: tops out near 25–30 m/s, crosses rolling terrain stably at 0.32 ms a step, and replays to an identical hash. Tune the feel\n362\tby sliders (`game.car.*`).\n363\t\n364\t- **Seating:** in phase `rules` each step, `placeActor(w, driver, seatPoint)` with the seat's feet about 0.3 m below the\n365\t  chassis centre (verified: the driver follows the car over 40 s). It throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` under a low level roof: catch\n366\t  it and eject the driver.\n367\t- **People on foot vs cars** (not verified; test it): a `flyer` chassis doesn't block actors, so an unoccupied car also holds a\n368\t  **blocker**, a kinematic body in group `crowd` moved to the chassis each step. Remove it while anyone is seated. Map shots\n369\t  on it to the vehicle. Hit people by `overlap` ahead of the bumper: damage by speed, then `handOff` to ragdoll.\n370\t- **Drawing:** chassis prop with `body:'none'`, writing its `sceneProp` `x, y, z, q` each step from the body. The view reads those\n371\t  fields and interpolates them, body or no body. Four wheel props and a steering-wheel prop are written the same way (spin,\n372\t  steer, suspension).\n373\t- **Driver view:** custom `cam3=driver` (`defineCamera`; §10.2), body drawn sitting (`action:drive`, hands on the wheel, `until:'next'`).\n374\t  `cameraInput` gives look; a view button toggles chase.\n375\t- **Damage:** HP 300. Under 40%: engine smoke, power ×0.6. Under 15%: flames, then explode after 10 s. **Repair:** stop, stand at\n376\t  the bonnet, hold use 3 s (`action:repair`, wrench sounds) back to 60%; a repair kit restores 100%.\n377\t- **Types:** open jeep; pickup technical with rear mounted MG (seat; `look` drives the mount, overheats, never jams); cargo truck\n378\t  (convoys, AI only); patrol boat (same body with buoyancy springs at `waterY` instead of rays, thrust at the stern, a bow MG).\n379\t- **Other rides:** Mine ropeway with `addZipline`. Rides live in the movement model, so they work for any seat whose wants hold\n380\t  `interact`; keep usables away from cable ends so one press means one thing. Ladders likewise.\n381\t\n382\t### 6.8 Buddies and the ledger (`buddies.ts`)\n383\t\n384\tThe three mercs you didn't pick (§8.3) live at places, each `defineBody` unique. **Debt** per buddy, an integer from −3 to +3 in a\n385\tLedger screen (\"You owe Ilse 2.\"). Rescue: +1 owed. Helping them or finishing their alternate plan: −1. At +3 they stop coming (\"You're\n386\toverdrawn.\"). **Alternate plans:** before a contract, visit a buddy for a better way to do it: extra objectives and pay, and they join\n387\tyou (NPC with `seat`-free AI). **When a buddy falls** (scripted once in Contract 5, and possibly anywhere they fight): they lie down\n388\tcalling you, with 60 s. Choose: syrette (hold use; costs one; saves them, debt −1), or **mercy** (the prompt appears with a sidearm out;\n389\tone shot; the cast comment forever), or leave them. Death is permanent and saved, and changes later lines and the ending's\n390\tlast word.\n391\t\n392\t### 6.9 Economy (`economy.ts`)\n393\t\n394\t**Rough stones.** Contract pay 15–30. **Tin boxes** (8; 5–10 stones each) hidden in wrecks and mounds; the tick-box (D-pad down / B) clicks\n395\tfaster inside 120 m and its lamp holds under 15 m; a mirrored lamp pulses on the map layer. **Ferreira's catalogue**, one item on screen at a time:\n396\tguns (unlocked at armoury crates), Reliability I/II (wear ×0.7/×0.5), syrette capacity, repair kit, camouflage smock (concealment +20%).\n397\tPrices 5–40. **Armoury crates** at safehouses reissue what you own, at full condition. Faction **standing**, one integer per side, changes\n398\tcontract wording, checkpoint behaviour (§6.6) and dealer rumours.\n399\t\n400\t### 6.10 Story engine (`contracts/`)\n401\t\n402\t`def('contract', id, spec)` with a schema. Steps are data; hooks are rare. Sim holds `story` flags and the active step; page shows goal text.\n403\t\n404\t```ts\n405\tdef('contract', 'contract:receipts', {\n406\t  giver: 'cassius', faction: 'front', pay: 15, standing: { front: 1, authority: -1 },\n407\t  brief: 'text:receipts-brief',\n408\t  steps: [\n409\t    { id: 'go', goal: 'Reach the Km-40 post', at: 'km40', radius: 40 },\n410\t    { id: 'take', goal: 'Take the ledger from the radio hut', use: 'ledger-km40' },\n411\t    { id: 'back', goal: 'Bring it to Brother Cassius', talk: 'cassius' },\n412\t  ],\n413\t  alts: [{ buddy: 'yaw', pitch: 'text:receipts-alt', adds: [{ id: 'radio', goal: 'Burn the radio hut', burn: 'km40-hut' }], pay: 8, debt: -1 }],\n414\t});\n415\t```\n416\t\n417\tStep kinds: `at`, `use`, `talk`, `kill`, `burn`, `carry`, `survive`, `escort`, `choice`. Lines run by event (`w.emit('say', { who, text })`), and\n418\tchoices return through a custom intent (`'game:pick'`), so replays and co-op hold them.\n419\t\n420\t### 6.11 Other world rules"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"18e2a4de-e9b2-46fd-9b76-d10abfe06908","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:29:37.693Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN: an open-world first-person mercenary game in a burning country\n\nInspired by Far Cry 2. Original world, cast, story, art and music. You build it from this plan and your TASK.md,\nwithout the plan's author. Paths are relative to your dev folder. \"The deliverable\" means the `.html` your TASK.md\nnames, in the folder above the dev folder (`..`); \"the exit-interview file\" is the JSON file your TASK.md names, beside it.\n\n## 0. How to use this plan\n\n- **The design is decided.** Build it; don't reopen it. Every number is a starting value and most are dev sliders:\n  tune by playtest scripts. Where you must deviate, do the simplest thing that keeps the feature, and write the call in\n  `labs/game/README.md`.\n- **\"Verified\"** means the plan's author ran it on this machine on 2026-11-04, on engine commit `e7a1243` and hub client\n  1.4.0, with throwaway probes. If a verified recipe fails for you, look for what changed; don't redesign around it.\n- **Your TASK.md wins** over this plan on anything it states. §15 maps each TASK.md requirement to the section here.\n- **Features beat content.** No feature on the never-cut list may be stubbed. If you run short, shrink content, never\n  below the floors:\n\n| Never cut | May shrink, never below |\n|---|---|\n| Gun wear, jams and clearing; wounds, syrettes and field surgery; fire with wind; fever and pills; buddies with rescue, debt and mercy; drivable vehicles with repair; map in hand; two factions' contracts and an ending; stones, locator and dealer; safehouses and saves; stealth in grass; day and night; dev mode with sliders; attract mode; hub session passing the harness; co-op on its own; touch notice; About/Credits; code-only audio with gibberish voices | Places: 7 (town + 6). Contracts: prologue + 5. Weapons: 8. Tapes: 4. Stone caches: 5. Buddies: 3. Enemy types: 4. Vehicles: pickup + boat. Songs: 3 |\n\n## 1. The game\n\n**Pitch.** You come up the river at the end of the dry season to serve a warrant on the Auctioneer, the arms dealer who\nkeeps a civil war solvent by selling to both sides. You have a fever, a rusting rifle, debts to people who may or may not\ndrag you out of the next fire, and a wind that is the only honest thing in the country.\n\n**Genre:** open-world first-person shooter with systemic fire and survival pressure. **Perspective:** first person, with\nan over-the-shoulder option in Settings, a chase option while driving, and short eye-level \"body camera\" moments (§10.2).\n\n**Pillars**\n\n1. **Everything wears out.** Guns, vehicles, your body, your friends. Reliability is the real economy.\n2. **Fire is your best weapon and you don't control it.** Wind decides. Burn scars stay and change the map.\n3. **No clean hands.** Two factions, no good side, debts kept in a ledger. The writing never winks.\n4. **The body is the interface.** Map in the hands, pills from the bottle, a bullet dug out of the arm, a wrench on the\n   engine, all in real time. Only the pause menu stops the world.\n5. **The land is the antagonist.** Long sightlines, chest-high grass, checkpoints on every road, heat haze.\n\n**What we take from the source, and what we make of it.** Mechanics are fair game; names, characters, places, story\nbeats, art and music are not.\n\n| Source's idea | This game's version |\n|---|---|\n| Fire spreads with the wind | Same verb, deeper: a forecastable wind, ember spotting, fuel types, firebreaks, smoke that blinds AI, scars that strip stealth cover and regrow |\n| Guns degrade and jam | Same, and condition shows on the gun in three rust tiers; enemy guns are junk; reliability upgrades at the dealer |\n| Malaria and pills | Blackwater fever and quinine; attacks can show harmless mirages of people you failed |\n| Buddies rescue you | A **ledger of debts**: each rescue is owed, and overdrawn buddies stop coming; mercy or a syrette when they fall |\n| Map held in the hands | Paper map and tick-box locator on a diegetic CSS layer; you can walk or drive with it up |\n| Diamonds | Rough stones in dead prospectors' tin boxes, found by a Geiger-style tick-box |\n| Arms dealer villain with tapes | The **Auctioneer**: cassette \"lots\" in the patter of a sale. Every contract you do adds to his catalogue |\n| Two rotten factions, ceasefire town | The Provisional Authority and the Basin Front; ceasefire in Sainte-Aurore |\n\n**Original-work rules.** Use nothing named or written in the source: no character, faction, place or mission names, no\ntaxi or hotel opening, no tapes of a villain quoting philosophers, no music, logos or screens that copy it.\nThe title is the one riff on the source's name, as TASK.md asks; everything else stands alone. Don't call the game a\nsequel. Portray the invented country's people as people: named characters on every side, with no real nation, ethnic\ngroup or leader named or caricatured.\n\n## 2. Setup and verified ground truth\n\nRun from the empty dev folder:\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p .cache && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge .cache/engine-src   # stays: the engine's examples, to read\nnode .cache/engine-src/tools/game/new-game.mjs . --name <slug> && rm -rf .cache/engine-src/.git\nnpm ci --no-audit --no-fund                     # 6 s. Do NOT run scripts/setup.sh: it downloads Node and Chrome outside your folder\nexport CHROMIUM_PATH=$(ls ~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-*/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell | head -1)\nnpm test && npm run check && node x shot labs/game   # all green on the starter (verified)\n```\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` and `docs/GAME-GUIDE.md` once. **`labs/playground/` is not in a game's workspace**, but it is the best\nworked example of nearly everything here (first person, guns, bodies, doors, sites, neighbours, looks, front end, attract\nmode, sound): read it at `.cache/engine-src/labs/playground/` as needed. Grep `docs/API.md`; don't read it whole.\n\nVerified facts that will save you hours:\n\n- **Browser flags.** TASK.md's listed flags (`--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan\n  --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`) alone **fail with this engine** (\"Instance dropped in popErrorScope\", never ready).\n  Use `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. Adding\n  `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader` is harmless. With these the starter is `ready` in 3.6 s from `file://`.\n- **Headless shell only.** Playwright's default headless works. Full Chromium dies here with \"Socket path too long\"\n  because run paths are long, so skip headed mode and xvfb.\n- **`CHROMIUM_PATH`** (above) makes `node x shot`, `x film`, `x inspect` and `x replay --browser` work. Node 24.22.1 is\n  fine. In Node drivers: `chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, args })` from `@playwright/test`.\n- **Ports.** `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` piped to a script never prints its port (buffered): use\n  `python3 -u`, or Node's `http` on port 0. Confirm the page's marker before trusting a result. Stop only your own PID.\n- **What the checks scan.** `npm run check` fails on any PNG or base64 blob under the dev folder, except in git-ignored\n  places: `out/` and `.cache/` are skipped by ESLint, Prettier, the asset scan and Vitest. Screenshots and temp bundles go\n  in `out/`, hub files in `.cache/hub/`, the deliverable outside the dev folder.\n- **Git.** The dev folder sits inside a larger repository that isn't yours. Make no commits there; `git init` inside the\n  dev folder if you want history.\n- **Sim costs on this machine.** A 1536 m terrain at 4 m cells adds 0.35 ms a step. An actor costs about 0.15 ms. A prop\n  with **no** body costs about nothing a step. A prop with **its own body** costs about 1.2 µs a step (3,000 trees 3.9 ms),\n  so trees are `body:'none'` props plus **one** fixed body holding all their colliders (verified). A site of 40 buildings\n  on that terrain starts in 1.1 s and steps 24 actors in 1.8 ms.\n- **`capture()` is 35–80 MB of JSON** at this scale. Never use it for saves or network resync.\n\n## 3. The engine: what to use and the walls\n\n| Need | Use | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| World | `defineTerrain`, `defineLevel` (format 2 storeys), `defineSite`, scene `site:`, `addSiteBodies`, `createSiteNav` | The scene must name `site:` or `terrain:`, or the ground isn't drawn |\n| Player feel | `defineMovement('movement:merc', …)` from apex (§6.1), `createCharacter`, `spawnActor`, settings `movement.*` | |\n| Drawing things | `defineProp` + `spawnProp`, `defineMaterial`, `defineTexture`, `defineGeometry`, `defineBody` | Props are instanced and interpolated |\n| Effects | `defineEmitter`, `frame.emit(id, at, key, scale)` in `onFrame`, sim events that burst emitters, `gpu: true` emitters, flame tongues on prop parts | Budget 4,096 CPU particles; use GPU emitters for smoke and fire |\n| Look | `defineLook` (`sky:'sky:daylight'`, filters), `setDaytime`, `post.combine` set live | Numbers and amounts change without a shader build |\n| Guns | `defineWeapon`, the `weapons` component (`weaponsFor`), `recoilStep`, `spreadOf`, `gunshot` events | Engine draws gun, sights, kick, tracers, flashes, holes |\n| People | `spawnActor({ player:false })` with `actor.intents`, `sense`/`canSee`, `takeToken`, `damage`, `reactTo`, `addRagdolls`/`handOff`, `followRoute`, `stepAside` | See `labs/playground/cast/neighbours.ts` |\n| Animals, refugees | Crowd bodies (`addAgent`, `crowdBody`, rig `quadruped`) | |\n| Body animation | `defineAction` + `actOn` (call it after step 1, not in `setup`: verified), library clips (`node x anim find crawl`) | Credit imported clips per `data/anim/SOURCES.md` |\n| Sound | `defineSfx`, `defineSong`, `createAudio` (`volume`, `music`, `intensity`, `stinger`, `play({position, bus})`, `footstep`) | `audio.context` is exposed |\n| UI | `engine.ui.root` + plain HTML/CSS, `createMenu`, `createDialog`, `createBar`, `createPadCursor`, `createStore`, `createEngine({ modal, store })` | `createMenu` already does pad, keys, hover-moves-focus, click |\n| Data as a tool | `defineKind`/`def` for contracts, places, squads, dealer stock | `node x describe contract` then lists them for designers |\n| New entries | `node x new <kind> labs/game/<dir>/<name>` | Writes module + test |\n\n**Five walls. Plan around them; don't fight them.**\n\n1. **No access to the three.js scene.** Game code may import only `engine/index.ts` and `engine/sim-api.ts` (lint). Everything\n   in the world is a prop, terrain, site, body, emitter, sky or look; everything else is the HTML overlay. For arbitrary\n   meshes (grass, road ribbons, canopies), `defineGeometry` can return raw buffers by borrowing classes off a kit shape\n   (verified, with a 36-blade grass tuft):\n\n   ```ts\n   const g = boxGeometry({ width: 1, height: 1, depth: 1 });\n   const Attr = g.getAttribute('position').constructor as new (a: Float32Array, n: number) => never;\n   g.setAttribute('position', new Attr(new Float32Array(pos), 3)); // also 'normal' and 'uv'\n   g.setIndex(indices); g.clearGroups(); return g; // set `budget` to its vertex count\n   ```\n   Give blades real normals (up-ish, both faces lit) and `side:'double'` in the material, or half of them draw black.\n2. **`addWeapons`, `addMelee` and `addInteraction` only serve `actor.player === true`**, reading the step's one set of\n   intents. They can't drive NPCs or other seats, and calling them breaks lockstep. **Don't call them.** Write `arms` (§6.2)\n   and `use` (§6.12) systems that keep writing the same `weapons` component and emit `gunshot` with the same payload\n   (`{ id, weapon, from, to, normal, body, target, hit }`), and set `motion.holstered` and `animator.weapon` as\n   `engine/sim/weapons.ts` does. Then the engine draws guns, sights and tracers for players and NPCs alike. Read that file\n   and copy its timing logic. `useDoor`, `strikeDoor`, `damage`, `entityOfBody`, `strikeEntity` are callable directly.\n3. **First-person arms are a closed rig.** Games can't pose them, and reloads aren't animated at all. Fakes: lower the gun\n   for a reload by setting `weapons.slot = -1` for the middle of the reload with `motion.holstered` kept false (film it to\n   check); kick by `shots`; big moments use the body camera (§10.2). Full-body actions always show in shoulder view and\n   to other players.\n4. **Terrain paint is slope and height only.** Roads are draped ribbon props. Burn scars are props. Biomes are scatter.\n5. **A running page can't switch scenes.** One scene, `game:world`, with a setting `game.mode`\n   (`title | story | attract | contract`); change it with `__engine.set`, then restart with `inspector.seed(n)`.\n\nTexture generators write `texel.color` in **sRGB bytes 0–255**, not 0–1 (verified; 0–1 draws black).\n\n## 4. Architecture\n\n```\nlabs/game/\n  index.html  main.ts          page entry: reads mode, starts engine, wires everything (keep small)\n  title.ts                     the game's title, one constant\n  scenes/                      SIM-SIDE: imports only engine/sim-api.ts (lint enforces scenes/** and cast/**)\n    world.ts                   defineScene('game:world'), setup order, modes\n    settings.ts                every tunable in one table: path, default, min, max, label, group\n    map.ts roads.ts scatter.ts terrain + site + places, road polylines, deterministic scatter\n    seats.ts arms.ts use.ts health.ts fever.ts fire.ts wind.ts vehicles.ts buddies.ts economy.ts story.ts save.ts digest.ts\n    ai/ perception.ts squads.ts soldier.ts driver.ts wildlife.ts\n    contracts/ *.ts            contracts as data; the engine that runs them\n    text/ *.ts                 every line of dialogue, briefing and tape, as data\n  cast/                        SIM-SIDE: spawn player, soldiers, buddies, civilians, animals; actions\n  props/ weapons/              SIM-SIDE defineProp, defineWeapon (sim-api exports them)\n  art/                         PAGE: textures, materials, geometry, bodies, emitters, looks, cameras\n  sounds/                      PAGE: sfx, songs, voice synth, event-to-sound map\n  ui/                          PAGE: hud, prompts, glyphs, title, pause, settings, map, ledger, dialogue, shop, dev, about, card, touch\n  net/                         PAGE: net.ts (interface), hub.ts, tabs.ts, rtc.ts, lockstep.ts, wire.ts\n  bot.ts attract.ts            bot intents shared by tests and attract mode\n  replays/                     one short golden replay\ntests/game/                    browser and harness drivers (.mjs), verify.mjs\nscripts/                       bundle.mjs, fetch-hub.mjs\n```\n\nRules from the engine that apply everywhere: sim code uses no clock, `Math.random`, DOM or storage; time in whole steps;\nrandomness from `w.rng('name')`; state in components; `Math.pow`, not `**`; every file opens with an `@file` comment, warns\npast 400 lines and fails past 600. Presentation reads the sim and never writes it.\n\n**Seats: one path for every player from day one.** Every human-controlled actor has a `seat` component. The first system\nin phase `intents` (`game.seats`) builds `seat.wants = { move, look, aim, b, p }` for each seat: for the actor with\n`actor.player === true` from the step's intents, for the others from the step's custom key `'game:seats'[n]`, which it\nalso copies to `actor.intents`. It computes `p` itself as the edges of `b` against last step, plus any `p` given. **All\ngame systems read `seat.wants`, never the raw intents.** NPCs have no seat. In solo play there is one seat. Sim settings\nthat fork behaviour by `actor.player` (`input.sprint`, `input.crouch`) stay at defaults in co-op.\n\n**Saves are game data, not captures.** `save.ts` writes plain JSON (seat position, inventory, condition, stones, flags,\nbuddies, hour, wind, burn map as run-length text, cleared places) to `createStore` at sleep and at contract steps. Load\nrestarts the scene and applies it through the dev action `load`. A session gets the hub's empty storage and saves nothing.\n\n**Data-driven so designers can extend it:** places, squads, contracts, dealer stock and weapons are registry kinds or\ntables with schemas. Adding a contract or a checkpoint takes no new code.\n\n## 5. The world\n\n**Map.** A 1536 × 1536 m site, 4 m cells (`size:[1536,1536], cell:4`; `size` is metres), x east, z south. A ring of hills\n70–120 m high (`hills` round the edge, plus a sim rule that turns back anything past 1450 m from centre) keeps you in;\nthe terrain ends at the edge, and a vehicle will fall off it (verified), so the rule must hold. Rolling ground: `height:14,\nscale:180, octaves:5, ridges:0.3`. Materials: ground `material:savanna` (straw over red earth), steep `material:laterite`,\nhigh `material:ironstone` from 45 m up. Every place sits on `flats`.\n\n**The river** crosses west to east near z≈900 as a chain of negative `hills` (depth ≤ 1.2 m below `waterY`), drawn as one\nflat water prop at `waterY` with `texture:water`. No swimming: you wade at half speed. Vehicles stall past 0.8 m, except\nfords. North of it is dry savanna; south is greener riverine woodland that burns slower (fuel table, §6.5).\n\n**Places** (coordinates are the centre; adjust to fit the terrain, keep the relations):\n\n| Place | At (x, z) | What it's for |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Sainte-Aurore**, ceasefire town | 760, 790 | Weapons forced holstered. Hotel Splendide (bar, Yaw), Customs House (Authority), Cinema Rex (Front), jetty. 12 buildings, townsfolk on routes |\n| **Km-40 checkpoint** | 620, 520 | First firefight. Boom gate, sandbags, watchtower, radio hut |\n| **Bridge Post checkpoint** | 1010, 790 | East road; a technical parks here |\n| **Ford Post checkpoint** | 560, 985 | South crossing |\n| **Pump Station** | 1010, 360 | Pipeline, fuel tanks, explosive set piece; co-op's arena |\n| **Salt Works** | 1240, 260 | White pans (no fuel: a natural firebreak), conveyors, wide-open fight; buddy rescue |\n| **Mine No. 6** | 300, 300 | Red pit in iron hills, rail cars, aerial ropeway (`addZipline`); the finale |\n| **Belvédère Estate** | 1130, 1180 | Tobacco barns, drying racks, the big burn |\n| **Mission Sainte-Claire** | 330, 1120 | Clinic, refugees on routes, Sister Perpetua, pills |\n| **Airstrip** | 1200, 620 | Ferreira's container (dealer), hangar safehouse, wrecked plane |\n| **Broken rail bridge** | 880, 905 | Landmark and ambush spot |\n| **Safehouses** | Water Tower 470, 650; Ferry Shed 640, 1040; Hangar 1240, 640 | Clear the guards to claim each |\n| **Barge wreck** | 300, 900 | Prologue start |\n\n**Roads** are polylines in `roads.ts` joining all of the above (one main east–west road through town, north road to Km-40\nthen Mine, east road to Bridge Post and Airstrip, south road over the ford to Mission and Estate). The same data draws the\ndraped ribbon props, gives footstep surface and fire-free cells, and steers AI drivers. A pipeline and a power line on\npoles run across the savanna as long-distance landmarks.\n\n**Scatter** is deterministic (`scatterTerrain` with `salt`, or your own by road and place distance):\n\n- About 1,200 trees: 3 flat-topped thorn trees, a fat bottle tree, thorn bushes. `body:'none'` plus one fixed body of\n  capsule colliders.\n- Grass as **patches**: a prop per 16 m square of fuel, 200–400 raw-geometry blades, knee to chest high, about 6,000 patches.\n  Removing one is how grass burns. A setting `game.detail` (0.1–1) thins scatter for tests and software adapters (read\n  `__engine.info().adapter.fallback`); default 1. TASK.md puts FPS out of scope, so don't hold back on real GPUs.\n- Rocks, termite mounds, wrecks, oil drums, burned-out cars, game trails.\n\n**Day and night.** `setDaytime(w, { hour, rate })` on `sky:daylight`: a day lasts `game.day.minutes` (24). Start at 17:00.\nSleeping skips to dawn, noon or dusk. Lamps with `lightsAtDusk`. AI sight is ×0.6 at night. A rain front arrives about once a\nday for 90 s (GPU rain emitter, wet fuel: no spread) and is forecast by thunder and darkening.\n\n## 6. Core systems (all sim-side unless noted)\n\n### 6.1 Player\n\n`movement:merc`: start from `movement:apex` (`node x describe movement`) and make it heavier: run 4.2, sprint 6.4,\ncrouch 2.0, jump 1.0 m, mantle on, wall-climb and superglide off, shorter slide, `holstered` ×1.05. Fall damage from landing\nspeed. In tall grass: −10% speed and a rustle sound.\n\n### 6.2 Guns (`arms.ts`)\n\nA system for every actor with `weapons`: draw, sights, fire, reload, recoil, per `engine/sim/weapons.ts`, driven by\n`seat.wants` for players and AI wants for NPCs. Shots leave the eye (1.52 m standing, 0.81 m crouched). Extra state in a component `gunState`, per slot: `condition` 0–1, `jammed`.\nThree `defineWeapon` ids per gun (`-new`, `-worn`, `-rusted`, same stats, different prop tint); swap the slot's id at\ncondition 0.66 and 0.33, so the gun's look shows its state.\n\n- **Wear:** each shot `condition -= game.wear.perShot × weapon.wear`. Dust storms and fire ×2.\n- **Jam:** per shot, `p = game.wear.jamK × max(0, 0.65 − condition)²  × weapon.jamRate`. Jam: dry click, gun won't fire,\n  prompt shows. Clearing: **hold** reload 0.9 s (with a 1-in-3 chance of needing it twice); the gun dips and racks, with a `jam` sound.\n- **Break:** below 0.08, each shot has a 2% chance the gun comes apart: it drops, you take 8 damage.\n- **Sources:** dealer guns start at 1.0; enemy guns drop at 0.15–0.5; an armoury crate reissues an owned gun at 1.0.\n- **Slots:** Sidearm, Primary, Special, plus machete (always), syrettes and throwables. Ammo per class, modest.\n- **Melee:** machete drawn as a `weapon` with `prop`; a chop is a fan of rays (`fanHits`), one hit, big damage, kick plus a\n  camera roll.\n- **Hits:** raycast; head (hit y above eye level −0.1) ×2.5, limbs ×0.7. NPC guns use the same system with a wider cone\n  (`game.ai.accuracy`).\n- **Fire guns:** flare pistol (ballistic flare; ignites the cell it lands in), molotov (thrown arc, ignites a 3-cell blob),\n  sprayer (crop-sprayer flamethrower: short cone, ignites along it, ammo is fuel). Rocket launcher and frag use\n  projectiles with blast `overlap`, `knock`, falloff damage and ignition.\n\n### 6.3 Health (`health.ts`)\n\n100 HP in 5 segments. Regen 6 HP/s to the top of the current segment after 4 s out of damage. Syrette (L1 / H, 0.9 s, the\n`action:syrette`): to full; carry 3, max 5 (upgrades 7). **Critical** at ≤ 20 HP: the syrette press becomes **field surgery**\n(2.6 s, interruptible, heals to 60 HP, uses no syrette): one of three body-camera actions in random order: dig the bullet out of the\nforearm, set a dislocated finger, cauterize with a lighter (§10.2). Screen edge pulses and heartbeat on critical. Damage\ndirection arcs on the HUD.\n\n**Down at 0 HP.** Story: if a buddy can come (alive, debt < 3, not on a contract elsewhere) you go down (low camera, drained\ncolour, your sidearm still fires, 25 s); the buddy runs in from cover 40 m off, fights, then `action:rescue` pair (drag and\nsyrette). You wake at 40 HP, debt +1, and a line from the buddy (\"That is two you owe me. I write them down.\"). Otherwise\nblack, a note (\"Reserve not met.\"), reload from last save. Co-op: teammates revive (hold use 3 s); bleed-out 40 s.\n\n### 6.4 Fever (`fever.ts`)\n\nScripted first attack in the prologue. Then every `game.fever.intervalMin` (11) ± 3 minutes. Warning, 20 s: heartbeat, slight\nvignette. Attack: `look:fever` amount rises (colour bleed, lens wobble, chroma, darkened edges), aim sway grows, move speed\n×0.7. Take a pill (D-pad left / P, 1.2 s) to end it. With no pill: at 60 s you collapse, as for Down. Strong attacks (past 30 s) spawn\n1–3 **mirages**: silent grey figures of dead buddies or soldiers you killed, standing in the grass, flagged so AI ignores them,\ngone when shot at or within 8 m. Pills start at 4, max 8, come only from the Mission's contracts and crates. A `Fever\nintensity` accessibility setting scales the screen effects, not the rules.\n\n### 6.5 Fire and wind (`fire.ts`, `wind.ts`): the star\n\n**Grid.** 8 m cells, 192 × 192. Per cell: fuel type, state (0 none, 1 unburnt, 2 burning, 3 burnt), timer, and regrow timer.\nFuel comes from scatter, places and roads at setup. Keep arrays in one component; iterate burning cells in index order; draw\nonly from `w.rng('fire')`. Update every 15 steps (4 Hz).\n\n| Fuel | Spread chance per tick (base) | Burns (s) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Dry grass (north) | 0.10 | 8 | Removes grass patches, leaves scorch props |\n| Green grass (south) | 0.04 | 8 | |\n| Brush | 0.07 | 14 | |\n| Tree | 0.03 | 40 | Becomes a charred tree prop. Throws embers |\n| Building, barn, racks | 0.05 | 60 | Roof and walls swap to charred props |\n| Road, salt, water, bare earth | 0 | – | Firebreak |\n\n**Spread.** For each of 8 neighbours with unburnt fuel: `p = base × game.fire.spread × (1 + game.fire.windBias × (wind/5) ×\ncos(angle to wind))`, floored at `0.15 × base`, × 1.4 uphill, × 0 in rain. **Embers:** a burning tree in wind ≥ 8 m/s has a 1% per\ntick chance to ignite a cell 2–5 cells downwind, which jumps roads. **Target (a test):** on dry grass with 5 m/s wind a fire front runs\n≥ 60 m downwind in 30 s and ≤ 25 m upwind. Slower than a sprint, faster than a crouch.\n\n**Effects.** Actors within 4 m of a burning cell take `game.fire.damage` (14 HP/s) and may catch: burning NPCs panic, run,\nand die (ragdoll with fire emitter); burning players have a fast drain until they leave fuel. Oil drums, tanks and ammo crates have heat:\ndrums explode, crates cook off in random pops. Vehicles take damage, and a fuel tank explodes. Burning and fresh-burnt cells count as\nsmoke: AI sight rays crossing 2 or more smoke cells fail. Animals flee downwind-perpendicular. Burnt grass offers no concealment. After\n`game.fire.regrow` (18) game-minutes scars regrow as green stubble with half fuel.\n\n**Drawing (page).** A burning cell spawns `prop:flame-patch` (parts with `flame.tongues`, an orange light spot on a few) and\nremoves it when done; the 32 nearest clusters run smoke and ember emitters with `frame.emit`, picking the variant for the\nwind's compass direction (emitter `velocity` is fixed data, so define 8 directions); ash falls near big fires. Scars are small dark\n`prop:scorch` patches tilted to the terrain normal. Fire crackle is positional. Light spots follow the engine's fixed\nlight pool.\n\n**Wind.** A `wind` component: direction, speed (base `game.wind.speed` 5 m/s, gusts ±2). Every `game.wind.shiftMinutes` (4)\nit swings ±30–110° over 20 s, chosen in advance. **Forecast:** 30 s before a shift, a HUD ribbon flutters and dust devils appear\non the new heading; flags at places and dust always show the current wind. The ribbon is shown while a fire weapon is out\nor while the map is up.\n\n### 6.6 Stealth and AI (`ai/`)\n\n- **Activation.** Squads within 350 m have actors; the rest are data. Cap about 60 live NPCs.\n- **Perception.** `sense` per NPC every 6 steps, staggered by id. Sight `game.ai.sight` (70 m) in a 120° cone, ×0.35 when\n  you're crouched in unburnt tall grass, ×0.8 standing in it, ×0.6 at night, then a `clearSight` ray and the smoke test. Noise radii: sprint 18,\n  walk 8, crouch 3, gunshot 120, suppressed 25, vehicle 60, explosion 250. A detection meter (0–1) rises by proximity at\n  `1/game.ai.reaction`; HUD shows a subtle arc toward a watcher only above 0.5.\n- **States.** Patrol → Suspicious (walks to the noise, barks) → Combat → Search → back. Plus Panic (fire) and Wounded.\n- **Combat.** Squad blackboard shares your last known position. `game.ai.attackers` tokens (4) cap shooters at once. Roles: Assault\n  flanks through `approachRing` and `createSiteNav().direction`; Suppressor holds cover and fires bursts; Officer calls and\n  tosses frags. Cover from a per-place list of points. They keep their guns' wear rules, and a jammed NPC swears and clears it (a real\n  window for you).\n- **Wounded.** Below 25% HP, 30% fall and crawl (library clip `mesh2motion/Crawl`) calling out; a squadmate may drag them\n  (`action:drag` pair). Finish them or leave them; they bleed out.\n- **Checkpoints.** Guards shoot on sight **unless** your gun is holstered and your standing with that faction ≥ +1: then they\n  shout, you get 6 s to pass at walking speed, and drawing a gun breaks it. Cleared posts repopulate after\n  `game.ai.respawnHours` (6) game hours when you're over 300 m away. Claimed safehouses don't.\n- **Patrols.** Technicals drive roads; on alert they chase and their gunner fires; passengers dismount when stopped.\n- **Types:** Rifleman, Officer, Sniper (towers), Gunner (technical), Rocketeer, Flamer (Front only). Outfits by faction.\n- **Wildlife and people.** Herds of 8–12 gazelles (`quadruped` crowd rig, custom body) graze and bolt from shots and fire.\n  Vultures circle old fights if you have time. Townsfolk and refugees on `followRoute`.\n\n### 6.7 Vehicles (`vehicles.ts`). Verified recipe\n\nA **dynamic body in group `flyer`** (`flyer` touches only world and other flyers, so seated capsules don't fight it, while shots\nstill hit it): box 1.8 × 1.0 × 3.9 m, density 220 (mass ≈ 1,544 kg), `linearDamping:0.02, angularDamping:0.6, canSleep:false`. System in\nphase `ai`. For each of 4 wheel points (±0.85, −0.2, ±1.35): cast a ray down the car's up axis, `maxDistance` 0.75, groups\n`world, prop`, excluding itself. If hit, with compression `c = 1 − dist/0.75`:\n\n- suspension `F = max(0, 42000 × c × 0.75 − 5200 × (point velocity · up))`;\n- lateral grip `−side × (1400/4) × 2.2 / 0.35`, drive `throttle × 7800 / 4`, both clamped to ±`F × 1.1`; front wheels turn by\n  `steer × 0.5` rad;\n- `physics.applyImpulse(body, (up×F + right×lat + fwd×drive) × dt, point)`.\n\nVerified: tops out near 25–30 m/s, crosses rolling terrain stably at 0.32 ms a step, and replays to an identical hash. Tune the feel\nby sliders (`game.car.*`).\n\n- **Seating:** in phase `rules` each step, `placeActor(w, driver, seatPoint)` with the seat's feet about 0.3 m below the\n  chassis centre (verified: the driver follows the car over 40 s). It throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` under a low level roof: catch\n  it and eject the driver.\n- **People on foot vs cars** (not verified; test it): a `flyer` chassis doesn't block actors, so an unoccupied car also holds a\n  **blocker**, a kinematic body in group `crowd` moved to the chassis each step. Remove it while anyone is seated. Map shots\n  on it to the vehicle. Hit people by `overlap` ahead of the bumper: damage by speed, then `handOff` to ragdoll.\n- **Drawing:** chassis prop with `body:'none'`, writing its `sceneProp` `x, y, z, q` each step from the body. The view reads those\n  fields and interpolates them, body or no body. Four wheel props and a steering-wheel prop are written the same way (spin,\n  steer, suspension).\n- **Driver view:** custom `cam3=driver` (`defineCamera`; §10.2), body drawn sitting (`action:drive`, hands on the wheel, `until:'next'`).\n  `cameraInput` gives look; a view button toggles chase.\n- **Damage:** HP 300. Under 40%: engine smoke, power ×0.6. Under 15%: flames, then explode after 10 s. **Repair:** stop, stand at\n  the bonnet, hold use 3 s (`action:repair`, wrench sounds) back to 60%; a repair kit restores 100%.\n- **Types:** open jeep; pickup technical with rear mounted MG (seat; `look` drives the mount, overheats, never jams); cargo truck\n  (convoys, AI only); patrol boat (same body with buoyancy springs at `waterY` instead of rays, thrust at the stern, a bow MG).\n- **Other rides:** Mine ropeway with `addZipline`. Rides live in the movement model, so they work for any seat whose wants hold\n  `interact`; keep usables away from cable ends so one press means one thing. Ladders likewise.\n\n### 6.8 Buddies and the ledger (`buddies.ts`)\n\nThe three mercs you didn't pick (§8.3) live at places, each `defineBody` unique. **Debt** per buddy, an integer from −3 to +3 in a\nLedger screen (\"You owe Ilse 2.\"). Rescue: +1 owed. Helping them or finishing their alternate plan: −1. At +3 they stop coming (\"You're\noverdrawn.\"). **Alternate plans:** before a contract, visit a buddy for a better way to do it: extra objectives and pay, and they join\nyou (NPC with `seat`-free AI). **When a buddy falls** (scripted once in Contract 5, and possibly anywhere they fight): they lie down\ncalling you, with 60 s. Choose: syrette (hold use; costs one; saves them, debt −1), or **mercy** (the prompt appears with a sidearm out;\none shot; the cast comment forever), or leave them. Death is permanent and saved, and changes later lines and the ending's\nlast word.\n\n### 6.9 Economy (`economy.ts`)\n\n**Rough stones.** Contract pay 15–30. **Tin boxes** (8; 5–10 stones each) hidden in wrecks and mounds; the tick-box (D-pad down / B) clicks\nfaster inside 120 m and its lamp holds under 15 m; a mirrored lamp pulses on the map layer. **Ferreira's catalogue**, one item on screen at a time:\nguns (unlocked at armoury crates), Reliability I/II (wear ×0.7/×0.5), syrette capacity, repair kit, camouflage smock (concealment +20%).\nPrices 5–40. **Armoury crates** at safehouses reissue what you own, at full condition. Faction **standing**, one integer per side, changes\ncontract wording, checkpoint behaviour (§6.6) and dealer rumours.\n\n### 6.10 Story engine (`contracts/`)\n\n`def('contract', id, spec)` with a schema. Steps are data; hooks are rare. Sim holds `story` flags and the active step; page shows goal text.\n\n```ts\ndef('contract', 'contract:receipts', {\n  giver: 'cassius', faction: 'front', pay: 15, standing: { front: 1, authority: -1 },\n  brief: 'text:receipts-brief',\n  steps: [\n    { id: 'go', goal: 'Reach the Km-40 post', at: 'km40', radius: 40 },\n    { id: 'take', goal: 'Take the ledger from the radio hut', use: 'ledger-km40' },\n    { id: 'back', goal: 'Bring it to Brother Cassius', talk: 'cassius' },\n  ],\n  alts: [{ buddy: 'yaw', pitch: 'text:receipts-alt', adds: [{ id: 'radio', goal: 'Burn the radio hut', burn: 'km40-hut' }], pay: 8, debt: -1 }],\n});\n```\n\nStep kinds: `at`, `use`, `talk`, `kill`, `burn`, `carry`, `survive`, `escort`, `choice`. Lines run by event (`w.emit('say', { who, text })`), and\nchoices return through a custom intent (`'game:pick'`), so replays and co-op hold them.\n\n### 6.11 Other world rules","numLines":420,"startLine":1,"totalLines":812}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xn8RxdHK72xUgX33mu9RJe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
