{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEL5mHfbHiEH4RocHkW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RqFo2yXEs9LFjQQsnHyT7D","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work/PLAN.md","offset":420,"limit":400},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15355,"cache_read_input_tokens":578758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15355},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"e766af18-2700-4791-ad38-83fc5d658344","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:29:49.773Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEL5VAxAbKABFn66twB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RqFo2yXEs9LFjQQsnHyT7D":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work/PLAN.md","offset":420,"limit":400}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RqFo2yXEs9LFjQQsnHyT7D","type":"tool_result","content":"420\t### 6.11 Other world rules\n421\t\n422\tCeasefire: inside Sainte-Aurore's radius guns are forced holstered and nobody shoots first. Falling back from the map edge: §5.\n423\tSave points: sleeping, and each contract step. Water: §5.\n424\t\n425\t### 6.12 Use (`use.ts`)\n426\t\n427\tOne system for every seat, replacing `addInteraction`. Each step (rate-limited per seat) find the nearest usable: a table of entries\n428\t(door, usable prop, dropped gun, vehicle seat, bed, crate, person, tape, tin box, phone) within 2 m of the eye and within 60° of the look,\n429\tpreferring what the eye ray hits. Write it to `seat.target` with a prompt verb, which the page shows only for its own seat. A press acts through\n430\tthe entry's data: doors with `useDoor`, a seat by entering the vehicle, a person by starting dialogue. **Carrying** (Contract 2's crates, charges): lift holsters your\n431\tgun and caps speed at walk; use again drops it; it can ride in a pickup's bed. **Picking up a gun** swaps it with the slot's, condition and all.\n432\t\n433\t## 7. Weapons\n434\t\n435\tInvented models, all drawn as low-poly props from boxes and frustums, each with new, worn and rusted tints. Values are starting points.\n436\t\n437\t| Gun | Slot | Class | Dmg | Rate | Mag | Wear | Jam | Notes |\n438\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n439\t| Mle. 50 pistol | Side | Semi | 18 | 5 | 8 | 1 | 1 | Starter |\n440\t| Veteran .38 | Side | Revolver | 34 | 2 | 6 | 0.5 | 0 | Slow, never jams |\n441\t| Coach gun | Side | Sawn-off | 12×8 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 0.5 | Two shells |\n442\t| Flare pistol | Side | Fire | 5 | 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | Ignites where it lands |\n443\t| OR-7 rifle | Prim | Auto | 16 | 10 | 30 | 1.2 | 1.5 | Everywhere; enemy junk |\n444\t| FR-2 bullpup | Prim | Auto | 18 | 12 | 25 | 0.6 | 0.5 | Dealer |\n445\t| Pump 12 | Prim | Shotgun | 10×8 | 1.2 | 6 | 0.8 | 0.7 | |\n446\t| Hunter .308 | Prim | Bolt | 90 | 0.8 | 5 | 0.6 | 0.5 | Scope |\n447\t| Whisper SMG | Prim | Suppressed | 12 | 13 | 30 | 1 | 1 | Noise radius 25 |\n448\t| \"Mother\" belt gun | Spec | LMG | 20 | 11 | 100 | 1.5 | 1.5 | Move slower |\n449\t| Sprayer | Spec | Flame | 6/tick | – | Fuel | 1 | 0.5 | Crop sprayer on your back |\n450\t| \"Postman\" launcher | Spec | Rocket | 150 | 0.4 | 1 | 0.5 | 0.2 | Ignites |\n451\t| Molotov, frag | Throw | | | | 4 each | | | R1 / G |\n452\t| Machete | Melee | | 60 | 1.4 | | | | Always carried |\n453\t\n454\t## 8. Story, cast, writing\n455\t\n456\t**Voice.** Dry, weary, literate; menace delivered politely; gallows humour with no jokes for the audience. People speak in complete\n457\tsentences, and nobody explains the theme. Never quippy, never heroic. All speech is gibberish audio (§9.3) with subtitles, so the words on\n458\tscreen do all the work. Keep lines short for 10-foot reading: 1–2 lines, 90 characters a line at most.\n459\t\n460\t### 8.1 The Auctioneer's tapes (cassettes at places; 6)\n461\t\n462\tSale patter, every one a \"lot\". Write in this register:\n463\t\n464\t> \"Lot fourteen. One rifle, Ostrava pattern, sold to the Front on Tuesday and to the Authority on Thursday. Same rifle. It has killed for\n465\t> both and complained to neither. I find that restful. Do I hear an objection? No. There never is.\"\n466\t\n467\t> \"Lot twenty-two. One bridge, unfinished. The contractor was paid twice and shot once. Reserve not met.\"\n468\t\n469\t### 8.2 People\n470\t\n471\t- **Commissioner Adèle Naré**, Provisional Authority, Customs House. Precise, polite, always eating. \"You will hear that we are\n472\t  monsters. It is true, but we keep records.\"\n473\t- **Brother Cassius Oyelu**, Basin Front, Cinema Rex. Lay preacher; contracts as sermons. \"The Lord sends rain on the just and the unjust. I\n474\t  send you, because you are cheaper.\"\n475\t- **Sister Perpetua**, Mission Sainte-Claire. \"Take the bitter ones with water. If there is no water, take them anyway. God is not fussy and\n476\t  neither is the fever.\"\n477\t- **Madame Ferreira**, Ferreira & Daughter, General Merchants: a container at the airstrip. \"Everything I sell works. For a while. That is also\n478\t  true of you.\"\n479\t- **Monsieur Lazare**, clerk at the Hotel Splendide. He hands you the warrant's paperwork, and he's the Auctioneer's old colleague.\n480\t- **The Auctioneer.** Heard everywhere, seen once: an old clerk in a rail car.\n481\t\n482\t### 8.3 The mercs (pick one at New Game; the others become buddies)\n483\t\n484\t| Merc | Who | Buddy gift | Sample line |\n485\t|---|---|---|---|\n486\t| **Ilse Brandt** | Ex-army field medic from Bremen; keeps accounts | Rescues faster | \"That is two you owe me. I write them down.\" |\n487\t| **Tomás Arriaga** | Colombian demolitions; sings; likes fire too much | Explosive alternate plans | \"The wind is a good employee. It never asks for a raise.\" |\n488\t| **Yaw Mensah** | Ghanaian ex-peacekeeper; the last decent man, and he resents it | Talks patrols down, holds posts | \"I came here to keep the peace. Somebody should tell it.\" |\n489\t| **Mirela Dragan** | Romanian ex-Legion marksman; few words | Overwatch from high ground | \"Stay down.\" / \"Still alive. Disappointing for somebody.\" |\n490\t\n491\tThe pick screen shows four big portraits (rendered bodies, one at a time), never a stat sheet.\n492\t\n493\t### 8.4 Contracts (about 45–60 minutes; each 3–9 minutes)\n494\t\n495\t| # | Contract | Giver | What happens | Teaches |\n496\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n497\t| P | **Lot Zero** | – | Night on a barge among crates with the Auctioneer's mark. The Front lights the reeds. It burns. Wade ashore with a rusted revolver that jams. Crouch through grass past a patrol, heal, fever hits, you collapse. Your first buddy buys you from a patrol: first debt. Wake at the Mission. Sister Perpetua gives pills; Lazare's warrant names the Auctioneer | Move, grass, jam, syrette, fever, rescue, debt |\n498\t| 1 | **Receipts** | Cassius | Steal a ledger from Km-40. Yaw's alternate: also burn the radio hut | Vehicle, map, firefight, checkpoints, standing, dealer visit |\n499\t| 2 | **Bitter** | Perpetua | An aid truck's quinine is in a burning field; bring 3 crates before the wind turns | Fire hazard, wind, pills |\n500\t| 3 | **The Reserve** | Naré | Destroy the Front's fuel at Pump Station with a flare from upwind. Tomás's alternate: bring the engineer out alive first | Fire as a weapon, forecast, stealth, alternate plans |\n501\t| 4 | **Slash and Burn** | Cassius | Burn Belvédère's barns, whose crop pays the Authority. The wind shifts mid-mission toward you. Technicals arrive. Escape by patrol boat | Big burn, mounted guns, boat |\n502\t| 5 | **Second Invoice** | A buddy | A buddy's call from Salt Works. Fight in the open white pans, no fuel to help you. They're down at the end: syrette, mercy or leave | Mercy, permadeath, ledger, overdraw |\n503\t| 6 | **Lot One** | Lazare | The sale at Mine No. 6: both factions come to bid. Cross the fight, ride the ropeway, reach the rail car. The final tape: the last lot is you. Choose: **Serve the warrant** (shoot him; the bidding reopens Tuesday), **Buy him out** (60 stones; he flies, you get his fever cure and his ledger), or **Burn the catalogue** (light the stock with the wind toward you; the buddy who owes you most decides whether you get out) | Everything |\n504\t\n505\tAfter an ending: credits, then the world stays open for free roam from the title's Continue. Side content: 8 tin boxes, 6 tapes, 3 safehouses, 3 checkpoints,\n506\t1 convoy to ambush on the east road, 1 assassination by field telephone (a pole phone call: kill the courier on the south road; pays stones).\n507\t\n508\t## 9. Look, animation, sound\n509\t\n510\t### 9.1 Art direction: the engine's native low-poly style, sun-bleached\n511\t\n512\t**Base style:** the engine's lit materials on simple shapes (clean look), no pixel or cel filters. **Palette:** straw `#B4985A`, red earth\n513\t`#80543A`, laterite `#9A4E2E`, bleached sky haze `#D8C9A8`, thorn green `#7F8A3E`, rust `#8C4A22`, char `#1F1A18`, flame `#F08A24`,\n514\tsalt `#E8E2D0`. Authority khaki with red armband and a black bar stencil; Front mismatched with blue scarves and a white triangle stencil.\n515\t\n516\t- **`look:dry-season`:** `sky:'sky:daylight'`, `grade` (temperature +0.18, saturation 0.9, contrast 1.08), `split` warm/teal, `vignette` 0.25,\n517\t  `air` (haze 0.35, height 8, shafts 0.6), light `grain`. A filter stays off until it has a `scope`, so give each `scope:'all'`. Verified:\n518\t  `sky:daylight` + `grade` over the savanna texture and thorn trees already reads as hot savanna.\n519\t- **`look:fever`:** laid over with `post.combine`: `chroma`, `lens`, `watercolor` bleed, heavy vignette, amount driven live.\n520\t- **Body camera and critical:** colour drain with `selective` or `grade`.\n521\t- **Materials and textures** (generators with `tileNoise`, `cellHash`): savanna, laterite, ironstone, salt crust, road gravel, mud plaster, corrugated tin\n522\t  (with rust streaks), sacking, painted stencil walls, tobacco leaf, canvas, gun metal, worn wood.\n523\t- **Props to make:** trees and grass (§5), charred variants, scorch, flame patch, termite mound, boulders; mud-brick huts, tin roofs, concrete bunker, watchtower,\n524\t  sandbags, tyre barricade, boom gate, oil drums, fuel tanks, propane, ammo and armoury crates, shipping container, water tower, power poles, pipeline, pump\n525\t  house, conveyors, salt mounds, drying barns and racks, rail cars, ropeway, jetty, barge, plane wreck, car wrecks, faction flags, posters; vehicles (§6.7); all guns (§7);\n526\t  syrette, pill bottle, tick-box, map, cassette player, tin box, field telephone. Engine props are fine for generic chairs, tables, lamps.\n527\t- **Buildings** as `defineLevel` format 2 storeys on the site, tile 0.5, 2–3 interiors worth entering per place, doors with `addLevelDoors` driven by your `use` system, breakable\n528\t  windows.\n529\t- **Bodies** (`defineBody`, read `.cache/engine-src/labs/playground/bodies/`): four mercs, two faction soldier bodies with seeded slot variation, officers, townsfolk, Sister, Naré, Cassius,\n530\t  Ferreira, Lazare, the Auctioneer, gazelle. Co-op armbands in the hub's seat colours.\n531\t\n532\t### 9.2 Animation: the engine's system plus new work\n533\t\n534\tAuthor with `defineAction` (`node x new action`), checked by `actionCheck`. Effector targets are `[forward, right, up]` metres from the shoulder centre; set them low and about 0.45 m forward\n535\tfor body-camera moments.\n536\t\n537\t- **Player:** `syrette`, `pill`, `surgery-dig`, `surgery-finger`, `surgery-burn`, `jam-clear`, `reload-rifle`, `reload-pistol` (for shoulder view and others to see), `repair`,\n538\t  `drive`, `gunner`, `map-hold`, `use-low`, `throw`, `machete-chop`.\n539\t- **People:** `rescue` + `rescued` pair, `drag` + `dragged` pair, `mercy-plea`, `wave-through`, `officer-point`, `panic-burn`, `smoke-idle`, `sit-talk`, `pray`, `eat`, `jam-swear`.\n540\t- **Library clips:** crawl (`mesh2motion/Crawl`), others by `node x anim find`. Import only the sets used, as `?raw`, to keep the file small.\n541\t- **Procedural:** wheels, steering, suspension, mounted gun, flags turning to the wind, ragdolls on death, conveyor, gazelle gait, rocking boat.\n542\t\n543\t### 9.3 Audio: code only, no audio files\n544\t\n545\t- **Music at 10% by default:** right after `createAudio()`, `audio.volume('music', 0.1)`. The engine's default is 0.5, so this is required and tested. Stored volume wins after the player changes it.\n546\t- **Songs (`defineSong`, original, 3–5):** sparse desert-blues over plucked pentatonic arpeggios and hand drums: Title, Roam (low and tense, intensity layers), Combat\n547\t  (`audio.intensity` by alert state), Fever (detuned, slow), Ending. Nothing that echoes the source's score.\n548\t- **SFX (`defineSfx`):** each gun class with distance tail (`sound` on the weapon), dry click, jam rack, reload parts, machete, grenade, rocket, flare, fire crackle in three sizes, flare-up whoosh,\n549\t  barrel explosion, cook-off pops, engines by rpm (pitch on a loop), gears, skid, wrench, car door, boat, footsteps by surface (`SURFACE_STEPS`, add grass rustle), wind by speed, insects day\n550\t  and night, thunder, rain, tick-box click, tape hiss and clunk, syrette, pill rattle, surgery wince, heartbeat, UI cues.\n551\t- **Voices (`sounds/voice.ts`):** Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Turn each line's text into syllables by hashing its words; each syllable is a very short formant-filtered voice (`defineSfx` per vowel and\n552\t  consonant class, or direct Web Audio on `audio.context`) with per-character base pitch, rate and vibrato; play in sequence on the `ui` bus while the subtitle types out. NPC barks use positional\n553\t  syllable bursts. Never real words.\n554\t- **Mix:** `room` reverb for interiors, `duck` during dialogue, `update(pose, queries)` each frame for 3D and occlusion. Settings sliders: Master, Music, Effects, Voices, Ambience.\n555\t\n556\t## 10. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n557\t\n558\t### 10.1 Controls\n559\t\n560\tEvery device gets the same game on the same screens; no desktop layout. Own action maps (`defineActionMap`, `look:true, aimWith:'centre', lock:true` for first person; a second for vehicles). Bindings rebindable with `input.listen`.\n561\t\n562\t| Action | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\n563\t|---|---|---|\n564\t| Move / Look | L stick / R stick | WASD / mouse |\n565\t| Fire / Aim | R2 / L2 | LMB / RMB |\n566\t| Jump, mantle | Cross | Space |\n567\t| Crouch | Circle | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the tab) |\n568\t| Sprint | L3 | Left Shift |\n569\t| Use (tap), Reload and clear jam (hold) | Square, `Hold:PadWest` | E, R |\n570\t| Next weapon / holster (hold) | Triangle | 1 2 3, wheel / X |\n571\t| Melee | R3 | V |\n572\t| Throw | R1 | G |\n573\t| Syrette (surgery when critical) | L1 | H |\n574\t| Map / Tick-box / Pills / Fire-gun quick-draw | D-pad up, down, left, right | M / B / P / F |\n575\t| Ledger | Create | L |\n576\t| Camera view toggle | Hold Create | T |\n577\t| Pause | Options | Esc |\n578\t| Drive: throttle, brake, steer, handbrake, exit, seat | R2, L2, L stick, Cross, Square, Triangle | W, S, A D, Space, E, Q |\n579\t\n580\tIn a hub session the game ignores Options while Create is held.\n581\t\n582\t**Mouse is native:** pointer lock in play; in menus hover moves focus and click picks (`createMenu`; custom panels too, `createPadCursor` for pad). **Things in the world:** under lock, the crosshair is the\n583\tpointer: looking at something usable highlights it with a world-anchored label, and with no weapon out a left click uses it, as well as E.\n584\t\n585\t**Prompts follow the last input.** `ui/glyphs.ts`: inline SVG for PlayStation shapes (✕ ○ □ △ L1 R1 L2 R2 L3 R3 Options Create, D-pad) and Xbox (A B X Y LB RB LT RT LS RS Menu View). Pick by `input.lastDevice`: `gamepad` → PlayStation\n586\tglyphs for any pad, or Xbox if Settings says so; keyboard → key caps and mouse icons with the actual binding (`input.bindingsFor`, `codeLabel`, `readKeyboardLayout`). Every prompt element carries `data-glyph` for tests, and they swap at once when the device changes. Verified: with a\n587\tstubbed DualSense, `input.lastDevice` turns `gamepad`, `input.held`/`strength` work, and `input.prompt('jump')` is `Cross`.\n588\t\n589\t### 10.2 First person without a closed door\n590\t\n591\tThe default camera is `cam3=first`. For **body moments** (surgery, syrette on critical, repair, rescue from the ground) blend (`__engine.camera.set(code, { blend: true })`) to custom `cam3=body` (`defineCamera`, `followCamera`, `makePose`):\n592\tat the eye about 0.1 m forward, pitch about −50°, body drawn whole because only `first` hides it. **Verified:** this shows the player's own sleeves, hands and gun in frame during a `defineAction`; framing needs tuning (holster the gun, arms farther out). The head's back faces don't block\n593\tit. `cam3=driver` is the same idea with a level pitch at the driver's eye. The world keeps running throughout.\n594\t\n595\t### 10.3 Screens and HUD\n596\t\n597\t**10-foot rules:** type scales with `vh`; body text ≥ 3.2vh (34 px at 1080p), headings 6vh, subtitles 3.4vh on a dark band; 5% safe margins; one decision a screen; at most 7 visible list items; no tables of data: the dealer and ledger show one thing large, stepped with\n598\tleft/right. System font stacks only (stencil-ish headings via `Impact, \"Arial Narrow\"`, typed notes via `\"Courier New\"`); no font files. Visual language: field notebook, stencil, carbon-copy paper, rust.\n599\t\n600\t**HUD (first person):** five syrette-shaped health segments, ammo and gun condition as a small rust bar, syrette and pill counts only when they change or are low; centre dot crosshair (none down the sights); goal line for 5 s when it changes; wind ribbon as per §6.5; damage arcs; prompts near centre-bottom. No\n601\tminimap, ever.\n602\t\n603\t**Map in hand (`ui/map.ts`), the world doesn't pause.** A paper map on a CSS 3D layer (`perspective`, `rotateX`, slides up with an arm-raise ease, sways with the camera's turn), SVG hands gripping its edges in the merc's skin tone. Contour lines baked once to a canvas from `terrain.heights`; places as ink labels once discovered; roads, river; burn scars as hatch from fire state; an arrow for you; goal marker;\n604\twind arrow. R stick or pointer moves a pencil cursor, Cross or click drops a waypoint (a world-anchored marker). You walk at half speed with it up, and you can drive with it up (it sits low and to the right). The tick-box shows beside it as a small device with lamp and needle.\n605\t\n606\t**Screens:** Title (Continue, New Game, Co-op, Settings, Controls, About); merc pick; Pause (Resume, Map, Ledger, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About, Quit to title); Settings; Controls with rebinding (a picture of the pad and a short list); Dialogue (subtitle band with portrait name; choices as a short `createMenu`); Sleep (dawn, noon, dusk); Dealer; Ledger (a page each: debts,\n607\tfactions, tapes, stones); Co-op lobby; Game over; Ending; Credits.\n608\t\n609\t**Settings:** Master, Music (10%), Effects, Voices, Ambience; Glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox); Camera (first / shoulder); FOV (`cam.fov`); mouse and stick sensitivity and invert (`input.*`), aim-assist-free; Crouch hold/toggle; Fever intensity; Screen shake; Subtitle size; Quality (`quality`); Fullscreen (`requestFullscreen`). Keep with `createStore`.\n610\t\n611\t### 10.4 Touch-only devices\n612\t\n613\tIf `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` and no pad or key has been seen: no touch controls (`touch` setting `off`, no `touchLayout`). Show a full-screen message exactly **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a **Settings** button over the attract mode, which keeps running. A pad press or key press dismisses it for good. Test with Playwright's phone profile.\n614\t\n615\tIf WebGPU is missing on any device, show a plain message naming a browser that has it; the engine has no WebGL fallback, and the sim still runs.\n616\t\n617\t## 11. Title, attract mode, dev mode, About\n618\t\n619\t### 11.1 Title\n620\t\n621\t`game.mode=title`: slow camera over the savanna at dusk with a fire line on the horizon (`cam3=fixed` or `rail`), title lettering in CSS, Title song. The view lights and shadows round the player actor, so park it near the camera's target, out of frame. Starting play sets the mode and calls `inspector.seed(n)`.\n622\t\n623\t### 11.2 Attract mode\n624\t\n625\tAfter **10 s without input** on the title or any menu off the title (keys, mouse move or click, pad buttons or sticks past deadzone all reset the timer), switch to `game.mode=attract` and restart. A page-side director (`attract.ts`) plays a loop of vignettes by placing the bot with dev actions and feeding `inspector.step(1, botIntents)` on a paused clock, with cheats on (`game.god`, infinite ammo; teleporting\n626\tand scripted fires are fine). Each runs 15–25 s with a banner: title + \"Press any button\":\n627\t\n628\t1. Chase camera: a technical tearing down the road at dusk. 2. First person: firefight at Km-40. 3. Flare into grass; wind carries it; soldiers panic. 4. A jam at the worst moment, cleared. 5. Fever attack with mirages, pill. 6. Down, buddy rescue, ledger line. 7. Map in hand and tick-box, finding a tin box. 8. Boat with mounted gun past the burning estate. 9. Dealer and tape caption, then loop.\n629\t\n630\tCamera and look change per vignette (`__engine.camera.set`). **Any input exits at once** to the title (restart). It runs on touch-only devices too, and off-line: nothing is fetched. Never start it when automation should test the title unless asked: a setting `game.attract=auto|off|on` for tests.\n631\t\n632\t### 11.3 Dev mode: Pause → Dev Mode (not in hub sessions)\n633\t\n634\tPad and mouse friendly, big rows, one category at a time:\n635\t\n636\t- **Balance:** live sliders on `scenes/settings.ts`, each with its value and a per-row and global **Reset to defaults**: wear per shot, jam multiplier, player damage, enemy damage, enemy accuracy, reaction, sight, hearing, attackers, respawn hours; fire spread, wind bias, burn time, fire damage, regrow; wind speed, shift interval; fever interval, severity; HP, regen, syrette heal; car engine, grip, spring, damper; prices, stone payouts; day length; `movement.*`. Settings use `when:'now'` and systems read them at each use. `__engine.set` applies a value; reset writes each default from the table back the same way.\n637\t- **Cheats:** god, infinite ammo, no wear/jam, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip, one-shot kills.\n638\t- **Teleport:** every place, the crosshair point, a chosen map point.\n639\t- **Spawn:** any gun with chosen condition, vehicle, squad, buddy, tin box.\n640\t- **World:** hour, time scale (`time.scale`), wind dial, rain, ignite at crosshair, burn all, regrow all, fever now.\n641\t- **Story:** jump to any contract or step, set flags, debts, standing, give stones.\n642\t- **Debug overlays:** fire grid, AI state labels (`engine.ui.label`), detection meters, nav paths; `__engine.stats()` numbers; digest; quick save/load.\n643\t\n644\tSliders survive across resume, not across New Game unless \"Keep\" is on.\n645\t\n646\t### 11.4 About/Credits\n647\t\n648\tReachable from title and pause; pad and mouse scrollable pages. Pages: Source Information (all fields in TASK.md), Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Credits (engine, three.js, Rapier, @stdlib, motion clips per `data/anim/SOURCES.md`, source note: \"inspired by Far Cry 2, not affiliated\"). **One source of truth:** `scripts/bundle.mjs` reads the exit-interview file and injects it as data, so the screen and the file can't differ. Usage reads literally \"added on import\".\n649\t\n650\t## 12. Multiplayer\n651\t\n652\t**Decision: `shared-world`, host-sequenced deterministic lockstep.** The engine's one superpower is bit-exact determinism, so instead of replicating fire cells, ragdolls and NPCs, every copy runs the same scene from the same seed, and the host sequences everyone's input. No per-entity networking code.\n653\t\n654\t**Verified end to end:** a probe with this recipe passes the real harness in all four of its configurations, each listed in §13; four copies computed identical digests at the same step despite 150 ms latency, jitter and 5% loss; the `server` copy ran `createHeadless` in the browser, with no WebGPU.\n655\t\n656\t### 12.1 The mode: **Contract Run** (`game.mode=contract`)\n657\t\n658\t1–4 mercs, about 5 minutes, in the Pump Station region: reach the depot, burn it (flare, sprayer or charges at 3 points, all driven by wind), survive the counter-attack, get out by the river boat or pickups. Revive teammates (hold use 3 s; bleed-out 40 s). Friendly fire and friendly fire-fire are on. All down, or time up without getting out: team loses. `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })`: score = objective 500 + kills 50 + rescues 150 + extracted 200 − downs 100 − teammates burned 200; awards like \"Best employee of the wind\". The hub deals by these tags:\n659\t\n660\t```html\n661\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n662\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n663\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n664\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Burn the depot, then get out alive together\">\n665\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick or WASD moves, R2 or click fires, Square or E uses\">\n666\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n667\t<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n668\t```\n669\t\n670\tSolo in-hub (1 seat) still works. Names and colours come from `info.players`; set names with `textContent`, armbands by seat colour. No chat, emotes or custom names, no `alert`, no new tabs, no menus before the round, and pause opens only Settings without stopping the sim. Quit does nothing.\n671\t\n672\t### 12.2 The session flow (order matters)\n673\t\n674\t1. `session.js` is the first script after `<meta charset>`, unmodified (bundler does this).\n675\t2. In `main.ts`, first thing: `if (AIHub.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. `null` means play on as standalone.\n676\t3. Start: `createEngine` with `search: ?seed=${info.seed}&game.mode=contract&game.seats=${n}&game.me=${info.me}&cam3=first&gfx.warmUp=asked`. **`gfx.warmUp=asked` is required:** with the default `all`, four copies sharing one main thread blocked past the deadlines. On a software adapter also lower `game.detail` (one fixed value across copies; pass through the host if adapters differ, or simply use a fixed contract-mode density).\n677\t4. **Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the sim exists, not when the first frame draws.** Poll `typeof window.__engine?.step === 'function'` every 20 ms (reached in about 1 s); then `__engine.pause()`, start the pump, `ready()`. The harness allows all copies 20 s, and rendering took 5–25 s on software WebGPU with 4 frames; the view catches up by itself.\n678\t5. **The pump:** a 16 ms `setInterval` alone passes the harness (verified); once frames flow, step from `onFrame` for smooth motion, and keep the timer for when frames stop. All copies run on the paused clock through `inspector.step`. **While paused, the camera still turns with mouse and stick** (verified: look is view state), so aim feels immediate on every copy.\n679\t6. `AIHub.server`: no engine. `createHeadless({ scene, seed, settings: { 'game.seats': n, 'game.me': -1, 'game.mode': 'contract' } })`, pump on the timer, call `finish`. If `navigator.gpu` is missing on a playing copy: `AIHub.fail('WebGPU is required')`.\n680\t7. `time-up` → host `finish` at once from its handler. `end` → stop input, stop sound (`audio.mute(true)`), stop stepping, send nothing. Host leaving voids the round by protocol; do nothing special.\n681\t\n682\t### 12.3 The lockstep core (`net/lockstep.ts`)\n683\t\n684\t```ts\n685\tconst TURN = 4;                         // steps a turn: 15 messages a second, under the hub's 20\n686\t// Local wire, rebuilt each frame in onFrame from engine.input (held/strength), frame.camera (yaw, pitch) and an aim ray:\n687\t//   { m:[x,z], l:[yaw,pitch], a:[x,y,z], b:[...buttons pressed or held since last sent] }   rounded to 3 decimals\n688\t// client, every 66 ms:  net.send({ k:'i', w: wire }, { to: host, reliable: true })\n689\t// host, every 66 ms, ONE message however many turns are due (a burst per turn breaks the rate limit; verified):\n690\t//   const due = Math.floor(net.time() / (1000 / 60));\n691\t//   const n = Math.min(Math.floor((due - sent) / TURN), 30); if (n > 0) {\n692\t//     latest[me] = wire; const f = { k:'f', s: sent, n, i: { ...latest }, x: seatEvents };\n693\t//     net.send(f, { reliable: true }); queue.push(f); sent += TURN * n; }\n694\t// every copy: for each frame in order, for each of TURN*n steps, when due:\n695\t//   engine.step(1, { ...toIntents(f.i[me]), 'game:seats': othersAsIntents(f.i, me), 'game:events': f.x });\n696\t// Playout: run max(1, dt*60) steps a frame while frames wait, up to 12 when far behind, so motion is smooth at 60 Hz.\n697\t```\n698\t\n699\t**Rules that keep copies identical:**\n700\t\n701\t- **Everything the sim sees comes through the host's frames.** A `leave` event, a pick in a dialogue, a revive: all are host-sequenced (`x`, `game:events`, or the wire). Never feed a local `leave` straight to the sim: copies hear it at different times.\n702\t- `game.me` differs per copy, so `actor.player` differs, so **`engine.hash()` differs across copies by design**. Compare `digest.ts` (seats, NPCs, vehicles' positions and HP, fire state counts, as a string) instead. Clients send `{ k:'d', s, h }` every 2 s; the host logs mismatches and shows a small \"out of sync\" note; tests fail on it. No resync: `capture()` is far too big, and determinism holds by construction.\n703\t- Keep sim settings identical across copies (from the host via URL), dev mode off, and sanitize wire data (finite numbers, known buttons) before it reaches intents: `normalizeIntents` throws on junk.\n704\t- A tap shorter than a turn must survive: OR presses into `b` until the wire is sent.\n705\t\n706\t### 12.4 The game on its own\n707\t\n708\tOutside the hub, Title → Co-op runs the same Contract Run with no server, through the same `Net` interface (`send`, `on('message')`, `time`, `players`, `isHost`):\n709\t\n710\t- **`net/tabs.ts`: \"Same computer\":** `BroadcastChannel`; host lists itself, others join; a second tab, window or screen. Verified from `file://` between two pages.\n711\t- **`net/rtc.ts`: \"Invite code\":** one `RTCPeerConnection` and ordered data channel per guest (star on the host), non-trickle ICE, `iceServers:[{urls:'stun:stun.l.google.com:19302'}]`, base64 of the description as a copy-and-paste code with a Copy button and a Paste field: host's code to guest, guest's reply to host. Verified from `file://` in two separate browser contexts with no STUN: connects in 0.3 s with 650-byte descriptions.\n712\t\n713\tUse the hub's seat colours and a local 3 s countdown. Rule: none of this runs while `AIHub.active` (network only through the hub).\n714\t\n715\t### 12.5 Own card\n716\t\n717\tBecause the game has its own world, use `card: true`: HTML/CSS card over the loading scene showing the game's name, players in colours with ready ticks, how to win, this player's controls, time left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross or a click: `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle, a named key or a click: `AIHub.answer('more')`. No menus; nothing changes the round. Play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`, after `start`.\n718\t\n719\t## 13. Testing\n720\t\n721\t**One command:** `node tests/game/verify.mjs [sim|page|hub]` (add `\"verify\"` to `package.json`). It prints only failures and a final one-line count (`verify: 212 passed, 0 failed`). Vitest with `--reporter=json` and parsed. Rerun a tier only after changing what it covers. Screenshots only for what a script can't judge; save them in `out/`. Keep one or two browsers open at a time. Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n722\t\n723\t| Tier | What it proves |\n724\t|---|---|\n725\t| **sim** (Vitest, Node; seconds to minutes) | Starter's four kinds kept: golden replay (1), capture/restore, bot, rules. Wear lowers condition and swaps tier ids; jam rate at given conditions over many shots; clearing works. HP, regen, syrette, surgery, down, rescue, debt, overdraw. Fever timeline, pills, collapse. **Fire front metric** (§6.5), firebreaks hold, embers jump, rain stops it, regrowth. Wind shifts on schedule with forecast. Stealth: same patrol detects standing in the open and misses crouched in grass; burned grass exposes. AI squad clears cover and flanks; jam window. Checkpoint repopulation; holstered pass with standing. Vehicle: drives a route, stays on terrain, repairs, explodes; `placeActor` seat; run-over. Economy purchases, caches, armoury. Save → reload → same state fields. Contract engine: every contract and alt completes by script. **Lockstep digest:** 1, 2, 4 headless copies with different `game.me` fed the same frames keep equal digests over 3,600 steps with a fight, a fire and a car in them. |\n726\t| **Whole-game playthrough** (sim) | `bot.ts` completes prologue through every ending on seeds 1–3 with `game.god`, through intents only, using teleport-free travel for contract 1 and dev travel after. One honest run: bot clears Km-40 without god on at least 7 of 10 seeds, as a balance alarm. |\n727\t| **page** (Playwright on the deliverable over `file://`) | Boots `ready` with no errors. Title → attract at 10 s; any key, mouse or pad input exits it (virtual clock not needed; use `game.attract` and a short setting for the wait, and one real 10 s test). Keyboard-only and pad-only (stubbed `navigator.getGamepads`) routes from title to first control. Prompts swap device on input; Xbox option; `data-glyph` values. Music bus reads 0.1 at first run; volume persists. `renderSong`, `renderSfx` and an `OfflineAudioContext` run of a voice line produce non-silent, unclipped audio (`node x qa audio`). Pause and Dev Mode: a slider changes behaviour, reset restores. Map opens without pausing the tick count. Mouse hover moves menu focus. About matches the exit-interview file. Phone profile shows the exact touch message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract running. WebKit and Firefox have no WebGPU here, so Chromium only; say so. |\n728\t| **hub** | Fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` to `.cache/hub/`; copy the deliverable beside them; serve on an OS-picked 127.0.0.1 port; confirm the page marker. All must give `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` (`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` when finished): `players=2`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; the same with `scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`; all with `&auto=1`. Launch args include the WebGPU flags of §2. Then standalone: same deliverable alone, solo; two pages over tabs link; two contexts over invite codes, digests equal. |\n729\t| **look** (rare) | `node x shot` numbers and `node x gallery prop` for art; 1920×1080 screenshots of each UI screen for the 10-foot judgement. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot; check state instead when it does. |\n730\t\n731\t**Not checkable here; say so in your feedback:** real GPUs, real pads, speakers, cross-machine determinism, iOS.\n732\t\n733\t## 14. Build order\n734\t\n735\tBuild a walking skeleton first, then keep the deliverable working at every step. Run `npm run check` and the relevant `verify` tier before moving on.\n736\t\n737\t| # | Do | Done when |\n738\t|---|---|---|\n739\t| 0 | §2 setup. Pick the title as TASK.md says (brainstorm silently, real RNG), into `title.ts`. Write `scripts/bundle.mjs` (§15.1), `fetch-hub.mjs`, `verify.mjs` skeleton. Add hub metas and a stub session | One-file loads over `file://`; harness passes with the starter + stub |\n740\t| 1 | Site, terrain, river, roads, scatter, looks, day cycle; `movement:merc`; `seats.ts`; action maps; first person; HUD shell | Walk the map in first person; prompts follow device |\n741\t| 2 | `arms.ts`, wear and jam, `health.ts`, one gun, Rifleman, perception, Km-40. **Now `lockstep.ts` + digest test + `net/hub.ts`**, so co-op stays honest from here | Bot clears Km-40; digests equal; harness passes with guns |\n742\t| 3 | Fire, wind, flare, grass burning, scars, panic | Fire metric test; looks like fire in a shot |\n743\t| 4 | Vehicles, driver AI, patrols, repair, boat, mounted guns | Bot drives a route; vehicle tests |\n744\t| 5 | Fever, buddies, ledger, stones, tick-box, dealer, safehouses, saves, rest of the guns and enemy types | Tier tests green |\n745\t| 6 | Contract engine, all story content, dialogue, voices, tapes, map in hand, endings | Playthrough bot finishes the game |\n746\t| 7 | Contract Run, own card, tabs and invite links | Full hub tier green |\n747\t| 8 | Title, pause, settings, controls, dev mode, attract, touch notice, About | Page tier green |\n748\t| 9 | Art, animation, audio passes across everything; balance by sliders and bot | No placeholder boxes or stand-ins anywhere; a search for TODO, FIXME, placeholder finds nothing |\n749\t| 10 | Finish: §15 | All below |\n750\t\n751\t## 15. Finish line\n752\t\n753\t### 15.1 Packaging: `scripts/bundle.mjs` (verified: 6.7 MB, loads from `file://`, harness passes)\n754\t\n755\t```js\n756\timport { build } from 'vite'; import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'; import { join } from 'node:path';\n757\tconst root = process.cwd();\n758\tconst result = await build({ root, configFile: false, logLevel: 'warn', base: './',\n759\t  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\n760\t  build: { write: false, modulePreload: false, cssCodeSplit: false, assetsInlineLimit: () => true, chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\n761\t    rollupOptions: { input: { game: join(root, 'labs/game/index.html') }, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } } } });\n762\tconst files = {}; let html;\n763\tfor (const item of [result].flat().flatMap((o) => o.output)) {\n764\t  const text = item.type === 'chunk' ? item.code : typeof item.source === 'string' ? item.source : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\n765\t  if (item.fileName.endsWith('.html')) html = text; else files[item.fileName] = text; }\n766\tconst find = (ref) => files[Object.keys(files).find((f) => ref.endsWith('/' + f) || ref === f || ref === './' + f)];\n767\thtml = html.replace(/<script type=\"module\" crossorigin src=\"([^\"]+)\"><\\/script>|<link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"([^\"]+)\">/g, (_t, s, c) => {\n768\t  if (c) return `<style>${find(c)}</style>`;\n769\t  const code = find(s).replaceAll('</script', '<\\\\/script');\n770\t  if (code.includes('<!--')) throw new Error('script holds <!--: split it in the source');\n771\t  return `<script type=\"module\">${code}</script>`; });\n772\tconst session = readFileSync('.cache/hub/session.js', 'utf8'); // the unmodified client: scripts/fetch-hub.mjs downloads it\n773\thtml = html.replace('<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />', () => `<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\\n<script>${session}</script>\\n${HUB_METAS}`);\n774\twriteFileSync(DELIVERABLE, html); // DELIVERABLE: the name your TASK.md gives, in '..'; inject the exit-interview file as data too\n775\t```\n776\t\n777\t`fetch-hub.mjs` downloads `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `.cache/hub/`, where lint and format can't touch them: the client must stay byte-identical. The protocol's full text is `README.md` at the same address; read it once. Everything in the deliverable is inline, so nothing depends on a CDN.\n778\t\n779\t### 15.2 Your own feedback\n780\t\n781\tKeep `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` current as AGENTS.md asks. Starting points, if they bite you too: arms rig closed to games; weapons, melee and use only for the `player` actor; no scene access for game meshes (raw geometry through `.constructor` is a hack); TASK.md's browser flags vs the engine's; `capture` size; `setup.sh` downloads outside the folder; one scene per page. Don't patch the engine (it stays read-only); `npm run check` proves it. Keep `labs/game/README.md` true: what the game is, how it plays, the calls you made.\n782\t\n783\t### 15.3 Exit interview\n784\t\n785\tWrite the exit-interview file in exactly the shape your TASK.md gives, with honest counts from your testing. Suggested catalogue values: genre `Shooter`, type `Game`, source `Far Cry 2`, series `Far Cry`, players `1–4`, tags from `3d, first-person, co-op, vehicles, exploration, low-poly`. Plan field: `PLAN.md`. Research: engine and hub source reading, this plan's verified probes, plus whatever you did. Validate with `JSON.parse`, rebuild so About shows it, and put Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in your final chat reply too, using \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm, and Usage as \"added on import\". Say plainly what you did not verify.\n786\t\n787\t### 15.4 Coverage: TASK.md → this plan\n788\t\n789\t| TASK.md item | Where |\n790\t|---|---|\n791\t| Genre, perspective | §1 |\n792\t| Title: riff, 50 brainstormed, real RNG | §14 step 0 (your job; `title.ts`) |\n793\t| Research: your choice | Done for engine and hub (§2, §3, §12); add your own if you wish, and report it |\n794\t| Single HTML in root, dev files in subfolder | §15.1 |\n795\t| Full workspace; engine read-only; add systems, art, animations on top | §2, §3, §15.2 |\n796\t| Art direction, animation | §9.1, §9.2, §10.2 |\n797\t| Audio: code only, gibberish voices, music 10% | §9.3, §13 page tier |\n798\t| Online and multiplayer: hub and on its own | §12 |\n799\t| Shared machine: ports, PIDs, files, browsers | §2, §13 |\n800\t| Performance unlimited, FPS out of scope | §5 (`game.detail` default 1 and only for tests and software adapters) |\n801\t| Testing: headless, one command, failures and count, playthrough, screenshots rarely, no debate agents | §13 |\n802\t| Stand-ins: pad, touch, audio, second player, 1080p | §13 |\n803\t| Feature-complete demo; distinctive world, characters, themes, tone | §1, §5, §6, §8 |\n804\t| Infrastructure for later content with normal tools | §4, §6.10 |\n805\t| Dev mode from pause, sliders, reset | §11.3 |\n806\t| Attract mode at 10 s, looping, cheats, any input exits | §11.2 |\n807\t| Narrative tone | §8 |\n808\t| 10-foot, controller first, native keyboard and mouse, hover focus, world clicks, prompts by last input, PS glyphs with Xbox option, no dense screens | §10 |\n809\t| Touch-only: message, settings button, attract runs | §10.4 |\n810\t| No TODOs or stubs | §0, §14 step 9 |\n811\t| Source Information, feedback in chat and About; the exit-interview file | §11.4, §15.3 |\n812\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"e9ff7f74-47ac-49c4-b955-b9f7dc038c2c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:29:49.922Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 6.11 Other world rules\n\nCeasefire: inside Sainte-Aurore's radius guns are forced holstered and nobody shoots first. Falling back from the map edge: §5.\nSave points: sleeping, and each contract step. Water: §5.\n\n### 6.12 Use (`use.ts`)\n\nOne system for every seat, replacing `addInteraction`. Each step (rate-limited per seat) find the nearest usable: a table of entries\n(door, usable prop, dropped gun, vehicle seat, bed, crate, person, tape, tin box, phone) within 2 m of the eye and within 60° of the look,\npreferring what the eye ray hits. Write it to `seat.target` with a prompt verb, which the page shows only for its own seat. A press acts through\nthe entry's data: doors with `useDoor`, a seat by entering the vehicle, a person by starting dialogue. **Carrying** (Contract 2's crates, charges): lift holsters your\ngun and caps speed at walk; use again drops it; it can ride in a pickup's bed. **Picking up a gun** swaps it with the slot's, condition and all.\n\n## 7. Weapons\n\nInvented models, all drawn as low-poly props from boxes and frustums, each with new, worn and rusted tints. Values are starting points.\n\n| Gun | Slot | Class | Dmg | Rate | Mag | Wear | Jam | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Mle. 50 pistol | Side | Semi | 18 | 5 | 8 | 1 | 1 | Starter |\n| Veteran .38 | Side | Revolver | 34 | 2 | 6 | 0.5 | 0 | Slow, never jams |\n| Coach gun | Side | Sawn-off | 12×8 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 0.5 | Two shells |\n| Flare pistol | Side | Fire | 5 | 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | Ignites where it lands |\n| OR-7 rifle | Prim | Auto | 16 | 10 | 30 | 1.2 | 1.5 | Everywhere; enemy junk |\n| FR-2 bullpup | Prim | Auto | 18 | 12 | 25 | 0.6 | 0.5 | Dealer |\n| Pump 12 | Prim | Shotgun | 10×8 | 1.2 | 6 | 0.8 | 0.7 | |\n| Hunter .308 | Prim | Bolt | 90 | 0.8 | 5 | 0.6 | 0.5 | Scope |\n| Whisper SMG | Prim | Suppressed | 12 | 13 | 30 | 1 | 1 | Noise radius 25 |\n| \"Mother\" belt gun | Spec | LMG | 20 | 11 | 100 | 1.5 | 1.5 | Move slower |\n| Sprayer | Spec | Flame | 6/tick | – | Fuel | 1 | 0.5 | Crop sprayer on your back |\n| \"Postman\" launcher | Spec | Rocket | 150 | 0.4 | 1 | 0.5 | 0.2 | Ignites |\n| Molotov, frag | Throw | | | | 4 each | | | R1 / G |\n| Machete | Melee | | 60 | 1.4 | | | | Always carried |\n\n## 8. Story, cast, writing\n\n**Voice.** Dry, weary, literate; menace delivered politely; gallows humour with no jokes for the audience. People speak in complete\nsentences, and nobody explains the theme. Never quippy, never heroic. All speech is gibberish audio (§9.3) with subtitles, so the words on\nscreen do all the work. Keep lines short for 10-foot reading: 1–2 lines, 90 characters a line at most.\n\n### 8.1 The Auctioneer's tapes (cassettes at places; 6)\n\nSale patter, every one a \"lot\". Write in this register:\n\n> \"Lot fourteen. One rifle, Ostrava pattern, sold to the Front on Tuesday and to the Authority on Thursday. Same rifle. It has killed for\n> both and complained to neither. I find that restful. Do I hear an objection? No. There never is.\"\n\n> \"Lot twenty-two. One bridge, unfinished. The contractor was paid twice and shot once. Reserve not met.\"\n\n### 8.2 People\n\n- **Commissioner Adèle Naré**, Provisional Authority, Customs House. Precise, polite, always eating. \"You will hear that we are\n  monsters. It is true, but we keep records.\"\n- **Brother Cassius Oyelu**, Basin Front, Cinema Rex. Lay preacher; contracts as sermons. \"The Lord sends rain on the just and the unjust. I\n  send you, because you are cheaper.\"\n- **Sister Perpetua**, Mission Sainte-Claire. \"Take the bitter ones with water. If there is no water, take them anyway. God is not fussy and\n  neither is the fever.\"\n- **Madame Ferreira**, Ferreira & Daughter, General Merchants: a container at the airstrip. \"Everything I sell works. For a while. That is also\n  true of you.\"\n- **Monsieur Lazare**, clerk at the Hotel Splendide. He hands you the warrant's paperwork, and he's the Auctioneer's old colleague.\n- **The Auctioneer.** Heard everywhere, seen once: an old clerk in a rail car.\n\n### 8.3 The mercs (pick one at New Game; the others become buddies)\n\n| Merc | Who | Buddy gift | Sample line |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Ilse Brandt** | Ex-army field medic from Bremen; keeps accounts | Rescues faster | \"That is two you owe me. I write them down.\" |\n| **Tomás Arriaga** | Colombian demolitions; sings; likes fire too much | Explosive alternate plans | \"The wind is a good employee. It never asks for a raise.\" |\n| **Yaw Mensah** | Ghanaian ex-peacekeeper; the last decent man, and he resents it | Talks patrols down, holds posts | \"I came here to keep the peace. Somebody should tell it.\" |\n| **Mirela Dragan** | Romanian ex-Legion marksman; few words | Overwatch from high ground | \"Stay down.\" / \"Still alive. Disappointing for somebody.\" |\n\nThe pick screen shows four big portraits (rendered bodies, one at a time), never a stat sheet.\n\n### 8.4 Contracts (about 45–60 minutes; each 3–9 minutes)\n\n| # | Contract | Giver | What happens | Teaches |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| P | **Lot Zero** | – | Night on a barge among crates with the Auctioneer's mark. The Front lights the reeds. It burns. Wade ashore with a rusted revolver that jams. Crouch through grass past a patrol, heal, fever hits, you collapse. Your first buddy buys you from a patrol: first debt. Wake at the Mission. Sister Perpetua gives pills; Lazare's warrant names the Auctioneer | Move, grass, jam, syrette, fever, rescue, debt |\n| 1 | **Receipts** | Cassius | Steal a ledger from Km-40. Yaw's alternate: also burn the radio hut | Vehicle, map, firefight, checkpoints, standing, dealer visit |\n| 2 | **Bitter** | Perpetua | An aid truck's quinine is in a burning field; bring 3 crates before the wind turns | Fire hazard, wind, pills |\n| 3 | **The Reserve** | Naré | Destroy the Front's fuel at Pump Station with a flare from upwind. Tomás's alternate: bring the engineer out alive first | Fire as a weapon, forecast, stealth, alternate plans |\n| 4 | **Slash and Burn** | Cassius | Burn Belvédère's barns, whose crop pays the Authority. The wind shifts mid-mission toward you. Technicals arrive. Escape by patrol boat | Big burn, mounted guns, boat |\n| 5 | **Second Invoice** | A buddy | A buddy's call from Salt Works. Fight in the open white pans, no fuel to help you. They're down at the end: syrette, mercy or leave | Mercy, permadeath, ledger, overdraw |\n| 6 | **Lot One** | Lazare | The sale at Mine No. 6: both factions come to bid. Cross the fight, ride the ropeway, reach the rail car. The final tape: the last lot is you. Choose: **Serve the warrant** (shoot him; the bidding reopens Tuesday), **Buy him out** (60 stones; he flies, you get his fever cure and his ledger), or **Burn the catalogue** (light the stock with the wind toward you; the buddy who owes you most decides whether you get out) | Everything |\n\nAfter an ending: credits, then the world stays open for free roam from the title's Continue. Side content: 8 tin boxes, 6 tapes, 3 safehouses, 3 checkpoints,\n1 convoy to ambush on the east road, 1 assassination by field telephone (a pole phone call: kill the courier on the south road; pays stones).\n\n## 9. Look, animation, sound\n\n### 9.1 Art direction: the engine's native low-poly style, sun-bleached\n\n**Base style:** the engine's lit materials on simple shapes (clean look), no pixel or cel filters. **Palette:** straw `#B4985A`, red earth\n`#80543A`, laterite `#9A4E2E`, bleached sky haze `#D8C9A8`, thorn green `#7F8A3E`, rust `#8C4A22`, char `#1F1A18`, flame `#F08A24`,\nsalt `#E8E2D0`. Authority khaki with red armband and a black bar stencil; Front mismatched with blue scarves and a white triangle stencil.\n\n- **`look:dry-season`:** `sky:'sky:daylight'`, `grade` (temperature +0.18, saturation 0.9, contrast 1.08), `split` warm/teal, `vignette` 0.25,\n  `air` (haze 0.35, height 8, shafts 0.6), light `grain`. A filter stays off until it has a `scope`, so give each `scope:'all'`. Verified:\n  `sky:daylight` + `grade` over the savanna texture and thorn trees already reads as hot savanna.\n- **`look:fever`:** laid over with `post.combine`: `chroma`, `lens`, `watercolor` bleed, heavy vignette, amount driven live.\n- **Body camera and critical:** colour drain with `selective` or `grade`.\n- **Materials and textures** (generators with `tileNoise`, `cellHash`): savanna, laterite, ironstone, salt crust, road gravel, mud plaster, corrugated tin\n  (with rust streaks), sacking, painted stencil walls, tobacco leaf, canvas, gun metal, worn wood.\n- **Props to make:** trees and grass (§5), charred variants, scorch, flame patch, termite mound, boulders; mud-brick huts, tin roofs, concrete bunker, watchtower,\n  sandbags, tyre barricade, boom gate, oil drums, fuel tanks, propane, ammo and armoury crates, shipping container, water tower, power poles, pipeline, pump\n  house, conveyors, salt mounds, drying barns and racks, rail cars, ropeway, jetty, barge, plane wreck, car wrecks, faction flags, posters; vehicles (§6.7); all guns (§7);\n  syrette, pill bottle, tick-box, map, cassette player, tin box, field telephone. Engine props are fine for generic chairs, tables, lamps.\n- **Buildings** as `defineLevel` format 2 storeys on the site, tile 0.5, 2–3 interiors worth entering per place, doors with `addLevelDoors` driven by your `use` system, breakable\n  windows.\n- **Bodies** (`defineBody`, read `.cache/engine-src/labs/playground/bodies/`): four mercs, two faction soldier bodies with seeded slot variation, officers, townsfolk, Sister, Naré, Cassius,\n  Ferreira, Lazare, the Auctioneer, gazelle. Co-op armbands in the hub's seat colours.\n\n### 9.2 Animation: the engine's system plus new work\n\nAuthor with `defineAction` (`node x new action`), checked by `actionCheck`. Effector targets are `[forward, right, up]` metres from the shoulder centre; set them low and about 0.45 m forward\nfor body-camera moments.\n\n- **Player:** `syrette`, `pill`, `surgery-dig`, `surgery-finger`, `surgery-burn`, `jam-clear`, `reload-rifle`, `reload-pistol` (for shoulder view and others to see), `repair`,\n  `drive`, `gunner`, `map-hold`, `use-low`, `throw`, `machete-chop`.\n- **People:** `rescue` + `rescued` pair, `drag` + `dragged` pair, `mercy-plea`, `wave-through`, `officer-point`, `panic-burn`, `smoke-idle`, `sit-talk`, `pray`, `eat`, `jam-swear`.\n- **Library clips:** crawl (`mesh2motion/Crawl`), others by `node x anim find`. Import only the sets used, as `?raw`, to keep the file small.\n- **Procedural:** wheels, steering, suspension, mounted gun, flags turning to the wind, ragdolls on death, conveyor, gazelle gait, rocking boat.\n\n### 9.3 Audio: code only, no audio files\n\n- **Music at 10% by default:** right after `createAudio()`, `audio.volume('music', 0.1)`. The engine's default is 0.5, so this is required and tested. Stored volume wins after the player changes it.\n- **Songs (`defineSong`, original, 3–5):** sparse desert-blues over plucked pentatonic arpeggios and hand drums: Title, Roam (low and tense, intensity layers), Combat\n  (`audio.intensity` by alert state), Fever (detuned, slow), Ending. Nothing that echoes the source's score.\n- **SFX (`defineSfx`):** each gun class with distance tail (`sound` on the weapon), dry click, jam rack, reload parts, machete, grenade, rocket, flare, fire crackle in three sizes, flare-up whoosh,\n  barrel explosion, cook-off pops, engines by rpm (pitch on a loop), gears, skid, wrench, car door, boat, footsteps by surface (`SURFACE_STEPS`, add grass rustle), wind by speed, insects day\n  and night, thunder, rain, tick-box click, tape hiss and clunk, syrette, pill rattle, surgery wince, heartbeat, UI cues.\n- **Voices (`sounds/voice.ts`):** Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Turn each line's text into syllables by hashing its words; each syllable is a very short formant-filtered voice (`defineSfx` per vowel and\n  consonant class, or direct Web Audio on `audio.context`) with per-character base pitch, rate and vibrato; play in sequence on the `ui` bus while the subtitle types out. NPC barks use positional\n  syllable bursts. Never real words.\n- **Mix:** `room` reverb for interiors, `duck` during dialogue, `update(pose, queries)` each frame for 3D and occlusion. Settings sliders: Master, Music, Effects, Voices, Ambience.\n\n## 10. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n\n### 10.1 Controls\n\nEvery device gets the same game on the same screens; no desktop layout. Own action maps (`defineActionMap`, `look:true, aimWith:'centre', lock:true` for first person; a second for vehicles). Bindings rebindable with `input.listen`.\n\n| Action | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move / Look | L stick / R stick | WASD / mouse |\n| Fire / Aim | R2 / L2 | LMB / RMB |\n| Jump, mantle | Cross | Space |\n| Crouch | Circle | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the tab) |\n| Sprint | L3 | Left Shift |\n| Use (tap), Reload and clear jam (hold) | Square, `Hold:PadWest` | E, R |\n| Next weapon / holster (hold) | Triangle | 1 2 3, wheel / X |\n| Melee | R3 | V |\n| Throw | R1 | G |\n| Syrette (surgery when critical) | L1 | H |\n| Map / Tick-box / Pills / Fire-gun quick-draw | D-pad up, down, left, right | M / B / P / F |\n| Ledger | Create | L |\n| Camera view toggle | Hold Create | T |\n| Pause | Options | Esc |\n| Drive: throttle, brake, steer, handbrake, exit, seat | R2, L2, L stick, Cross, Square, Triangle | W, S, A D, Space, E, Q |\n\nIn a hub session the game ignores Options while Create is held.\n\n**Mouse is native:** pointer lock in play; in menus hover moves focus and click picks (`createMenu`; custom panels too, `createPadCursor` for pad). **Things in the world:** under lock, the crosshair is the\npointer: looking at something usable highlights it with a world-anchored label, and with no weapon out a left click uses it, as well as E.\n\n**Prompts follow the last input.** `ui/glyphs.ts`: inline SVG for PlayStation shapes (✕ ○ □ △ L1 R1 L2 R2 L3 R3 Options Create, D-pad) and Xbox (A B X Y LB RB LT RT LS RS Menu View). Pick by `input.lastDevice`: `gamepad` → PlayStation\nglyphs for any pad, or Xbox if Settings says so; keyboard → key caps and mouse icons with the actual binding (`input.bindingsFor`, `codeLabel`, `readKeyboardLayout`). Every prompt element carries `data-glyph` for tests, and they swap at once when the device changes. Verified: with a\nstubbed DualSense, `input.lastDevice` turns `gamepad`, `input.held`/`strength` work, and `input.prompt('jump')` is `Cross`.\n\n### 10.2 First person without a closed door\n\nThe default camera is `cam3=first`. For **body moments** (surgery, syrette on critical, repair, rescue from the ground) blend (`__engine.camera.set(code, { blend: true })`) to custom `cam3=body` (`defineCamera`, `followCamera`, `makePose`):\nat the eye about 0.1 m forward, pitch about −50°, body drawn whole because only `first` hides it. **Verified:** this shows the player's own sleeves, hands and gun in frame during a `defineAction`; framing needs tuning (holster the gun, arms farther out). The head's back faces don't block\nit. `cam3=driver` is the same idea with a level pitch at the driver's eye. The world keeps running throughout.\n\n### 10.3 Screens and HUD\n\n**10-foot rules:** type scales with `vh`; body text ≥ 3.2vh (34 px at 1080p), headings 6vh, subtitles 3.4vh on a dark band; 5% safe margins; one decision a screen; at most 7 visible list items; no tables of data: the dealer and ledger show one thing large, stepped with\nleft/right. System font stacks only (stencil-ish headings via `Impact, \"Arial Narrow\"`, typed notes via `\"Courier New\"`); no font files. Visual language: field notebook, stencil, carbon-copy paper, rust.\n\n**HUD (first person):** five syrette-shaped health segments, ammo and gun condition as a small rust bar, syrette and pill counts only when they change or are low; centre dot crosshair (none down the sights); goal line for 5 s when it changes; wind ribbon as per §6.5; damage arcs; prompts near centre-bottom. No\nminimap, ever.\n\n**Map in hand (`ui/map.ts`), the world doesn't pause.** A paper map on a CSS 3D layer (`perspective`, `rotateX`, slides up with an arm-raise ease, sways with the camera's turn), SVG hands gripping its edges in the merc's skin tone. Contour lines baked once to a canvas from `terrain.heights`; places as ink labels once discovered; roads, river; burn scars as hatch from fire state; an arrow for you; goal marker;\nwind arrow. R stick or pointer moves a pencil cursor, Cross or click drops a waypoint (a world-anchored marker). You walk at half speed with it up, and you can drive with it up (it sits low and to the right). The tick-box shows beside it as a small device with lamp and needle.\n\n**Screens:** Title (Continue, New Game, Co-op, Settings, Controls, About); merc pick; Pause (Resume, Map, Ledger, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About, Quit to title); Settings; Controls with rebinding (a picture of the pad and a short list); Dialogue (subtitle band with portrait name; choices as a short `createMenu`); Sleep (dawn, noon, dusk); Dealer; Ledger (a page each: debts,\nfactions, tapes, stones); Co-op lobby; Game over; Ending; Credits.\n\n**Settings:** Master, Music (10%), Effects, Voices, Ambience; Glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox); Camera (first / shoulder); FOV (`cam.fov`); mouse and stick sensitivity and invert (`input.*`), aim-assist-free; Crouch hold/toggle; Fever intensity; Screen shake; Subtitle size; Quality (`quality`); Fullscreen (`requestFullscreen`). Keep with `createStore`.\n\n### 10.4 Touch-only devices\n\nIf `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` and no pad or key has been seen: no touch controls (`touch` setting `off`, no `touchLayout`). Show a full-screen message exactly **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a **Settings** button over the attract mode, which keeps running. A pad press or key press dismisses it for good. Test with Playwright's phone profile.\n\nIf WebGPU is missing on any device, show a plain message naming a browser that has it; the engine has no WebGL fallback, and the sim still runs.\n\n## 11. Title, attract mode, dev mode, About\n\n### 11.1 Title\n\n`game.mode=title`: slow camera over the savanna at dusk with a fire line on the horizon (`cam3=fixed` or `rail`), title lettering in CSS, Title song. The view lights and shadows round the player actor, so park it near the camera's target, out of frame. Starting play sets the mode and calls `inspector.seed(n)`.\n\n### 11.2 Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 s without input** on the title or any menu off the title (keys, mouse move or click, pad buttons or sticks past deadzone all reset the timer), switch to `game.mode=attract` and restart. A page-side director (`attract.ts`) plays a loop of vignettes by placing the bot with dev actions and feeding `inspector.step(1, botIntents)` on a paused clock, with cheats on (`game.god`, infinite ammo; teleporting\nand scripted fires are fine). Each runs 15–25 s with a banner: title + \"Press any button\":\n\n1. Chase camera: a technical tearing down the road at dusk. 2. First person: firefight at Km-40. 3. Flare into grass; wind carries it; soldiers panic. 4. A jam at the worst moment, cleared. 5. Fever attack with mirages, pill. 6. Down, buddy rescue, ledger line. 7. Map in hand and tick-box, finding a tin box. 8. Boat with mounted gun past the burning estate. 9. Dealer and tape caption, then loop.\n\nCamera and look change per vignette (`__engine.camera.set`). **Any input exits at once** to the title (restart). It runs on touch-only devices too, and off-line: nothing is fetched. Never start it when automation should test the title unless asked: a setting `game.attract=auto|off|on` for tests.\n\n### 11.3 Dev mode: Pause → Dev Mode (not in hub sessions)\n\nPad and mouse friendly, big rows, one category at a time:\n\n- **Balance:** live sliders on `scenes/settings.ts`, each with its value and a per-row and global **Reset to defaults**: wear per shot, jam multiplier, player damage, enemy damage, enemy accuracy, reaction, sight, hearing, attackers, respawn hours; fire spread, wind bias, burn time, fire damage, regrow; wind speed, shift interval; fever interval, severity; HP, regen, syrette heal; car engine, grip, spring, damper; prices, stone payouts; day length; `movement.*`. Settings use `when:'now'` and systems read them at each use. `__engine.set` applies a value; reset writes each default from the table back the same way.\n- **Cheats:** god, infinite ammo, no wear/jam, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip, one-shot kills.\n- **Teleport:** every place, the crosshair point, a chosen map point.\n- **Spawn:** any gun with chosen condition, vehicle, squad, buddy, tin box.\n- **World:** hour, time scale (`time.scale`), wind dial, rain, ignite at crosshair, burn all, regrow all, fever now.\n- **Story:** jump to any contract or step, set flags, debts, standing, give stones.\n- **Debug overlays:** fire grid, AI state labels (`engine.ui.label`), detection meters, nav paths; `__engine.stats()` numbers; digest; quick save/load.\n\nSliders survive across resume, not across New Game unless \"Keep\" is on.\n\n### 11.4 About/Credits\n\nReachable from title and pause; pad and mouse scrollable pages. Pages: Source Information (all fields in TASK.md), Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Credits (engine, three.js, Rapier, @stdlib, motion clips per `data/anim/SOURCES.md`, source note: \"inspired by Far Cry 2, not affiliated\"). **One source of truth:** `scripts/bundle.mjs` reads the exit-interview file and injects it as data, so the screen and the file can't differ. Usage reads literally \"added on import\".\n\n## 12. Multiplayer\n\n**Decision: `shared-world`, host-sequenced deterministic lockstep.** The engine's one superpower is bit-exact determinism, so instead of replicating fire cells, ragdolls and NPCs, every copy runs the same scene from the same seed, and the host sequences everyone's input. No per-entity networking code.\n\n**Verified end to end:** a probe with this recipe passes the real harness in all four of its configurations, each listed in §13; four copies computed identical digests at the same step despite 150 ms latency, jitter and 5% loss; the `server` copy ran `createHeadless` in the browser, with no WebGPU.\n\n### 12.1 The mode: **Contract Run** (`game.mode=contract`)\n\n1–4 mercs, about 5 minutes, in the Pump Station region: reach the depot, burn it (flare, sprayer or charges at 3 points, all driven by wind), survive the counter-attack, get out by the river boat or pickups. Revive teammates (hold use 3 s; bleed-out 40 s). Friendly fire and friendly fire-fire are on. All down, or time up without getting out: team loses. `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })`: score = objective 500 + kills 50 + rescues 150 + extracted 200 − downs 100 − teammates burned 200; awards like \"Best employee of the wind\". The hub deals by these tags:\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Burn the depot, then get out alive together\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick or WASD moves, R2 or click fires, Square or E uses\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n\nSolo in-hub (1 seat) still works. Names and colours come from `info.players`; set names with `textContent`, armbands by seat colour. No chat, emotes or custom names, no `alert`, no new tabs, no menus before the round, and pause opens only Settings without stopping the sim. Quit does nothing.\n\n### 12.2 The session flow (order matters)\n\n1. `session.js` is the first script after `<meta charset>`, unmodified (bundler does this).\n2. In `main.ts`, first thing: `if (AIHub.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. `null` means play on as standalone.\n3. Start: `createEngine` with `search: ?seed=${info.seed}&game.mode=contract&game.seats=${n}&game.me=${info.me}&cam3=first&gfx.warmUp=asked`. **`gfx.warmUp=asked` is required:** with the default `all`, four copies sharing one main thread blocked past the deadlines. On a software adapter also lower `game.detail` (one fixed value across copies; pass through the host if adapters differ, or simply use a fixed contract-mode density).\n4. **Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the sim exists, not when the first frame draws.** Poll `typeof window.__engine?.step === 'function'` every 20 ms (reached in about 1 s); then `__engine.pause()`, start the pump, `ready()`. The harness allows all copies 20 s, and rendering took 5–25 s on software WebGPU with 4 frames; the view catches up by itself.\n5. **The pump:** a 16 ms `setInterval` alone passes the harness (verified); once frames flow, step from `onFrame` for smooth motion, and keep the timer for when frames stop. All copies run on the paused clock through `inspector.step`. **While paused, the camera still turns with mouse and stick** (verified: look is view state), so aim feels immediate on every copy.\n6. `AIHub.server`: no engine. `createHeadless({ scene, seed, settings: { 'game.seats': n, 'game.me': -1, 'game.mode': 'contract' } })`, pump on the timer, call `finish`. If `navigator.gpu` is missing on a playing copy: `AIHub.fail('WebGPU is required')`.\n7. `time-up` → host `finish` at once from its handler. `end` → stop input, stop sound (`audio.mute(true)`), stop stepping, send nothing. Host leaving voids the round by protocol; do nothing special.\n\n### 12.3 The lockstep core (`net/lockstep.ts`)\n\n```ts\nconst TURN = 4;                         // steps a turn: 15 messages a second, under the hub's 20\n// Local wire, rebuilt each frame in onFrame from engine.input (held/strength), frame.camera (yaw, pitch) and an aim ray:\n//   { m:[x,z], l:[yaw,pitch], a:[x,y,z], b:[...buttons pressed or held since last sent] }   rounded to 3 decimals\n// client, every 66 ms:  net.send({ k:'i', w: wire }, { to: host, reliable: true })\n// host, every 66 ms, ONE message however many turns are due (a burst per turn breaks the rate limit; verified):\n//   const due = Math.floor(net.time() / (1000 / 60));\n//   const n = Math.min(Math.floor((due - sent) / TURN), 30); if (n > 0) {\n//     latest[me] = wire; const f = { k:'f', s: sent, n, i: { ...latest }, x: seatEvents };\n//     net.send(f, { reliable: true }); queue.push(f); sent += TURN * n; }\n// every copy: for each frame in order, for each of TURN*n steps, when due:\n//   engine.step(1, { ...toIntents(f.i[me]), 'game:seats': othersAsIntents(f.i, me), 'game:events': f.x });\n// Playout: run max(1, dt*60) steps a frame while frames wait, up to 12 when far behind, so motion is smooth at 60 Hz.\n```\n\n**Rules that keep copies identical:**\n\n- **Everything the sim sees comes through the host's frames.** A `leave` event, a pick in a dialogue, a revive: all are host-sequenced (`x`, `game:events`, or the wire). Never feed a local `leave` straight to the sim: copies hear it at different times.\n- `game.me` differs per copy, so `actor.player` differs, so **`engine.hash()` differs across copies by design**. Compare `digest.ts` (seats, NPCs, vehicles' positions and HP, fire state counts, as a string) instead. Clients send `{ k:'d', s, h }` every 2 s; the host logs mismatches and shows a small \"out of sync\" note; tests fail on it. No resync: `capture()` is far too big, and determinism holds by construction.\n- Keep sim settings identical across copies (from the host via URL), dev mode off, and sanitize wire data (finite numbers, known buttons) before it reaches intents: `normalizeIntents` throws on junk.\n- A tap shorter than a turn must survive: OR presses into `b` until the wire is sent.\n\n### 12.4 The game on its own\n\nOutside the hub, Title → Co-op runs the same Contract Run with no server, through the same `Net` interface (`send`, `on('message')`, `time`, `players`, `isHost`):\n\n- **`net/tabs.ts`: \"Same computer\":** `BroadcastChannel`; host lists itself, others join; a second tab, window or screen. Verified from `file://` between two pages.\n- **`net/rtc.ts`: \"Invite code\":** one `RTCPeerConnection` and ordered data channel per guest (star on the host), non-trickle ICE, `iceServers:[{urls:'stun:stun.l.google.com:19302'}]`, base64 of the description as a copy-and-paste code with a Copy button and a Paste field: host's code to guest, guest's reply to host. Verified from `file://` in two separate browser contexts with no STUN: connects in 0.3 s with 650-byte descriptions.\n\nUse the hub's seat colours and a local 3 s countdown. Rule: none of this runs while `AIHub.active` (network only through the hub).\n\n### 12.5 Own card\n\nBecause the game has its own world, use `card: true`: HTML/CSS card over the loading scene showing the game's name, players in colours with ready ticks, how to win, this player's controls, time left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross or a click: `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle, a named key or a click: `AIHub.answer('more')`. No menus; nothing changes the round. Play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`, after `start`.\n\n## 13. Testing\n\n**One command:** `node tests/game/verify.mjs [sim|page|hub]` (add `\"verify\"` to `package.json`). It prints only failures and a final one-line count (`verify: 212 passed, 0 failed`). Vitest with `--reporter=json` and parsed. Rerun a tier only after changing what it covers. Screenshots only for what a script can't judge; save them in `out/`. Keep one or two browsers open at a time. Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n| Tier | What it proves |\n|---|---|\n| **sim** (Vitest, Node; seconds to minutes) | Starter's four kinds kept: golden replay (1), capture/restore, bot, rules. Wear lowers condition and swaps tier ids; jam rate at given conditions over many shots; clearing works. HP, regen, syrette, surgery, down, rescue, debt, overdraw. Fever timeline, pills, collapse. **Fire front metric** (§6.5), firebreaks hold, embers jump, rain stops it, regrowth. Wind shifts on schedule with forecast. Stealth: same patrol detects standing in the open and misses crouched in grass; burned grass exposes. AI squad clears cover and flanks; jam window. Checkpoint repopulation; holstered pass with standing. Vehicle: drives a route, stays on terrain, repairs, explodes; `placeActor` seat; run-over. Economy purchases, caches, armoury. Save → reload → same state fields. Contract engine: every contract and alt completes by script. **Lockstep digest:** 1, 2, 4 headless copies with different `game.me` fed the same frames keep equal digests over 3,600 steps with a fight, a fire and a car in them. |\n| **Whole-game playthrough** (sim) | `bot.ts` completes prologue through every ending on seeds 1–3 with `game.god`, through intents only, using teleport-free travel for contract 1 and dev travel after. One honest run: bot clears Km-40 without god on at least 7 of 10 seeds, as a balance alarm. |\n| **page** (Playwright on the deliverable over `file://`) | Boots `ready` with no errors. Title → attract at 10 s; any key, mouse or pad input exits it (virtual clock not needed; use `game.attract` and a short setting for the wait, and one real 10 s test). Keyboard-only and pad-only (stubbed `navigator.getGamepads`) routes from title to first control. Prompts swap device on input; Xbox option; `data-glyph` values. Music bus reads 0.1 at first run; volume persists. `renderSong`, `renderSfx` and an `OfflineAudioContext` run of a voice line produce non-silent, unclipped audio (`node x qa audio`). Pause and Dev Mode: a slider changes behaviour, reset restores. Map opens without pausing the tick count. Mouse hover moves menu focus. About matches the exit-interview file. Phone profile shows the exact touch message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract running. WebKit and Firefox have no WebGPU here, so Chromium only; say so. |\n| **hub** | Fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` to `.cache/hub/`; copy the deliverable beside them; serve on an OS-picked 127.0.0.1 port; confirm the page marker. All must give `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` (`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` when finished): `players=2`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; the same with `scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`; all with `&auto=1`. Launch args include the WebGPU flags of §2. Then standalone: same deliverable alone, solo; two pages over tabs link; two contexts over invite codes, digests equal. |\n| **look** (rare) | `node x shot` numbers and `node x gallery prop` for art; 1920×1080 screenshots of each UI screen for the 10-foot judgement. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot; check state instead when it does. |\n\n**Not checkable here; say so in your feedback:** real GPUs, real pads, speakers, cross-machine determinism, iOS.\n\n## 14. Build order\n\nBuild a walking skeleton first, then keep the deliverable working at every step. Run `npm run check` and the relevant `verify` tier before moving on.\n\n| # | Do | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | §2 setup. Pick the title as TASK.md says (brainstorm silently, real RNG), into `title.ts`. Write `scripts/bundle.mjs` (§15.1), `fetch-hub.mjs`, `verify.mjs` skeleton. Add hub metas and a stub session | One-file loads over `file://`; harness passes with the starter + stub |\n| 1 | Site, terrain, river, roads, scatter, looks, day cycle; `movement:merc`; `seats.ts`; action maps; first person; HUD shell | Walk the map in first person; prompts follow device |\n| 2 | `arms.ts`, wear and jam, `health.ts`, one gun, Rifleman, perception, Km-40. **Now `lockstep.ts` + digest test + `net/hub.ts`**, so co-op stays honest from here | Bot clears Km-40; digests equal; harness passes with guns |\n| 3 | Fire, wind, flare, grass burning, scars, panic | Fire metric test; looks like fire in a shot |\n| 4 | Vehicles, driver AI, patrols, repair, boat, mounted guns | Bot drives a route; vehicle tests |\n| 5 | Fever, buddies, ledger, stones, tick-box, dealer, safehouses, saves, rest of the guns and enemy types | Tier tests green |\n| 6 | Contract engine, all story content, dialogue, voices, tapes, map in hand, endings | Playthrough bot finishes the game |\n| 7 | Contract Run, own card, tabs and invite links | Full hub tier green |\n| 8 | Title, pause, settings, controls, dev mode, attract, touch notice, About | Page tier green |\n| 9 | Art, animation, audio passes across everything; balance by sliders and bot | No placeholder boxes or stand-ins anywhere; a search for TODO, FIXME, placeholder finds nothing |\n| 10 | Finish: §15 | All below |\n\n## 15. Finish line\n\n### 15.1 Packaging: `scripts/bundle.mjs` (verified: 6.7 MB, loads from `file://`, harness passes)\n\n```js\nimport { build } from 'vite'; import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'; import { join } from 'node:path';\nconst root = process.cwd();\nconst result = await build({ root, configFile: false, logLevel: 'warn', base: './',\n  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\n  build: { write: false, modulePreload: false, cssCodeSplit: false, assetsInlineLimit: () => true, chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\n    rollupOptions: { input: { game: join(root, 'labs/game/index.html') }, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } } } });\nconst files = {}; let html;\nfor (const item of [result].flat().flatMap((o) => o.output)) {\n  const text = item.type === 'chunk' ? item.code : typeof item.source === 'string' ? item.source : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\n  if (item.fileName.endsWith('.html')) html = text; else files[item.fileName] = text; }\nconst find = (ref) => files[Object.keys(files).find((f) => ref.endsWith('/' + f) || ref === f || ref === './' + f)];\nhtml = html.replace(/<script type=\"module\" crossorigin src=\"([^\"]+)\"><\\/script>|<link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"([^\"]+)\">/g, (_t, s, c) => {\n  if (c) return `<style>${find(c)}</style>`;\n  const code = find(s).replaceAll('</script', '<\\\\/script');\n  if (code.includes('<!--')) throw new Error('script holds <!--: split it in the source');\n  return `<script type=\"module\">${code}</script>`; });\nconst session = readFileSync('.cache/hub/session.js', 'utf8'); // the unmodified client: scripts/fetch-hub.mjs downloads it\nhtml = html.replace('<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />', () => `<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\\n<script>${session}</script>\\n${HUB_METAS}`);\nwriteFileSync(DELIVERABLE, html); // DELIVERABLE: the name your TASK.md gives, in '..'; inject the exit-interview file as data too\n```\n\n`fetch-hub.mjs` downloads `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `.cache/hub/`, where lint and format can't touch them: the client must stay byte-identical. The protocol's full text is `README.md` at the same address; read it once. Everything in the deliverable is inline, so nothing depends on a CDN.\n\n### 15.2 Your own feedback\n\nKeep `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` current as AGENTS.md asks. Starting points, if they bite you too: arms rig closed to games; weapons, melee and use only for the `player` actor; no scene access for game meshes (raw geometry through `.constructor` is a hack); TASK.md's browser flags vs the engine's; `capture` size; `setup.sh` downloads outside the folder; one scene per page. Don't patch the engine (it stays read-only); `npm run check` proves it. Keep `labs/game/README.md` true: what the game is, how it plays, the calls you made.\n\n### 15.3 Exit interview\n\nWrite the exit-interview file in exactly the shape your TASK.md gives, with honest counts from your testing. Suggested catalogue values: genre `Shooter`, type `Game`, source `Far Cry 2`, series `Far Cry`, players `1–4`, tags from `3d, first-person, co-op, vehicles, exploration, low-poly`. Plan field: `PLAN.md`. Research: engine and hub source reading, this plan's verified probes, plus whatever you did. Validate with `JSON.parse`, rebuild so About shows it, and put Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in your final chat reply too, using \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm, and Usage as \"added on import\". Say plainly what you did not verify.\n\n### 15.4 Coverage: TASK.md → this plan\n\n| TASK.md item | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Genre, perspective | §1 |\n| Title: riff, 50 brainstormed, real RNG | §14 step 0 (your job; `title.ts`) |\n| Research: your choice | Done for engine and hub (§2, §3, §12); add your own if you wish, and report it |\n| Single HTML in root, dev files in subfolder | §15.1 |\n| Full workspace; engine read-only; add systems, art, animations on top | §2, §3, §15.2 |\n| Art direction, animation | §9.1, §9.2, §10.2 |\n| Audio: code only, gibberish voices, music 10% | §9.3, §13 page tier |\n| Online and multiplayer: hub and on its own | §12 |\n| Shared machine: ports, PIDs, files, browsers | §2, §13 |\n| Performance unlimited, FPS out of scope | §5 (`game.detail` default 1 and only for tests and software adapters) |\n| Testing: headless, one command, failures and count, playthrough, screenshots rarely, no debate agents | §13 |\n| Stand-ins: pad, touch, audio, second player, 1080p | §13 |\n| Feature-complete demo; distinctive world, characters, themes, tone | §1, §5, §6, §8 |\n| Infrastructure for later content with normal tools | §4, §6.10 |\n| Dev mode from pause, sliders, reset | §11.3 |\n| Attract mode at 10 s, looping, cheats, any input exits | §11.2 |\n| Narrative tone | §8 |\n| 10-foot, controller first, native keyboard and mouse, hover focus, world clicks, prompts by last input, PS glyphs with Xbox option, no dense screens | §10 |\n| Touch-only: message, settings button, attract runs | §10.4 |\n| No TODOs or stubs | §0, §14 step 9 |\n| Source Information, feedback in chat and About; the exit-interview file | §11.4, §15.3 |\n","numLines":393,"startLine":420,"totalLines":812}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RqFo2yXEs9LFjQQsnHyT7D","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
