{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEXNsFBeL314d4VzfAm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KPrGJ1t8gz7ZHGXYWAAcxx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:80]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n\n# Map edge.\nrep('''70–120 m high (`hills` round the edge, plus a sim rule that turns back anything past 1450 m from centre) keeps you in;\nthe terrain ends at the edge, and a vehicle will fall off it (verified), so the rule must hold.''',\n'''70–120 m high (`hills` round the edge, plus a sim rule that turns back anything within 40 m of the edge) keeps you in;\nthe terrain simply ends there, and a vehicle will fall off it (verified), so the rule must hold.''')\n\n# Original-work rule vs real-country mercs.\nrep('''Don't call the game a\nsequel. Portray the invented country's people as people: named characters on every side, with no real nation, ethnic\ngroup or leader named or caricatured.''','''Don't call the game a\nsequel. The country, its war and its factions are invented: no real conflict, ethnic group or leader is named or caricatured,\nand its people are written as individuals on every side. The hired mercs come from real countries and are written as individuals too.''')\n\n# describe.\nrep('''| Data as a tool | `defineKind`/`def` for contracts, places, squads, dealer stock | `node x describe contract` then lists them for designers |''',\n'''| Data as a tool | `defineKind`/`def` for contracts, places, squads, dealer stock | Schemas check entries; `__engine.describe('contract')` lists them for designers |''')\n\n# Jam and wear numbers.\nrep('''- **Wear:** each shot `condition -= game.wear.perShot × weapon.wear`. Dust storms and fire ×2.\n- **Jam:** per shot, `p = game.wear.jamK × max(0, 0.65 − condition)²  × weapon.jamRate`. Jam: dry click, gun won't fire,\n  prompt shows.''','''- **Wear:** each shot `condition -= game.wear.perShot (0.0012) × weapon.wear`, ×2 near fire. A new OR-7 stays jam-free for about 240 shots.\n- **Jam:** per shot, `p = 0.25 × game.wear.jamK (1) × max(0, 0.65 − condition)² × weapon.jamRate`: about 0.6% at condition 0.5, 2.6% at 0.33,\n  6% at 0.15, before `jamRate`. Jam: dry click, gun won't fire, prompt shows.''')\n\n# Fire table and spread, calibrated.\nrep('''| Dry grass (north) | 0.10 | 8 | Removes grass patches, leaves scorch props |\n| Green grass (south) | 0.04 | 8 | |\n| Brush | 0.07 | 14 | |\n| Tree | 0.03 | 40 | Becomes a charred tree prop. Throws embers |\n| Building, barn, racks | 0.05 | 60 | Roof and walls swap to charred props |''','''| Dry grass (north) | 0.016 | 8 | Removes grass patches, leaves scorch props |\n| Green grass (south) | 0.008 | 8 | Often dies out by itself in light wind |\n| Brush | 0.012 | 14 | |\n| Tree | 0.005 | 40 | Becomes a charred tree prop. Throws embers |\n| Building, barn, racks | 0.008 | 60 | Roof and walls swap to charred props |''')\nrep('''cos(angle to wind))`, floored at `0.15 × base`, × 1.4 uphill, × 0 in rain. **Embers:** a burning tree in wind ≥ 8 m/s has a 1% per\ntick chance to ignite a cell 2–5 cells downwind, which jumps roads. **Target (a test):** on dry grass with 5 m/s wind a fire front runs\n≥ 60 m downwind in 30 s and ≤ 25 m upwind. Slower than a sprint, faster than a crouch.''','''cos(angle to wind))`, floored at `0.15 × base`, × 0.7 on diagonals, × 1.4 uphill, × 0 in rain. Front speed is very sensitive to\n`base`, because each cell has several burning neighbours: 0.10 gave 19 m/s when this rule was simulated outside the engine, and 0.016 gave the\nfigures below. **Embers:** a burning tree in wind ≥ 8 m/s has a 1% per tick chance to ignite a cell 2–5 cells downwind, which jumps roads.\n**Targets (a test), simulated on dry grass in 30 s:** 5 m/s wind: 90–140 m downwind (3.8 m/s), ≤ 25 m upwind, about 60 m each flank. No wind: about\n60 m all round. 10 m/s wind: about 150 m. So it outruns a crouch (2.0 m/s) and never a sprint (6.4 m/s).''')\n\n# Vehicles: define side.\nrep('''- lateral grip `−side × (1400/4) × 2.2 / 0.35`, drive `throttle × 7800 / 4`, both clamped to ±`F × 1.1`; front wheels turn by\n  `steer × 0.5` rad;''','''- lateral grip `−side × (1400/4) × 2.2 / 0.35`, with `side` = point velocity · wheel right; drive `throttle × 7800 / 4`; both clamped to\n  ±`F × 1.1`; on the front wheels, right and forward are turned by `steer × 0.5` rad;''')\n\n# Holstered fists tip.\nrep('''`cam3=driver` is the same idea with a level pitch at the driver's eye. The world keeps running throughout.\n''','''`cam3=driver` is the same idea with a level pitch at the driver's eye. The world keeps running throughout.\n\nWith the gun holstered, the `first` rig shows raised fists. Where that looks wrong (the ceasefire town), a level `cam3=walk` of the same kind drops the hands out of frame; it must take `input.look` and `input.turn` as `first` does (not verified).\n''')\n\n# Own card: not verified, safe fallback.\nrep('''No menus; nothing changes the round. Play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`, after `start`.''','''No menus; nothing changes the round. Play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`, after `start`. The harness tests this by dispatching an Enter `keydown` in the frame, so listen on `window`. The probe ran with `card: false`, which passes; the own card itself isn't verified, so if it fights you late in the build, fall back to the hub's card with the tags above.''')\n\n# game:events once.\nrep('''//   engine.step(1, { ...toIntents(f.i[me]), 'game:seats': othersAsIntents(f.i, me), 'game:events': f.x });''','''//   engine.step(1, { ...toIntents(f.i[me]), 'game:seats': othersAsIntents(f.i, me), ...(first ? { 'game:events': f.x } : {}) });''')\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf8').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"1450\\|0\\.10 \\|for designers\\|first ?\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-120","description":"Apply calibrated numbers and review fixes to the plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2289,"cache_read_input_tokens":620050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2289},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"d56e5a5e-9f72-47c9-b1ca-aa741f198909","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:32:38.308Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEXNaPGbJ9hQfFZe4iH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KPrGJ1t8gz7ZHGXYWAAcxx":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211932__xd07c4f/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:80]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n\n# Map edge.\nrep('''70–120 m high (`hills` round the edge, plus a sim rule that turns back anything past 1450 m from centre) keeps you in;\nthe terrain ends at the edge, and a vehicle will fall off it (verified), so the rule must hold.''',\n'''70–120 m high (`hills` round the edge, plus a sim rule that turns back anything within 40 m of the edge) keeps you in;\nthe terrain simply ends there, and a vehicle will fall off it (verified), so the rule must hold.''')\n\n# Original-work rule vs real-country mercs.\nrep('''Don't call the game a\nsequel. Portray the invented country's people as people: named characters on every side, with no real nation, ethnic\ngroup or leader named or caricatured.''','''Don't call the game a\nsequel. The country, its war and its factions are invented: no real conflict, ethnic group or leader is named or caricatured,\nand its people are written as individuals on every side. The hired mercs come from real countries and are written as individuals too.''')\n\n# describe.\nrep('''| Data as a tool | `defineKind`/`def` for contracts, places, squads, dealer stock | `node x describe contract` then lists them for designers |''',\n'''| Data as a tool | `defineKind`/`def` for contracts, places, squads, dealer stock | Schemas check entries; `__engine.describe('contract')` lists them for designers |''')\n\n# Jam and wear numbers.\nrep('''- **Wear:** each shot `condition -= game.wear.perShot × weapon.wear`. Dust storms and fire ×2.\n- **Jam:** per shot, `p = game.wear.jamK × max(0, 0.65 − condition)²  × weapon.jamRate`. Jam: dry click, gun won't fire,\n  prompt shows.''','''- **Wear:** each shot `condition -= game.wear.perShot (0.0012) × weapon.wear`, ×2 near fire. A new OR-7 stays jam-free for about 240 shots.\n- **Jam:** per shot, `p = 0.25 × game.wear.jamK (1) × max(0, 0.65 − condition)² × weapon.jamRate`: about 0.6% at condition 0.5, 2.6% at 0.33,\n  6% at 0.15, before `jamRate`. Jam: dry click, gun won't fire, prompt shows.''')\n\n# Fire table and spread, calibrated.\nrep('''| Dry grass (north) | 0.10 | 8 | Removes grass patches, leaves scorch props |\n| Green grass (south) | 0.04 | 8 | |\n| Brush | 0.07 | 14 | |\n| Tree | 0.03 | 40 | Becomes a charred tree prop. Throws embers |\n| Building, barn, racks | 0.05 | 60 | Roof and walls swap to charred props |''','''| Dry grass (north) | 0.016 | 8 | Removes grass patches, leaves scorch props |\n| Green grass (south) | 0.008 | 8 | Often dies out by itself in light wind |\n| Brush | 0.012 | 14 | |\n| Tree | 0.005 | 40 | Becomes a charred tree prop. Throws embers |\n| Building, barn, racks | 0.008 | 60 | Roof and walls swap to charred props |''')\nrep('''cos(angle to wind))`, floored at `0.15 × base`, × 1.4 uphill, × 0 in rain. **Embers:** a burning tree in wind ≥ 8 m/s has a 1% per\ntick chance to ignite a cell 2–5 cells downwind, which jumps roads. **Target (a test):** on dry grass with 5 m/s wind a fire front runs\n≥ 60 m downwind in 30 s and ≤ 25 m upwind. Slower than a sprint, faster than a crouch.''','''cos(angle to wind))`, floored at `0.15 × base`, × 0.7 on diagonals, × 1.4 uphill, × 0 in rain. Front speed is very sensitive to\n`base`, because each cell has several burning neighbours: 0.10 gave 19 m/s when this rule was simulated outside the engine, and 0.016 gave the\nfigures below. **Embers:** a burning tree in wind ≥ 8 m/s has a 1% per tick chance to ignite a cell 2–5 cells downwind, which jumps roads.\n**Targets (a test), simulated on dry grass in 30 s:** 5 m/s wind: 90–140 m downwind (3.8 m/s), ≤ 25 m upwind, about 60 m each flank. No wind: about\n60 m all round. 10 m/s wind: about 150 m. So it outruns a crouch (2.0 m/s) and never a sprint (6.4 m/s).''')\n\n# Vehicles: define side.\nrep('''- lateral grip `−side × (1400/4) × 2.2 / 0.35`, drive `throttle × 7800 / 4`, both clamped to ±`F × 1.1`; front wheels turn by\n  `steer × 0.5` rad;''','''- lateral grip `−side × (1400/4) × 2.2 / 0.35`, with `side` = point velocity · wheel right; drive `throttle × 7800 / 4`; both clamped to\n  ±`F × 1.1`; on the front wheels, right and forward are turned by `steer × 0.5` rad;''')\n\n# Holstered fists tip.\nrep('''`cam3=driver` is the same idea with a level pitch at the driver's eye. The world keeps running throughout.\n''','''`cam3=driver` is the same idea with a level pitch at the driver's eye. The world keeps running throughout.\n\nWith the gun holstered, the `first` rig shows raised fists. Where that looks wrong (the ceasefire town), a level `cam3=walk` of the same kind drops the hands out of frame; it must take `input.look` and `input.turn` as `first` does (not verified).\n''')\n\n# Own card: not verified, safe fallback.\nrep('''No menus; nothing changes the round. Play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`, after `start`.''','''No menus; nothing changes the round. Play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`, after `start`. The harness tests this by dispatching an Enter `keydown` in the frame, so listen on `window`. The probe ran with `card: false`, which passes; the own card itself isn't verified, so if it fights you late in the build, fall back to the hub's card with the tags above.''')\n\n# game:events once.\nrep('''//   engine.step(1, { ...toIntents(f.i[me]), 'game:seats': othersAsIntents(f.i, me), 'game:events': f.x });''','''//   engine.step(1, { ...toIntents(f.i[me]), 'game:seats': othersAsIntents(f.i, me), ...(first ? { 'game:events': f.x } : {}) });''')\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf8').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"1450\\|0\\.10 \\|for designers\\|first ?\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-120","description":"Apply calibrated numbers and review fixes to the plan"}}}
