{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEcd1wTRQmYHb4zhwVx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` is written and ends with a table mapping each `TASK.md` requirement to its section; `planner-exit-interview.json` is saved with all four answers and parses as valid JSON. I made no commits and deleted my scratch clones and test code.\n\n**The game:** an open-world first-person mercenary game set in an invented country at the end of its dry season. You're there to serve a warrant on the Auctioneer, an arms dealer selling to both sides of a civil war.\n- **Carried over from the source:** fire spread by wind, guns that wear out and jam, recurring fever, buddies who rescue you, and a map held in your hands.\n- **Original:** all names, characters, story and art. As `STAGE.md` asks, builders choose the title.\n\n**Tested on this machine:**\n- **Co-op:** the host orders everyone's inputs and each copy runs the same simulation, so no per-object networking is needed. It passed all four hub harness scenarios: 2 players, 4 players on a bad network, the host leaving, and a server-hosted round. Copies stayed in sync at the steps I compared.\n- **Packaging:** the starter game bundles into one HTML file of about 6.7 MB that loads from `file://`.\n- **Vehicles:** a jeep with simulated suspension drives over terrain with a seated driver at 0.32 ms per step, and a replay gives the identical hash.\n- **Playing without the hub:** browser-tab and WebRTC links both work between pages opened from `file://`.\n- **Fire and jams:** my first fire values spread about five times too fast, so I recalibrated them in a simulation outside the engine. I set the jam rates by calculation, so they haven't been run in play.\n\n**Problems the plan warns builders about:**\n- The WebGPU flags in `TASK.md` fail with this engine (it never reaches ready); the plan gives flags that work.\n- The engine's weapon, melee and use systems only serve the player actor, so calling them would break co-op.\n- Game code can't reach the 3D scene, and first-person arms can't be posed; the plan gives workarounds for both.\n\n**Marked \"not verified\" in the plan or left for builders to test:**\n- the game's own pre-round card, with a tested fallback to the hub's card\n- the body that stops people walking through parked cars\n- the lowered-gun reload trick\n- the holstered first-person camera\n\nReal GPUs, real controllers, speakers and sync across different machines can't be checked here, and the plan tells builders to say so.\n\nEverything is in the `work` folder:\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `planner-exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4479,"cache_read_input_tokens":625977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4479},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"3dddf940-2f74-4a00-93f3-2e391897e4fd","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:33:34.241Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEccjZYMdt9anu7185Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: PLAN.md covers everything TASK.md asks for.]: PLAN.md exists and maps every TASK.md requirement, but the stage instructions in STAGE.md were not fully followed: STAGE.md asks for planner-exit-interview.json with answers to four specific questions, which was done, yet TASK.md also requires the exit-interview file in the exact shape it specifies (sourceInformation, testingFeedback, engineFeedback, promptFeedback, aiHub) saved beside the .html, and the deliverable itself (the single HTML file named in TASK.md) was never built. The PLAN.md itself is a plan, not the game, so 'PLAN.md covers everything TASK.md asks for' is the stated done condition; however the transcript shows the plan's own build and exit-interview steps were deferred to builders, while the plan's coverage table claims items such as the title and exit-interview shape are covered by reference rather than by PLAN.md content, and the assistant's own summary notes only partial verification."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"0e534e58-9417-4888-9f3a-3487f7375099","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:33:38.505Z","isSynthetic":true}
