{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E83q86NFqh5oGnJERgouV5","type":"tool_result","content":"Cloning into '.research/my-3dge'...\ntotal 92\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  4 22:35 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha  4096 Nov  4 22:35 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 13624 Nov  4 22:35 bridge.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 27469 Nov  4 22:35 harness.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 20248 Nov  4 22:35 round.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 16707 Nov  4 22:35 session.js\nnew-game: made the game \"probe\" in .research/wk: the engine at my-3dge@e7a1243 (2135 files, read-only, pinned by engine-lock.json) and the starter game in labs/\nadded 590 packages in 9s\ne7a1243\n9: * - **The brazier**: the fire a brazier holds, three flame tongues and its torch light, flickering; it has no body\n18: * `:436-442` (`BRAZ`'s flames: three cones 2.2 units in radius, orange `#ff7a2a` round yellow `#ffd36a` cores, 1.6\n64:      \"A brazier's fire: three flame tongues dancing on the coals and its flickering torch light. It stands on the stand the level's brazier glyph draws, under each light spot tagged torch.\",\n67:        name: 'flames',\n70:        material: 'material:flame',\n74:        flame: { tongues: 3, ring: 0.1, height: 0.4375, sway: 0.0875, core: '#ffd36a' },\n9: *   overhead; their numbers are in engine/gfx/cameras/presets.ts), turned round its target by `turn`, zoomed, fixed on\n12: *   the target's height: above the followed point, or the fixed target's y when x and z are given.\n14: * - `cam3=orbit[,<azimuth>,<elevation>,<distance>[,<x>,<y>,<z>]]`: round a target, fixed when one is given.\n15: * - `cam3=fly[,<x>,<y>,<z>,<yaw>,<pitch>[,<fov>]]` and `cam3=fixed[,…]`: a free camera and one that stays put.\n19: * along +Z, 90 along +X); pitch is + up. A bare `fly` or `fixed` starts from the camera before it.\n26: * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/40-cameras.js:266-338` (`camDesc`, `camLink`, the `?cam=` and `?cam3=`\n32: * formatCameraCode(parseCameraCode('fly,1,1.7,-4,90,-10')); // 'cam3=fly,1,1.7,-4,90,-10,70'\nengine/gfx/cameras/codes.test.ts:8:import { createFixedCamera } from './fixed';\nengine/gfx/cameras/codes.test.ts:36:  'cam3=fixed',\nengine/gfx/cameras/codes.test.ts:37:  'cam3=fixed,0,3,-6,-179.5,-17.19,50',\nengine/gfx/cameras/codes.test.ts:41:const WHOLE = CANONICAL.filter((code) => !['cam3=orbit', 'cam3=fly', 'cam3=fixed'].includes(code));\nengine/gfx/cameras/codes.test.ts:101:    const fixed = parseCameraCode('cam3=fixed,1,2,3,270,-10') as FreeSpec;\nengine/gfx/cameras/codes.test.ts:102:    expect(fixed).toMatchObject({ type: 'fixed', position: [1, 2, 3] });\nengine/gfx/cameras/codes.test.ts:103:    expect(fixed.yaw).toBeCloseTo(270 * DEG, 12);\nengine/gfx/cameras/codes.test.ts:104:    expect(formatCameraCode(fixed)).toBe('cam3=fixed,1,2,3,-90,-10,70'); // the heading wrapped, the default lens written\n14: * - `gpu`: its particles go to the GPU's ring (engine/gfx/enhanced/particles.ts) while `feature:gpuParticles` is on.\n148:  gpu: {\n152:      \"Whether its particles go to the GPU's ring while feature:gpuParticles is on (WP 11.3): for decorative ones in their thousands, rain and dust; the CPU pool takes them otherwise.\",\n33:  'emitter:smoke': {\n34-    description: 'Rising smoke that darkens, spreads and fades (shardfall).',\n35-    ...{ area: [0.2, 0.05, 0.2], velocity: [0, 0.9, 0], spread: 0.3, gravity: -0.3, drag: 0.6, turbulence: 1 },\n36-    ...{ life: [2.2, 3.6], size: [0.15, 0.75], color: ['#818186', '#b3b3b8'], alpha: [0.55, 0], additive: false },\n37-    ...{ rate: 14, count: 6 },\n38-  },\n39-  'emitter:steam': {\n40-    description: 'White steam rising fast and thinning out (shardfall).',\n41-    ...{ area: [0.15, 0.02, 0.15], velocity: [0, 1.6, 0], spread: 0.4, gravity: -0.5, drag: 1, turbulence: 1.5 },\n42-    ...{ life: [1, 1.8], size: [0.1, 0.6], color: ['#f3f6f9', '#ffffff'], alpha: [0.45, 0], additive: false },\n43-    ...{ rate: 20, count: 8 },\n44-  },\n45-  'emitter:sparks': {\n46-    description: 'Hot sparks streaking out, falling and bouncing on the floor (shardfall).',\n47-    ...{ velocity: [0, 3.5, 0], spread: 3, gravity: 9.8, drag: 0.3, life: [0.4, 1], size: [0.05, 0.015] },\n48-    ...{ color: ['#ffc171', '#ff7c3f'], brightness: [6, 2], alpha: [1, 0], stretch: true, lands: true, bounce: 0.35 },\n49-    ...{ rate: 40, count: 16 },\n--\n110:  'emitter:fire': {\n111-    description: 'Flames licking up, white-hot to red, with a flickering light (shardfall).',\n112-    ...{ area: [0.22, 0.05, 0.22], velocity: [0, 1.5, 0], spread: 0.45, gravity: -1.5, drag: 1, turbulence: 1.5 },\n113-    ...{ life: [0.45, 0.9], size: [0.3, 0.04], color: ['#ffae5e', '#ff713a'], brightness: [4, 1.2] },\n114-    ...{ alpha: [0.9, 0], rate: 70, count: 12 },\n115-    light: { color: '#ffb070', intensity: 30, distance: 10, offset: [0, 0.4, 0], flicker: 0.6 },\n116-  },\n117-} satisfies Record<string, EmitterSpec>;\n118-\n119-/** The 2D engine's particle kinds the presets lack: see the file comment. */\n120-const KINDS = {\n121-  'emitter:bits': {\n122-    description: 'Debris chips thrown up and out, bouncing on the floor (the 2D engine’s bits).',\n123-    ...{ area: [0.1, 0.2, 0.1], velocity: [0, 7.5, 0], spread: 4.7, gravity: 26.25, drag: 0.8, life: [0.7, 1.3] },\n124-    ...{ size: [0.06, 0.06], color: ['#6a5a4a', '#3a3438'], alpha: [1, 1], additive: false, lands: true },\n125-    ...{ bounce: 0.45, count: 8 },\n126-  },\n--\n156:        emitter: 'emitter:fire',\n157-        count: 45,\n158-        set: { area: [0.4, 0.4, 0.4], spread: 2.5, size: [0.35, 0.05], life: [0.25, 0.55] },\n159-      },\n160-      {\n161:        emitter: 'emitter:smoke',\n162-        count: 22,\n163-        offset: [0, 0.3, 0],\n164-        set: { area: [0.5, 0.5, 0.5], spread: 1.2, size: [0.3, 1.1] },\n165-      },\n[This command modified 14 files you've previously read: labs/playground/README.md, tools/game/template/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.tmpl, engine/app/loop.ts, lean/READ