{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TDTWzBAVoYhjEfMCiENRcv","type":"tool_result","content":"10: * Its `options` (WP 13.16, `SpawnPropOptions`): its body's type, its light (the component `propLight`, which the view\n11- * reads) and components from the start; a prop with `health` holds its hit points (`propHealth`), and nothing else\n12- * gains a component, so earlier hashes hold. `propOfBody(w, body)` is the body-to-entity lookup uses and hits read.\n13- *\n14- * `hitProp(w, id, from, knock?)` hits a prop from `from` (a swing, a blast): it calls the prop's `hit` hook with the\n15- * means to knock it, engine/physics/bodies.ts's `knock` on its body with the caller's strength (`speed`, `up`,\n16- * `spin`) under the hook's own; the default hook knocks a dynamic prop away and leaves the others. Shared code calls\n17- * the hook and never compares ids. `removeProp(w, id)` removes the entity and its body.\n18- *\n19- * The component's name is `sceneProp`, as names are global and fixtures/scenes/physics-props declares its own `prop`.\n20- * Its `x` and `z` are metres, so the stage places it, and draws it as its prop instead of a stand-in.\n21- *\n22- * Invariants: everything a prop is in the sim is its component and its body; the readback writes only what the body\n--\n97:export interface SpawnPropOptions {\n98-  /** Its body's type instead of its prop's: a broken door's leaf falls (`'dynamic'`). */\n99-  as?: 'dynamic' | 'fixed' | 'kinematic';\n100-  /** Whether it is on at first, and its light group: either makes it switchable (`propLight`). */\n101-  on?: boolean;\n102-  group?: string;\n103-  /** More components its entity holds from the start (a door's `door`, a switch's `switch`). */\n104-  components?: Readonly<Record<string, object>>;\n105-  /** Its body knocked away from `from` as it is made (a broken prop's pieces: engine/physics/bodies.ts's `knock`). */\n106-  knock?: PropKnock & { from: readonly [number, number, number] 