{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjGHa5XChxjLByVs7BgJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Uoxf3GTzPHvx7NMPrmrHkz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\na='''- **Your TASK.md wins** over this plan on anything it states. §15 maps each TASK.md requirement to the section here.'''\nb='''- **Your TASK.md wins** over this plan on anything it states. §15.4 maps each TASK.md requirement to the section here that states it.'''\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b,1)\na='''- **Headless shell only.** Playwright's default headless works.'''\nb='''- **WebGPU needs a secure page:** `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1`. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\n- **Headless shell only.** Playwright's default headless works.'''\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b,1)\na='''- **\"Verified\"** means the plan's author ran it on this machine on 2026-11-04, on engine commit `e7a1243` and hub client\n  1.4.0, with throwaway probes. If a verified recipe fails for you, look for what changed; don't redesign around it.'''\nb='''- **\"Verified\"** means the plan's author ran it on this machine on 2026-11-04, on engine commit `e7a1243` and hub client\n  1.4.0, with throwaway probes on software WebGPU. If a verified recipe fails for you, look for what changed; don't redesign around it. What couldn't be checked here is listed in §13.'''\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf8').write(s)\n\nd=json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json',encoding='utf8'))\nd[1]['answer']=d[1]['answer'].rstrip()+\" Also, 'done when PLAN.md covers everything TASK.md asks for' doesn't say whether pointing back at TASK.md counts as covering it. I first referred to TASK.md for things like the title procedure and the exit-interview shape, then wrote them out in the plan. And TASK.md's deliverables (the game's HTML and its exit interview) read as if they apply to whoever holds the file, while STAGE.md gives them to the builders, so it helps to say so outright.\"\nd[2]['answer']=d[2]['answer'].rstrip()+\" Testing the plan's own assumptions also corrected it: lowering the gun for a reload didn't work as a holster trick, so it became a flipbook of tilted weapon props, and sim look intents don't steer the first-person camera, so attract mode needed the camera input route.\"\nd[3]['answer']=d[3]['answer'].rstrip()+\" Finally, state in the stage instructions that a planner must not build the game or write its exit interview, and whether the plan must restate TASK.md or may refer to it.\"\njson.dump(d,open('planner-exit-interview.json','w',encoding='utf8'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nd=json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json',encoding='utf8'))\nprint(len(d),'answers;',[q['question'] for q in d])\n\n# Coverage audit: every section the table names exists; every TASK.md requirement phrase is present in the plan's own words.\nheads=set(re.findall(r'^#{2,3} (\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)',s,flags=re.M))\nrefs=set(re.findall(r'§(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)',s))\nprint('section refs with no heading:',sorted(r for r in refs if r not in heads))\nneed=['50 titles','real random number generator','Animalese','10%','single' if False else 'one HTML file','CDN','read-only','file://','127.0.0.1','pkill','killall','fuser -k','FPS','one command','one-line count','scripted playthrough','Screenshots only','subagents','Attract' if False else 'attract','10 s','Any input','Dev Mode','Reset to defaults','Controller or keyboard required','Settings** button','PlayStation','Xbox','Hover' if False else 'hover moves focus','left click','Create','Options','No TODOs','sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub','artDirection','tagline','Tech demo','Kids & Learning','How many issues did testing catch','critical issues','most helpful test','least helpful test','What did you like most a