{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjGL8h8WCWFSWUA9xX9m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` now states everything `TASK.md` asks for in its own text, and `planner-exit-interview.json` is updated and still parses. I did not build the game or write its exit interview, even though the hook flagged both as missing.\n\n**Why not build the game:** `STAGE.md` says other agents build it from this plan and pick the title themselves. The HTML's file name and the exit interview's title field both need that title, so doing either here would break the stage's instructions. The hook's own text also accepts that the plan covering `TASK.md` is the done condition.\n\n**What the feedback got right:**\n- **Added to the plan:** these were only pointed at before, and are now written out:\n    - the title procedure\n    - the shared-machine rules\n    - every Source Information field\n    - the full exit-interview JSON shape\n    - all the feedback questions\n    - the stand-ins for hardware this machine lacks\n- **New rule for builders:** a feature-coverage test, so the demo provably shows every mechanic.\n- **Coverage check:** a script found every required phrase I listed from `TASK.md` in the plan, and every section reference points to a real heading.\n\n**Items I had left unverified are now tested:**\n\n| Item | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Game's own pre-round card | Passes all four harness scenarios |\n| Parked car blocking people on foot | Stops a walker |\n| Holstered walking camera | Keeps the hands out of frame and turns with the stick |\n| Boat | New numbers; floats level, reaches 16 m/s |\n| Co-op sync through fire, jeep, NPC and movement | Identical over 3,600 steps with 2 and 4 seats plus a server copy |\n| Fire inside the engine | 109 m downwind, 17 m upwind in 30 s, matching the plan's targets |\n\n**Testing also corrected the plan in three places:**\n- **Reload animation:** the lowered-gun trick only holsters the gun. Swapping through tilted gun models does animate it in first person, so the plan now uses that.\n- **Attract mode camera:** the bot can't steer the first-person camera through `look` intents. The plan now uses the route that works, `cameraInput.view`.\n- **First-use stalls:** the first holster cycles and the first flame stall briefly, so the plan has them run behind the loading screen.\n\n**Still unverifiable here:** real GPUs, real controllers, speakers, sync across different machines, and iOS. Everything above ran on software WebGPU, and §13 of the plan tells builders to report these gaps.\n\nI made no commits and deleted my scratch files. Everything is in the `work` folder:\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `planner-exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":670,"cache_read_input_tokens":733642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":670},"output_tokens":687,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"3e8c01be-97fd-417b-ab82-9f5b229d1c7b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:56:01.134Z","request_id":"req_011CgjGL8KKShziwgwqCo1R3"}
