{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjGmqF7yAFcrazguNgGm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` now covers every sentence of `TASK.md`, this time checked line by line rather than by phrase search. The plan still leaves the game build and its exit-interview file to the builders, because `STAGE.md` assigns them that work. The plan's first bullet now says so, and §15.3 gives them the JSON shape, copied verbatim from `TASK.md`.\n\n**The audit:** I split `TASK.md` into 160 sentences and assigned each by hand to the plan text that fulfils it, or to a stated reason it needs none. A script then failed on any unassigned sentence or misquoted plan text.\n\n| Audit result | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Sentences mapped to specific plan text | 138 |\n| Needing no action (headings, machine facts such as CPU and disk) | 22 |\n| Unassigned | 0 |\n| Misquoted | 0 |\n\nThe script only proves the quotes exist, so which text counts as covering each sentence was my call. The plan describes the game; none of it has been built or played, only tested with throwaway probes.\n\n**Gaps the read-through found, now fixed in the plan:**\n- **Polish:** \"polished vertical slice\" now has a concrete checklist behind it.\n- **Pacing:** pacing now has an actual rule.\n- **Designer tools:** a required test now adds a contract, checkpoint and dealer item as data only, then plays them.\n- **Controllers:** the UI section now says \"any standard-mapping pad\", and the game draws its own button glyphs, because `input.prompt` follows the pad's brand (it says `A` on a pad reporting as Xbox).\n- **Aim assist:** a controller-first shooter had none. It's now specified, and I tested the mechanism behind it (camera input combining with the stick).\n- **iPhone touch notice:** it must be built before the engine starts, or it can't be trusted on WebKit's iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here. I tested that it shows when built this way.\n- **Node Playwright:** the plan now explains how the workspace's 1.64.1 fits with `TASK.md`'s 1.63.0 note.\n\nThe engine's `main` moved one commit during this work. That commit only changes how building walls are cut away for cameras, so nothing the plan relies on is affected, and the plan notes it.\n\n**Still unverifiable on this machine:** real GPUs, real controllers, speakers, sync across different machines, and iOS. §13 tells builders to report these gaps.\n\nI made no commits and deleted my scratch files. `planner-exit-interview.json` still parses, with all four answers.\n\nEverything is in the `work` folder:\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `planner-exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2651,"cache_read_input_tokens":800578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2651},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"18447f65-5621-4591-b234-7876af035444","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:01:52.326Z","request_id":"req_011CgjGmpppxuToZZBw7b2T4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: PLAN.md covers everything TASK.md asks for.]: STAGE.md asks for planner-exit-interview.json and the plan itself, and both exist. But the stop condition requires PLAN.md to cover everything TASK.md asks for, and the transcript shows the plan's own audit found gaps (polish, pacing, designer tools, controllers, aim assist, touch notice, Node Playwright) that were only fixed afterwards. The coverage claim rests on an audit where the assistant chose which plan text counts as covering each sentence, and the plan still defers the game build and exit-interview file to builders, so the mapping of TASK.md's deliverable requirements to PLAN.md is not confirmed by evidence."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"280274e2-c787-4891-b21f-841f0e60d1cb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:01:56.800Z","isSynthetic":true}
