{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjHnVE1PNgBR54Ab22mp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` covers every `TASK.md` requirement, and that claim now rests on checks beyond my own mapping. The game and its exit-interview file still don't exist, because `STAGE.md` gives that work to the builders and leaves the title to them. The HTML's file name needs that title, so building it here would break the stage.\n\n**New evidence, none of it depending on which plan text I chose:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Acceptance script added to the plan, reading names, JSON shape, question counts, date and model from `TASK.md` itself | Passes 122 checks on a complete mock |\n| 20 faults injected on purpose (renamed file, altered hub client, missing key, wrong genre, music not at 10%, leftover TODO, edited engine file and others) | All caught, after fixing one real hole: an external script slipped through at first |\n| Plan's commands and scripts extracted from `PLAN.md` unchanged and run in a mock builder folder | Setup and `npm run check` pass; sim 6/6; hub harness 53/53 across all four configurations |\n| Every content word in `TASK.md` searched for in the plan (569 words) | 66 absent, none a missing requirement; I still tightened three weak links |\n| Sentence audit rerun on the final text (160 sentences) | 138 mapped to quoted plan text, 22 need no action, 0 unassigned, 0 misquoted |\n\nEach row of the plan's coverage table now also has a \"Proved by\" column naming the test that will prove that requirement once the game is built. The dry-run setup also corrected the plan's order: the title must be picked first, because the dev folder is named after it.\n\n**What this doesn't prove:**\n- **Mock, not a game:** passing shows the acceptance check works, not that a real game will meet it.\n- **Browser UI tests not yet written:** dev mode, attract mode, button glyphs and hover focus are specified, but builders write that test script, so it hasn't been run.\n- **Judged by eye:** art, writing tone, pacing and polish have no script; the plan marks them \"judged\" and tells builders to report them honestly.\n- **No independent reviewer:** I took `TASK.md`'s ban on review subagents as binding, so the sentence mapping is still my own judgement.\n- **Real hardware:** GPUs, controllers, speakers, sync across machines and iOS can't be checked here.\n\n**Your call:** an independent coverage review, or building the game in this stage, would go against those instructions, so I'd only do either if you say so. Without that, I consider the stage done.\n\nI made no commits and deleted my scratch files; `planner-exit-interview.json` still parses with all four answers.\n\nEverything is in the `work` folder:\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `planner-exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":860516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1738},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c3db9ff-22de-4370-a6c8-816de35b9215","uuid":"7350345d-ed53-4781-bffb-21f5dbed94fd","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:15:15.739Z","request_id":"req_011CgjHnUuATGH6pGvVSMDoj"}
