{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjJ79Xcr9LaGppjynD9T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012bqEZQg8Ute9q2Q7e5NxGS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p .research && cat > .research/appendix.py <<'EOF'\nimport re,sys\nT=open('TASK.md',encoding='utf8').read().split('\\n')\ns=open('PLAN.md',encoding='utf8').read()\nHEAD='## Appendix A: TASK.md, sentence by sentence'\nif HEAD in s: s=s[:s.index(HEAD)].rstrip()+'\\n'\nP=s.split('\\n')\ndef norm(t):\n    t=t.replace('’',\"'\").replace('‘',\"'\").replace('“','\"').replace('”','\"').replace('**','').replace('`','')\n    return re.sub(r'\\s+',' ',t).strip()\nstarts=[];buf=''\nfor l in P: starts.append(len(buf)); buf+=norm(l)+' '\nsecs=[(i,re.match(r'#{2,3} (\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)',l).group(1)) for i,l in enumerate(P,1) if re.match(r'#{2,3} \\d',l)]\ndef loc(f):\n    at=buf.find(norm(f))\n    if at<0: return None\n    line=sum(1 for x in starts if x<=at)\n    sec=[n for i,n in secs if i<=line]\n    return (f'§{sec[-1]}' if sec else 'top',line)\nA=[]\ndef a(t,*p,why=None): A.append((norm(t),list(p),why))\nfor h in ['Working Environment and deliverable:','## This computer',\"### What this computer doesn't have\",'### Sharing this computer','## Goal','Scope','## UI & UX','## Done','## Source Information','Testing Feedback','Engine Feedback','Prompt Feedback']: a(h,why='heading')\na('SOURCE: Far Cry 2','Inspired by Far Cry 2.')\na('Genre: Pick','Genre: open-world first-person shooter with systemic fire and survival pressure.')\na('Perspective: Pick','Perspective: first person, with an over-the-shoulder option in Settings')\na(\"Game Title: A playful\",'A playful riff on the source\\'s name.')\na('Silently brainstorm 50','Silently brainstorm 50 titles (don\\'t show the list), then pick one with a real random number generator by running code')\na('Research: Whether','Research. How much is your choice.')\na('Package: For ease','bundle into one HTML file in the folder above it, named as your TASK.md says.')\na('Dependencies that can','External CDN dependencies are allowed, but this plan\\'s recipe inlines everything')\na('Tech Stack: Build on','my-3dge in its full workspace.')\na('The engine stays read-only','The engine stays read-only; add whatever systems, art and animation the game needs on top.')\na('The rest of the tech','The rest of the stack is your choice')\na('Art Direction: Use','The engine\\'s native style and animation system as the base')\na('Make new art assets','Props to make:')\na('Animation: Use','Animation: the engine\\'s system plus new work')\na('Make new animations','Author with defineAction')\na('Audio: All music','All music, effects and voices are written in code with no audio files')\na('Voices are Animalese','voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish')\na('Music is to be set','Music at 10% by default: right after createAudio(), audio.volume(\\'music\\', 0.1).')\na('Online: https','Follow the [AI Hub session protocol]')\na('Create a subfolder','Name the dev folder from that title by the pattern in your TASK.md')\na('You can develop separate','Develop in separate modules in the dev folder, then bundle into one HTML file')\na('You may use external CDN','External CDN dependencies are allowed')\na('Do not read files outside','Don\\'t read files outside what you need')\na('They share this machine','share this machine\\'s ports and processes')\na('Prefer file://','Prefer file:// and the engine\\'s headless tools.')\na('If you need a server','bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result.')\na('Stop only processes','Stop only processes you started, by PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or killing whatever holds a port.')\na('Performance: Treat','Treat the budget as unlimited')\na('Add as much detail','add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights and shadows as the scene needs.')\na('Out of scope (handled','FPS targets and optimization are out of scope.')\na('Testing: Test as much','Headless scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game')\na('Keep them behind one','behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, rerun only after changing the code it covers.')\na('Use screenshots only','Screenshots only for what a script can\\'t check.')\na(\"Don't use subagents\",'No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit')\na('Effort: Spend','Effort. Spend it however you see fit.')\na('Checked 2026-11-04','as checked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs')\na('- Computer:','Worki9, 13th Gen Intel i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap')\na('Ubuntu 26.04.1','Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).')\na('- Space:','850 GB free in the home folder; /tmp is 9.8 GB in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.')\na('- Display:','No display in runs (DISPLAY unset).','so skip headed mode and xvfb.')\na('- Browsers:','Use --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader.')\na('Phone and tablet device','phone and tablet profiles built in.')\na('WebGPU only works','WebGPU needs a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1.')\na('A WebGPU canvas','A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game\\'s state instead.')\na('For Node, npm install','you don\\'t need npm install playwright@1.63.0.')\na('Playwright runs here','Leave PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE as it is set.')\na('- Tools:','Tools: node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1')\na('- Rust:',\"Rust: rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1 and stable\")\na('- Not installed:','Not installed: sox, bun, deno.')\na('- Network:','Internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).')\na('- Memory:','means memory ran out (earlyoom), not a bug in your game')\na('Run fewer browsers','run fewer browsers rather than retrying.')\na('No script can check','Stand-ins for what this computer lacks (never required for real)')\na('Test with the stand-ins','Stand-ins for what this computer lacks (never required for real)')\na('- No physical','no controller, so replace navigator.getGamepads')\na('Emulate one:','replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub returning a standard-mapping pad via add_init_script/addInitScript')\na('- No touch','no touch device, so use Playwright\\'s phone and tablet profiles')\na(\"Use Playwright's phone\",'use Playwright\\'s phone and tablet profiles and tap with page.touchscreen')\na('- Nobody to listen','nobody to listen, so check sound by what Web Audio produces')\na('Check sound by what','through an OfflineAudioContext or AnalyserNode levels')\na('- No second','no second player, so play multiplayer with two pages or contexts')\na('Play multiplayer with','play multiplayer with two pages or contexts')\na('- No real iPhone','no real iPhone or iPad, so use WebKit with an iPhone profile')\na('WebKit with an iPhone','the closest there is, though it isn\\'t iOS Safari')\na('- No TV.','no TV, so judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080')\na('Judge the 10-foot','judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080')\na('- Other agents run','other agents work in the folders beside yours')\na('Keep one or two','Keep one or two browsers open at once and close them.')\na('- Keep every file','Keep every file inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder')\na('- The browsers are','Never run playwright install or playwright install-deps.')\na('- The system Python','The system Python has Playwright and nothing else')\na('For one (Pillow','uv run --with pillow python script.py, adding --with playwright==1.63.0 when the script drives a browser.')\na('Build an original','An original game inspired by Far Cry 2')\na('Create a feature-complete','a feature-complete demo and a complete, polished vertical slice')\na('Capture what makes','turns the source\\'s world, characters, themes and tone into mechanics, pacing and UX.')\na('The demo must be','It must be long enough to show all features and mechanics, so a player clearly understands how it plays and feels and what they can and cannot do')\na('Treat the demo','Polish: what \"complete and polished\" means here')\na('It should contain','Adding a contract or a checkpoint takes no new code, and a test proves it')\na('Include a dev mode','Dev mode: Pause → Dev Mode')\na('Balance is key','Balance: live sliders on scenes/settings.ts, each with its value and a per-row and global Reset to defaults')\na('Attract Mode: After','After 10 s without input on the title or any menu off the title','Any input exits at once to the title')\na('The AI (or replay)','it may cheat freely: infinite health, ammo and abilities, no clip.')\na('Its only job','Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible; it plays no part in balance.')\na('Multiplayer: Follow','Decision: shared-world, host-sequenced deterministic lockstep.','Outside the hub, Title → Co-op runs the same Contract Run with no server')\na('Narrative tone','A writing style similar to the source\\'s, in entirely original words.')\na('Design the game around','Design for a PS5 DualSense, or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping, played on a TV at 10 feet.')\na(\"With keyboard and mouse\",'Keyboard and mouse get the same game on the same screens, and must feel native rather than like stand-ins for controller buttons')\na('The keyboard uses','keys are the ones PC players expect')\na('The mouse aims','in menus hover moves focus and click picks','with no weapon out a left click uses it')\na('On-screen prompts','PlayStation glyphs for any pad, or Xbox if Settings says so; keyboard → key caps and mouse icons with the actual binding')\na('Do not use overly','no dense, web-style data screens and no tables of data')\na('Touch-only devices:','no touch controls','Show a full-screen message exactly \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button')\na('Let the attract','over the attract mode, which keeps running')\na('No TODOs, placeholders','No TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features.')\na('The demo is complete','The demo is complete.')\na('CRITICAL: Put','put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your final chat reply and on the About/Credits screen')\na('Write \"unknown\"','writing \"unknown\" for anything you can\\'t confirm')\nfor t,p in [('- Date:','| Date | The date and time your TASK.md gives |'),('- Source: the work','| Source | Far Cry 2 |'),('- Plan: the file','| Plan | The file name of the plan you were given: PLAN.md |'),('- Genre and Perspective','| Genre and Perspective |'),('- Tech: stack','| Tech | my-3dge at the commit engine-lock.json names'),('- Art Direction: style','| Art Direction | The engine\\'s native low-poly style'),('- Animation: system','| Animation | The engine\\'s animation system'),('- Audio: music','| Audio | All in code'),('- Online: network','| Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1'),('- Testing: testing','| Testing | The testing parameters allowed'),('- Research: research','| Research | Engine and hub source reading'),('- Environment:','| Environment, Model | Exactly as your TASK.md gives them |'),('- Model:','| Environment, Model | Exactly as your TASK.md gives them |'),('- Usage: write','| Usage | Write \"added on import\".')]: a(t,p)\na(\"You can't see your own\",\"You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it\")\na('Exit interview: before','The exit-interview file, in exactly this shape')\na('Tools read it','Tools read it.')\nfor l in T[109:127]:\n    x=l.strip()\n    if x in ('{','}','},'): a(x,why='punct')\n    elif x: a(x,x)\na(\"The catalogue's model\",'The catalogue\\'s model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run\\'s record')\nfor q in ['How many issues did testing catch?','How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?','What was the most helpful test you ran?','What was the least helpful test you ran?','What did you like most about the engine?','Did you get stuck or guess wrong?','What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?','What was the hardest part about using the engine?','What did you change in the engine, and why?','If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?','What did you like most about this prompt?','What was confusing?','What was the hardest thing to do?','What would you change in this prompt?']: a('- '+q,q)\na('(none if nothing)','What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)')\nunits=[]\nfor n,l in enumerate(T,1):\n    l=norm(l)\n    if not l: continue\n    if 110<=n<=127: units.append((n,l)); continue\n    for u in re.split(r'(?<=[.?!])\\s+(?=[A-Z\"\\[(])',l): units.append((n,u.strip()))\ndef scrub(u,n):\n    u=re.sub(r'\\[GameTitle-SOURCE-[^\\]]+\\]','[the name your TASK.md gives]',u).replace('exit-interview.json','the exit-interview file')\n    if n==105: u='- Environment: as your TASK.md gives it'\n    if n==106: u='- Model: as your TASK.md gives it'\n    if n==94: u='- Date: as your TASK.md gives it'\n    return u\nrows=[];missing=[];bad=[];skipped=0\nfor n,u in units:\n    hit=None\n    for t,p,why in A:\n        if u.startswith(t) or (t in u and len(t)>12): hit=(t,p,why);break\n    if hit is None: missing.append((n,u));continue\n    t,p,why=hit\n    if not p: skipped+=1;continue\n    cells=[]\n    for f in p:\n        w=loc(f)\n        if w is None: bad.append((n,f));continue\n        q=norm(f)\n        cells.append(f'{w[0]} (line {w[1]}): {q if len(q)<=96 else q[:93]+\"…\"}')\n    v=scrub(u,n); v=v if len(v)<=96 else v[:93]+'…'\n    rows.append('| %d | %s | %s |'%(n,v.replace('|','\\\\|'),' / '.join(cells).replace('|','\\\\|')))\nprint('sentences',len(units),'rows',len(rows),'headings or JSON punctuation',skipped,'UNASSIGNED',missing,'MISQUOTED',bad)\nif missing or bad: sys.exit(1)\nintro=f'''{HEAD}\n\nFor whoever wants to check this plan against the brief without taking anyone's word for it; builders can skip it. Every sentence of TASK.md is listed by its line number, beside the words in this plan that answer it and where they are. A script built this table from the two files and refused any sentence left unassigned and any wording not found in the plan; which words answer which sentence was the plan author's call, so read them against each other. Long sentences are cut with an ellipsis, and names each builder's TASK.md sets for itself are left out. Only headings and JSON punctuation ({skipped} lines) have no row.\n\n| Line | TASK.md | This plan |\n|---|---|---|\n'''\ns=s.rstrip()+'\\n\\n'+intro+'\\n'.join(rows)+'\\n'\nopen('PLAN.md','w',encoding='utf8').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -I .research/appendix.py; echo \"exit $?\"; rm -rf .research; python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport re,json\ns=open('PLAN.md',encoding='utf8').read()\nf=chr(96)*3\nprint('code blocks:',len([b for b in s.split(f) if re.match(r'(js|ts|json|sh|html)\\n',b)]))\nprint('names left out still out:',re.findall(r'GameTitle-SOURCE-claude|claude-opus-5-5|exit-interview\\.json|Anthropic',s))\nprint('section refs with no heading:',sorted(r for r in set(re.findall(r'§(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)',s)) if r not in set(re.findall(r'^#{2,3} (\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)',s,flags=re.M))))\na=s[s.index('## Appendix A'):].split('\\n')\nprint('appendix rows:',len([l for l in a if re.match(r'\\| \\d',l)]));print('\\n'.join(l[:190] for l in a if l.startswith(('| 24 ','| 76 ','| 87 ')))[:900])\nEOF\nls -A; wc -l -c PLAN.md","description":"Write the sentence-by-sentence coverage table into the plan and verify it","timeout":30000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":905525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":618},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"pare